Cambodia, Bangladesh to Continue Strengthening Employment and Vocational Training Agreement
Cambodia and Bangladesh have pledged to further strengthen employment and vocational training agreements as the Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) between the two countries expires.
This statement was made on the occasion of Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, and Mr. Mohammed Abdul Hy, Ambassador of the People's Republic of Bangladesh to Cambodia, paid a courtesy call on the morning of 31 May. 2022, Office of the Ministry of Labor.
Mr. Ith Sam Heng stated that for the field of employment and vocational training Cambodia-Bangladesh has a Memorandum of Understanding since 2017, the technical team has worked in accordance with the agreement because Kovid-19 interrupted. Two years later, today both sides have the opportunity to discuss to continue this cooperation with each other.
The Ambassador requested the Cambodian Technical Working Group on Labor and Vocational Training to travel to Dhaka for the second meeting with the Bangladesh Technical Working Group on the renewal of the MoU, and invited Minister Ith Sam Heng to visit the working group. Cambodia itself in Bangladesh.
At the same time, the Minister sees that the two countries' labor sectors are similar in terms of production and export, especially in the textile and garment sector.
