(Kep): Dr. Ing Phirun, Secretary of State, Representative of Prof. Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health and Dr. Som Piseth, Governor of Kep Province, presided over the celebration of World No Tobacco Day 2022 on May 31, 2022. At Kep Provincial Hall.
On that occasion, Dr. Ing Phirun said that worldwide, 600 million trees are cut down every year to produce cigarettes, and about one tree produces about 15 packs of cigarettes. Factories pollute the air and cause respiratory diseases.
Of that, 4.5 trillion cigarette butts are thrown away, which pollutes soil and water, such as fish, which contain toxic chemicals that can cause illness to people who eat them and other eating disorders, he said. Water contains tobacco. A cigarette can contain up to 14 grams of carbon dioxide and use about 3.7 liters of water to produce it. Throughout the life cycle of cigarettes (from growth to disposal), tobacco emits more than 80 million tons of carbon dioxide each year.
He also called on the general public who are using tobacco products to give up the habit of using tobacco products and those who have not yet started using tobacco products to avoid using tobacco products for the health and salvation of our planet. He called on all relevant institutions to develop and promote the effective implementation of the law on tobacco control for sustainable development.
