889 families in Taing Kork district received a total of 2,312 hectares of land and expressed their gratitude to Samdech Techo Hun Sen
(Kampong Thom): A total of 889 families in Kork Trabek village, Sralao commune, Taing Kork district, Kampong Thom province received land occupancy and enjoyment of 2,312 hectares, which has been living and enjoying for many years. 1,085 plots of land. This is according to the letter of the Office of the Council of Ministers No. 393, dated May 31, 2022.
Kork Trabek Village is a remote village located in three areas around the Tonle Sap Lake near the border of Kampong Thom and Kampong Chhnang Provinces, near the Tonle Sap Lake.
On May 31, 2022, Mr. Thong Khon, Chairman of the Royal Government Working Group visited Kampong Thom Province and Mr. Nguon Rattanak, Governor of Kampong Thom Province, led the officials to disseminate the speech of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and the Royal Sub-Decree. Government No. 105 on the redevelopment of 6,385 hectares from three areas to two areas of the Tonle Sap Lake area in Kampong Thom province and handed over to the people for possession and enjoyment.
President Thong Khon recalled Samdech Techo PM's remarks on land clearing for people in the area around the Tonle Sap Lake. The handing over to the people is not the flooded forest land, because Samdech Techo has clearly stated that it is necessary to jointly protect the flooded forest, especially after handing it over to the people, and the people cannot cut down the flooded forest. No more.
Mr. Pol Chhin, Sralao Commune Chief, as well as the Village Chief and the people of Kork Trabek Village, expressed their great joy when they learned that Samdech Techo Prime Minister decided to hand over to them to cultivate rice fields and thanked Samdech Techo. Many think of them as citizens with real needs.
Mr. Thong Khon insisted to the people in Kork Trabek village that when receiving the land and enjoying it from the head of the Royal Government, please do not sell it to any other trader or investor.
The Chairman of Kampong Thom Provincial Field Team also stated that the handing over of land to the people by Samdech Techo Prime Minister reflects the wise leadership of Samdech Techo who has virtue, common sense and high consideration for the people's livelihood. "Especially to protect the area around the Tonle Sap Lake and protect the interests of the people."
Provincial Governor Nguon Rattanak also said that the land allocation for the three areas should not be beyond the set boundaries, so the people, commune chiefs, district administrations, provincial administrations and relevant departments and offices must have Clarity together to serve the interests of the people and implement the sub-decree of the Royal Government as well as the words of Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
President Thong Khon and the Governor of Kampong Thom Province also called on the people to participate in the conservation of resources in the Tonle Sap Lake area, especially the flooded forest in the area around the Tonle Sap Lake and fish species must not encroach on the flooded forest and forest. Illegal fishing.
In addition, Mr. Thong Khon and the provincial administration will also cooperate in building and repairing roads for people in Kork Trabek village.
According to Mr. Hak Mong Huot, the current governor of Taing Kork district, the village has a population of more than 300 families, most of them since after the liberation on January 7 due to the need for daily living. Apart from fishing, the people in Kork Bek village also try to grow rice. Kratie CPP President Visits People at Home and Reminds That CPP Does Not Promise the Wind Like Other Political Parties
