(Oddar Meanchey): Candidate for commune chief of the Candlelight Party in Trapeang Prasat commune, Trapeang Prasat district, Oddar Meanchey province, released a video apologizing publicly after admitting his mistake by giving false information to Radio Free Asia that he was not Known and kicked a motorcycle from behind while participating in the election campaign, injuring one leg in Tuol Krous village, Thlat commune, Anlong Veng district on May 24, 2022.
But in fact, after being interrogated by the Oddar Meanchey provincial police for more than three hours, she confessed that she was not kicked in the back by an unidentified person, just riding a motorcycle. Only a little. The reason for giving false information to Radio Free Asia is for political gain and to get the support of the people.
Please note that Radio Free Asia reports that a woman named Sorn Chanthorn, a candidate for the commune chief of the Candlelight Party in Trapeang Prasat commune, claimed that two unknown people rode a motorbike and hit her motorbike after participating in the election campaign, causing leg injuries. One side is in Tuol Krous village, Thlat commune, Anlong Veng district, Oddar Meanchey province on May 24, 2022.
According to RFA, the woman described the incident as political persecution to prevent her from engaging in political life with the Candlelight Party. Despite such an accident, he did not complain to the police to arrest and punish the perpetrators because he did not trust the authorities.
Immediately after receiving the information, Oddar Meanchey Provincial Police Commissioner Major General Huot Sothy sent a specialized force to investigate and summoned Sorn Chanthorn for questioning at the Trapeang Prasat Administrative Police Station on 28 May.
The woman gave the answer and claimed it was an accident (separation) and she also gave the same answer to RFA and the answer to the authorities. On May 29, 2022, the provincial police force, in cooperation with the Trapeang Prasat District Police Inspectorate, summoned Sorn Chanthorn for questioning and re-interview at District Police Inspectorate.
After a three-hour, 30-minute interrogation, the woman realized her guilt because she wanted to gain political advantage and get more votes, so she gave the wrong answer to RFA. Disgrace the honor of the nation. He apologized to the leadership of the Special Forces at all levels in writing and videotaped the speech.
