Reuters reports that the proposed sanctions on Russia's oil imports are part of the EU's sixth package of sanctions against Russia over its aggression against Ukraine.
The sanctions package includes the severance of Russia's largest bank, Sberbank, from the SWIFT remittance system, the banning of Russian media companies from the European Union, and the addition of more people to the list of individuals whose assets have been frozen. And that can not enter the EU.
The whole package has been opposed by Hungary, which says the embargo on the oil trade will hurt its economy because it cannot easily access other types of oil. Slovakia and the Czech Republic have expressed similar concerns.
Discussions on the Russian oil trade ban have been going on for a month without progress, and European leaders are willing to reach an agreement for their summit to avoid There seems to be inconsistency in its response to Moscow. According to Reuters.
