Mr. Buon Heng reported on the preparation of instructions on the procedures and procedures for providing administrative services through the OWSO mechanism as follows:
* By studying and collecting documents at the 5 commune administrations, the working group can assess the overall situation of providing administrative services at the commune level:
* First: Types of administrative services: Commune / Sangkat administration is providing two major types of administrative services, including: civil registration (10 services) and issuance of certificates (13 services) as defined in Inter-Ministerial Prakas No. 14342 dated 29 December 2016 of the Ministry of Interior and the Ministry of Economy and Finance on the Provision of Administrative Services at the Sub-National Administration
* Third: Based on the results of this study, the working group of the General Department of Administration has prepared a draft instruction on the procedures and procedures for providing administrative services through the OWSO mechanism of the commune / sangkat administration, focusing on On site preparation, staffing, procedures for providing administrative services and sample forms, attachments for providing services through the OWSO mechanism of Commune / Sangkat Administration
* Fifth: After receiving comments from all stakeholders, the working group of the General Department of Administration last edited and requested the high signature of Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior on 13 May. 2022
* Sixth: Instructions on the procedures and procedures for providing administrative services through the OWSO mechanism of the commune / sangkat administration, divided into 5 points, including: 1. The organization of the OWSO mechanism. And staffing. 3. Procedures for providing services. 4. Application forms for administrative services. 5. Support, dissemination and monitoring and evaluation, and 6. Mediation to resolve complaints.
For the details of this instruction, the representative of the Department of Functions and Resources will present the whole ceremony shortly.
Mr. Prak Sam Oeun stated that after the presentation and clarification on the questions related to the content of Instruction No. 018, he would like to send instructions and instructions on some of the work that the Capital and Provincial Administration must continue to do when returning: :
* First, to copy the instruction No. 018 Sann dated 13 May 2022 on the procedures and procedures for providing administrative services through the one-stop-shop mechanism of the commune / sangkat administration to all commune / sangkat administrations and stakeholders. In its jurisdiction.
* Second: The Deputy Governor of the Capital and Provinces who participated in the outreach meeting must report the results of this meeting to the Capital and Provincial Governors and organize a working group to disseminate this instruction to the Commune / Sangkat Administration in the Capital and Provinces. Body. Dissemination to all Commune / Sangkat Administration shall be made after the announcement of the validity and inauguration of the Commune / Sangkat Council of the fifth mandate.
* Third, the Capital and Provincial Administration shall set a specific date for the launch of the OWSO for the provision of administrative services in all its commune / sangkat administrations. This setting should be arranged quickly, without delay.
* Fifth: Capital and provincial administrations must regularly monitor, inspect and evaluate the provision of administrative services through the one-stop-shop mechanism of the commune / sangkat administration, including location, staffing, service delivery procedures, and Use of forms.
Five Gangsters Arrested by Poipet Armed Forces After Assassinating a Young Man
(Banteay Meanchey): Five gangsters under the age of 18 were arrested by Poipet City Gendarmerie after they attacked a young man, causing multiple injuries.
The massacre took place on the night of May 26, 2022 at the Caltex gas station in Palilei 2 village, Poipet commune, Poipet city, Banteay Meanchey province, and the five perpetrators were arrested by the military on the morning of May 27, 2022. May 2022.
The victim, Ouk Veasna, male, 18 years old, living in Kbal Koh Village, Sangkat Poipet, Poipet City, Banteay Meanchey Province, suffered multiple injuries on his body, including: broken left wrist, left toe, left head and calf. Both hands.
He said that for some reason, the suspects used violence against the victims, mistaken people, thinking that the victims were a group that had used violence against them in the past.
According to the Poipet City Gendarmerie Commander, after the arrest, his Gendarmerie confiscated one recycled knife and three Honda Dream motorcycles. After the interrogation, the Poipet City Armed Forces prepared a case to be sent to court for legal action.
