Lem Phorvarith, Development Officer of the Cambodian Aquaculture Association, told Fresh News on May 30 that after the situation in Kovid improved, the fish market in Cambodia improved last year, but the price did not seem to increase. During the outbreak of Kovid 19.
He said the 30% increase in demand was sufficient to supply farmers and prevent them from facing the same fish stocks in the ponds as last year, as in the past most ponds owners had reduced their production.
He said that although the fish market in Cambodia has improved, some fish farmers do not seem to have decided to increase the number of fish in the pond, waiting to survey the market, while the feed and shipping costs are high. The fish remain the same, making them less profitable. However, he expects fish prices to rise again by the end of the year due to the full economic opening and various events.
Mr. Lok Loeun, the owner of a farm in Kampong Cham province, which can produce 800 to 1,000 tons of fish a year, believes that the change in the fish market is better because the Royal Government prevents fishing crimes in the Tonle Sap Lake and imports from neighboring countries. Reduced because the price of fish in Vietnam and Thailand is more expensive than Cambodia, which makes the fish market is not as narrow as two years ago.
According to the owner of this fish farm, this year the price of catfish has increased by about 1,000 riel per kilogram, but some other species such as catfish, trout, trout and trout have decreased due to the type of fish. These are available from natural lakes and rivers, and most are imported from Vietnam as such fish.
