President of the Cambodian Association of Travel Agents Encourages Tourism Professionals to Return to Work (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Ms. Chhay Sivlin, President of the Association of Cambodian Travel Agents, encouraged and requested tourism professionals to return to work. In the tourism sector, while Cambodia has returned to a better state, combined with the influx of tourists from Thailand and Vietnam.
Speaking to Fresh News on May 30, 2022, Ms. Chhay Sivlin said that international tourists are gradually returning to Cambodia after Cambodia reopened the country and opened the southern corridor with the country. Vietnam and Thailand, together with the exemption of documents and the exclusion of tourists.
Ms. Chhay Sivlin said, "Currently, Vietnamese tourists who come to Cambodia are ahead of Chinese tourists, and the second leading tourist is Thai tourists." "Factors that lead Vietnamese and Thai tourists to come to Cambodia because Vietnam-Thailand has just opened to traffic combined with the convenience of traveling to Cambodia via land."
She added that these factors are why travel agencies are looking for ways to provide quality services, combining tourism products, destinations and resorts to make new services rich and affordable.
