The old lady brought a cow and a krama from Cambodia to the United States as a reward for her grandchildren on the day of graduation from the US Military Academy
(Phnom Penh): An elderly woman brought a cow and a krama from Cambodia to the United States as a reward for her grandson on the day of graduation from the US Military Academy. This cowhide and krama is a legacy of Pich Moon, who used it regularly when he was a child on a rural land in Kampong Chhnang province.
Pich Moon graduated with great pride from the US Military Academy after four years of hard work. The graduation ceremony was held on May 27, 2022 under the presidency of US President Joe Biden.
The achievement of graduating from a military school on American soil, which is rare for young Cambodians, is something that has already led to many surprises and surprises for young Pich Moon. But the writings and pictures depicting the grandmother's bringing of cows and scarves from Cambodia to the United States to young Pich Moon led to even more astonishment.
This post and image has led to a lot of sharing on Facebook. Pich Moon described that the krama and the cow rope, which are the memories of his childhood, have been kept by his grandmother for 10 years.
Young Pich Moon mentioned his grandmother's confirmation that the cow and krama were kept by her grandmother and looked at when she missed her grandson. When handing over the cow rope and krama on graduation day, the grandmother told her grandson not to forget his birth as a cowboy.
Pich Moon described that he almost shed tears when he heard the words of the rich man who nurtured and cared for him from birth to adulthood. Pich Moon considers this cow necklace and scarf as the most precious gift in his life.
Please note that Pich Moon is a farmer living in Krous village, Rolea Bier commune, Rolea Bier district, Kampong Chhnang province. He received a scholarship to study at the American Military Academy for four years and just graduated in 2022.
Pich Moon majored in math and aerospace research and also gained pilot skills. Pich Moon states that studying in the United States is one of his dreams that came from reading a book while herding cattle, having read about the life of an American commander on a mission during World War II in the Asia-Pacific region. . The U.S. military commander graduated from the U.S. Military Academy.
It is the story of this US military commander that inspires young Diamond Moon to nurture his ambitions and deep endeavors to enter the US Military Academy.
Prior to receiving a scholarship to the US Military Academy, Pich Moon also holds a Bachelor of Medicine and a Bachelor of International Relations degree from Cambodia. Pich Moon is a young man who has struggled hard to study. Because of the poor family life, when they came to study in Phnom Penh, they used to live on the porch of their house and pick food from the trash can.
Pich Moon had another heart attack while working as a waitress at a restaurant when he was hit on the head by a high-ranking military officer for refusing a glass of wine from the officer. Remembering this story, the young Pich Moon insisted on the high-ranking people to give value to the poor people, the smaller people in the same humanity.
The home of Pich Moon in his hometown of Krous village, Rolea Bier commune, Rolea Bier district, Kampong Chhnang province.
