(Phnom Penh): As the living standard of Cambodians is gradually improving day by day, the demand for food products has also changed in terms of hygiene and health.
Around the future of the supermarket sector, an experienced local businessman sees that the market or super market in Cambodia will grow in the next 3 to 5 years because Cambodia's economy continues to grow and people's livelihoods become more prosperous.
The tycoon claimed that the increase was due to the fact that the Cambodian market is now a developing market, with the Cambodian economy reopening and people moving around, and when there is prosperity, the first expense is food. .
He said that today's customers have a demand for convenience, which refers to buying food close to them without having to spend a lot of time to go shopping far away, especially the rich options.
Oknha Chandara stated that compared to the neighboring countries, the market in Cambodia is still small at present. Therefore, supermarkets that are small enough or called Mart (Mart) will grow more and more in Cambodia to meet the needs and convenience of customers as this type of market is expanding more and more in Phnom Penh and in the city. Some large provinces.
The presence of small retail supermarkets not only provides income to the economy through the payment of taxes, but all goods sold have quality standards recognized by the Ministry of Health, especially food to ensure that consumers will not harm health.
These factors have changed the habits of some Cambodians to switch from shopping in traditional markets to shopping in small supermarkets or malls like this, as it offers more convenience in shopping and saves time. Therefore, investing in this type of supermarket has become an attraction for both local and foreign investors.
