(Kampong Cham): More than 20 12th grade students of Samdech Techo Hun Sen High School in Boeung Kok participated in a classroom forum on the history of Democratic Kampuchea (1975-1979) organized by the Research Office and the Khmer Rouge Library in Kampong Cham province. Regional Teacher of Kampong Cham Province.
The students who attended this class forum, Rom Amy, Grade 11-B, Social Science, Techo Hun Sen High School, Boeung Kok, expressed that when the teacher gave a presentation on the history of the Khmer Rouge, she remembered her grandmother, Yeng. Srun, about 70 years old, survived the Khmer Rouge regime. During the Khmer Rouge regime, her grandmother lived in Trean village, Trean commune, Kampong Siem district, Kampong Cham province.
Rom Amy said her grandmother was forced to work without rest and without enough food. He lived on a farm and a dam site. Amy's grandmother always told her about the hardships at the time. Amy also sympathizes with the Cambodian people who lived under the Khmer Rouge regime and do not want the regime to return. The tragic story of the victims and survivors of the Khmer Rouge is in her memory.
