According to the Minister of Public Works, Cambodia currently has three power stations, one at the Ministry of Public Works and Transport in Sihanoukville and one at Caltex gas stations, and the ministry is preparing to add more in Battambang and Siem Reap.
The ministry has set up an electric vehicle charging station in the ministry that can accommodate six vehicles at a time. The installation will be completed in June. In addition, PTT gas station on the Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville Expressway is ready to put two. Total Gas Station is also preparing its location to operate the power plant.
The senior minister stated that when there is more use of this type of car, it will encourage more investment in charging stations. In the future, Cambodia will have electric vehicle charging stations in all provinces throughout.
