According to preliminary studies, the use of electric vehicles will reduce costs significantly compared to vehicles using internal combustion engines. The Senior Minister claimed that the users of electric vehicles in Cambodia will receive a 50% reduction in import tax, a special tax reduction from 30% to 10%. The cost of repairing this type of car is also lower due to less spare parts and less than three times less electricity consumption than fuel consumption.
For vehicle charging stations, which are designed under the cooperation between the Ministry and UNDP, will cost only 1,300 riels per kilowatt.
At the same time, the Ministry of Public Works and Transport is studying the reduction of public service fees for electric vehicles to encourage and attract more electric vehicle users. The Ministry will also work with the General Department of Taxation of the Ministry of Economy and Finance to study the annual transportation tax deduction for electric vehicles.
The Minister of Public Works believes that in the future, more companies will invest in the installation and import of electric vehicles, leading to lower electric vehicle prices. Currently in Cambodia, electric cars on the market are priced from more than 10,000 US dollars. Electric motorcycles available in the Cambodian market start at $ 700.
