"Guns" become the leading cause of death among children in the United States
WASHINGTON (Reuters) - Gunfire has become the leading cause of death among children in the United States as gun violence rises, official data show. This was released by the AFP news agency on Friday, May 27, 2022.
The CDC data shows that a total of 4,368 children and adolescents under the age of 19 died from gunshot wounds in 2020, the latest record year. In those cases, two-thirds were caused by murder. Thirty percent were suicides, while 3 percent were unintentional and 2 percent were indefinable.
According to the North Korean state news agency KCNA, authorities are stepping up testing and disinfection across the country after reports of a contagious situation this week stabilized, along with signs that the wave of fever symptoms had eased. The death toll is low. The North Korean Anti-Virus Office has collected samples from several sources to determine which areas are infected.
The KCNA added, "Emergency epidemics at all levels are prioritizing the disinfection of tens of thousands of cubic meters of rivers, lakes and wastewater and thousands of tons of garbage daily, as well as sample analysis. "Collected from those places." However, the mode of testing is not specified.
As of Thursday evening, North Korea had reported an additional 100,460 people with symptoms of fever, a significant drop from the previous 10 days. The total number of cases of fever nationwide since the outbreak in April was 3,270,850 and 69 deaths.
The Cambodian Higher Education Association submitted four proposals to the Cambodian Institute of Accounting and Auditing.
(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian Higher Education Association has submitted four proposals to the Cambodian Institute of Accounting and Auditing (Kicpaa) after the Cambodian Institute of Accounting and Auditing held a forum with higher education institutions at the Phnom Penh Hotel on the morning of May 25, 2022. Past.
The four proposals that higher education institutions have submitted to the Institute of Accounting and Auditing of Cambodia are:
1: Request the Cambodian Institute of Accounting and Auditing to open its own school to train students to meet their desired needs. Higher education institutions are not institutions that produce students to meet the needs of the Cambodian Institute of Accounting and Auditing.
2. Request the Institute of Accounting and Auditing of Cambodia to call on its members, which are independent audit firms, to increase the salaries of their employees in accordance with their income.
3: Request the Institute of Accounting and Auditing of Cambodia to appeal to its members, which are independent audit firms, to recruit first-time students for a minimum of $ 1,000 so that these independent audit firms have access to outstanding students to apply. .
4: Request the Institute of Accounting and Auditing of Cambodia to open its doors to the Association of Higher Education Institutions, whose vision on this specialization is to contribute to the Council of the Institute of Accounting and Auditing of Cambodia.
The Cambodian Higher Education Association has also confirmed that it will convene a meeting to decide on the proposal immediately.
