In a special message on the Tonle Sap Lake issue, Samdech Techo Hun Sen said, "We strongly oppose the use of the power of the powerful and the use of the money of the rich to take refuge under the banner." "People and occupy the flooded land for their own benefit."
Contrary to this opposition, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also mentioned his support, encouragement and support to the people who have the right business who have been cultivating this land for a long time. Samdech claimed that the land that people have been cultivating for a long time, the Royal Government has given to people to cultivate more.
But cases where recent logging violations are not allowed are the subject of tree replanting. This is the emphasis of Samdech Techo Prime Minister.
In addition, Samdech Techo Hun Sen appealed to all people when receiving land at the farm and please do not continue to clear the land to expand the land and do not go outside. As a trader or a powerful person, to conspire with the people in that area and clear hundreds of thousands of hectares of land and lease it to the people, as in the past, the Royal Government needs to act on this issue.
Please be reminded that Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on November 28, 2021, issued a strict order to the relevant ministries and institutions and the governor of Tonle Sap Lake to prevent and crack down on illegal logging. Flooding and land grabbing along the Tonle Sap Lake, especially in Kampong Chhnang province.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen's order came after the Royal Academy of Cambodia, led by Dr. Sok Touch, conducted a study on the Tonle Sap Lake, which found serious problems with logging and encroachment on flooded forest land, especially in Kampong Chhnang province. And needs to be addressed immediately.
At the same time, Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara also issued a decision to establish a working group to inspect and investigate the encroachment on flooded forest land in Tonle Sap area in Kampong Chhnang, Pursat, Battambang, Banteay Meanchey, Siem Reap and Kampong Thom provinces immediately. .
As a result, after the order of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, tens of thousands of hectares of flooded forest land were also reclaimed from illegal occupation and subsequent arrests were made in connection with this case. Separately, the confiscated land was also replanted with trees, while the location where the people enjoyed for many years, the Royal Government did not confiscate.
