Russia says West blamed for Ukraine grain crisis
The Kremlin said on Thursday that the West was responsible for the escalating food crisis due to the issue of Ukraine's grain shipments to world markets and demanded that the United States and its allies Eliminate the so-called illegal sanctions. This is according to the release by Reuters on Thursday, May 26, 2022.
In addition to the massive deaths and devastation caused by Russia's invasion of Ukraine, Western attempts to isolate Russia through sanctions have pushed up prices of grain, cooking oil, fertilizer and energy. The impact on global economic growth.
The United Nations, which says the global food crisis is worsening, is trying to mediate to liberate all of Ukraine's grain, while Western leaders have blamed Russia for closing the strait.
