(Kandal): 156 families living in temporary constructions of Dam 92.94 and Canal 54 in the Techo Takhmao International Cantonment Project received legal housing under the win-win policy, especially the Prime Minister Hun Sen Cambodia.
The handover ceremony was held on May 25, 2022 under the chairmanship of Mr. Kong Sophoan, Governor of Kandal Province and Mr. Beng Hong Socheat Khemro, Director General of the General Department of Housing and Chairman of the Working Group to Support the Preparation of the International Airport Project. Techo Krong Takhmao.
On that occasion, Mr. Beng Hong Socheat Khemro said that the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia has approved the construction of a new international airport to replace the Phnom Penh-Pochentong International Airport, which covers an area of only 400 hectares and can accommodate about 5 million passengers. . The Royal Government has selected Kandal Province and part of Takeo Province for the construction of TF Khmao Techo International Airport Class 4F on a total area of 2,600 hectares.
"The airport development project has affected 171 families who are temporarily staying on the 92.94 dam and 54 canals, and the Royal Government has decided to provide housing for all 171 families," he said. Granted them to stay until the issuance of a certificate of ownership of real estate to them today.
On the occasion of awarding the certificate of ownership of real estate, Mr. Kong Sophoan expressed his congratulations to all people who have received the certificate of ownership of real estate at this time.
The provincial governor continued that the provision of housing will lead to the issuance of real estate ownership certificates to the people at this time, which proves that the Royal Government under the wise leadership of Samdech Techo, who always takes into account the well-being of the people. Anytime, anywhere and close to the people without abandoning any citizen.
