General Commission of National Police opens basic training course for 257 police officers at Cambodia-Vietnam Friendship National Police School
(Kampong Speu): With the guidance and permission of General Dr. Neth Savoeun, General Commissioner of the National Police, this morning, May 26, 2022, the Cambodia-Vietnam Friendship National Police School held a basic training course for police officers. 257 people.
The opening ceremony was presided over by Lt. Gen. Chan Sitha, Deputy Commissioner General, Representative of Lt. Gen. Dr. Neth Savoeun, and was attended by Lt. Gen. Un On, Deputy Chief of Staff and Director of the Cambodia-Vietnam Friendship Police. Several other relevant police officers.
According to Lt. Gen. Un, a total of 257 trainees (35 females) from the General Secretariat of the National Police and the Anti-Counterfeit Products Training Committee are currently participating in the police vocational training. Which poses a high risk to 12 health and social safety.
He added that starting from the policy and strategy for the reform of the Cambodia-Vietnam Friendship National Police School, it has played an important role as a staff member for the General Commission of the National Police on the development of training plans for the National Police Force. .
After the inauguration in 2015, the school has opened 22 training courses for the National Police Force across the country, with a total of 2,666 participants, 119 females.
On that occasion, Lt. Gen. Chan Sitha praised the school leaders and all police officers of the Cambodia-Vietnam Friendship National Police School for their attention and responsibility for the training of the National Police Force from the beginning. To the present as well as to the future. He said that training now is really important.
The Deputy Commissioner of the National Police stated that in the face of challenges, the competent forces in the field of security and order must have high capacity and technical skills to perform their duties, as well as be agile and smart in Targeting to crack down and rescue in case of any incidents.
He added that studying at school is just a study of some theory and techniques that will help provide knowledge and skills for all trainees can be used in practice only when performing tasks. However, the practical implementation of the task requires the competent forces to perform their duties responsibly, using physical, mental and intellectual strength to solve the problems that arise.
On behalf of the General Commission of the National Police, Lt. Gen. Chan Sitha also shared some opinions on the direction of capacity building and improving the efficiency of the National Force as follows:
* First, we must continue to work to strengthen the National Police at all levels and in all areas, which are law enforcement forces with high professionalism, with proper respect for state laws, promote respect for human rights, and respect for the rights and freedoms of citizens. To be firm in their professional ethics, to be honest in their profession, to adhere to discipline, dignity and cleanliness in serving the people
* Second, while promoting the implementation of the policy of safe villages and communes in order to further strengthen security, safety, public order and respect for the law, and strongly promote long-term sustainable socio-economic development. And to provide comfort to the people and society as a whole
* Fifth: In order to improve the efficiency of the above tasks, the National Police must continue to be reformed more deeply by striving to increase the training and capacity building of the National Police at all levels while promoting professional conscience and respect. Moral discipline to improve the quality of the ability of the entire National Police Force to provide security services to the people more widely, honestly, friendly everywhere and on time
