(Phnom Penh): "Tourism co-financing project to restore and promote growth in the tourism sector" with a total financing amount of $ 150 million is to provide loans only for business bases in four target sectors, while the procedures and requirements vary according to Each state-owned bank or microfinance institution.
At the same time, Ms. Neou Sotheary, Director of Credit Project of SME Bank, also said that "Target sectors that will receive loans from this co-financing project include hotels, guesthouses, restaurants, businesses that supply products and services to support tourism. "Such as souvenirs, massages, transporting tourists."
She also mentioned the unique features of the co-financing scheme, saying that each business owner could borrow up to $ 400,000 with a special interest rate of 6.5% per annum (minimum). Up to 7 years with both fixed term and installment loan The business owner can use this loan as capital expenditure or working capital in the business.
She said that the loan application is made through the bank or microfinance institution that is a partner of SME Bank, so the business owner has to ask for details with the banking agent or the microfinance institution itself because the procedures and conditions are always different. Some in those institutions.
There are three main procedures and conditions for applying for a loan from this co-financing project:
2. The possibility of repayment is to check the financial statements, income, expenses, monthly, annual to assess the possibility of repayment to the bank or not or to what extent.
3: Purpose of the loan, whether the purpose of the loan is to restore the tourism business or to do something else? Because this loan is only for repairing, renovating old business locations or rehabilitating old businesses affected by the Kovid crisis.
"In principle, if any tourism business owner applies for a loan before receiving a loan from this co-financing project, when the bank or microfinance institution agrees, it means that you go first to get the loan first," said Neou Sotheary.
