Regarding this appointment, according to Article 33 of the statute of the Candlelight Party, which is kept at the Ministry of Interior, it is determined as follows:
"The party president appoints at least one vice chairman from among the members of the board of directors after the approval of the absolute majority of the board of directors for a five (five) year term. The Vice President of the Party shall lead the work of the party as determined by the Chairman. In the absence of the party president, one vice president is authorized by the party acting chairman.
Separately, Article 20 of the Statute of the Candlelight Party, which is related to the Congress, states that
"Representatives of party members, the congress determines the direction and politics of the party, is the party's top institution. The Congress shall be attended by the delegates and approve the major decisions submitted by the Board of Directors. The Congress elects the party president by an absolute majority vote (50% + 1) of the members present.
The rights and procedures for electing party presidents and members of the board of directors are set out in the party's internal regulations. "Congress can reform the party structure."
