China says it will hold military exercises near Taiwan as a warning to US
The Chinese military's Eastern Regional Command said it had just conducted exercises and patrols in the air and sea areas near Taiwan. "This is a warning against conspiracy between the United States and Taiwan," a spokesman for the headquarters said. "It's a hypocritical and vain act for the United States to speak differently and relate to the Taiwan issue."
On Monday, US President Joe Biden angered Beijing by saying the United States would use military force to help Taiwan if China attacked the island. But on Tuesday, Biden also clarified that there was no change in China's policy on the Taiwan issue.
So far, China has not ruled out the use of military force to reunite with Taiwan, and the Taiwan Strait remains a hotbed of possible military conflicts.
As the United States adheres to the "one China" policy, giving Beijing official recognition only, Washington has made a commitment under its own law to provide a means of self-defense for Taiwan. However, the United States has continued to pursue a strategic policy that does not specify a clear reaction to the response in case China launches an attack on Taiwan.
