World Bank Senior Officials: Five Activities to Create Rehabilitation Programs to Meet Education Poverty
(Phnom Penh) - In a special lecture on "Poverty of Education", Toby Linden, Director of Education for East Asia and the Pacific of the World Bank, stated that measures to address poverty Of study can be done by creating a rehabilitation program as a framework with five core activities.
Mr. Toby Linden said this morning, May 25, 2022, in a lecture organized by the Royal University of Phnom Penh with the participation of Dr. Chet Chealy, Rector of the Royal University of Phnom Penh. Also present were leaders of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, professors and students of the Royal University of Phnom Penh.
Toby Linden added that Kovid 19 had disrupted school operations. According to data showing the global drop in education in the Asia-Pacific region, schools were temporarily suspended for an average of 175 days between February 2020 and February 2022. Prior to the outbreak, 53% of 10-year-olds in low- and middle-income countries could not read easily and the rate of improvement in education was very slow.
He added that after the epidemic, the poverty of education can reach a high level of more than 70%. In the case of Cambodia, the number of students with basic disability increased from 34% to 45% for the Khmer language, so urgent measures are needed to ensure that students in this generation receive a better education than the previous generation.
NEC Introduces Political Parties' Campaigning for Elections
(Phnom Penh): Pursuant to the Law on Commune / Sangkat Council Election (CPPCC) and the Rules and Procedures for the 5th Mandate Commune / Sangkat Council Election 2022 (CPPCC) ) The election campaign aims for political parties that are allowed to register candidates and disseminate their policies and political programs for commune development to voters.
The election campaign lasts for 14 days and all campaign activities must stop 24 hours before election day. Based on the calendar of the 5th Mandate Commune / Sangkat Council Election 2022, the election campaign will start from May 21 to June 3, 2022.
During the first few days of the campaign, with the coordination and good cooperation of the local authorities and the Election Commission at the hierarchical level, all registered political parties conducted campaigning activities. Each constituency, as far as possible, in accordance with the designated program and in an environment of security, safety and public order, non-violent, non-threatening.
In order to make the election campaign of political parties run more smoothly in accordance with the laws and regulations in force, the NEC would like to introduce the following to all political parties and candidates:
* Second: Do not buy to motivate voters by providing financial means, facilities or other means.
* Fourth, to inform the Commune / Sangkat Election Commission at least 3 days before the campaign day and to follow the guidelines of the competent authorities to ensure security, safety, public order and avoid traffic jams.
* Fifth: Must strictly abide by the rules, regulations and procedures of the election, ethics for political parties and candidates in the election process and other relevant legal documents in force.
The NEC strongly hopes that all political parties and candidates will work together to implement this guideline with a high sense of responsibility so that the upcoming election campaign and election can be free, fair and just. As well as ensuring a good political environment before and after the election.
