Mr. Chak Borin, Director of the Department of Labor and Vocational Training of Kampong Speu Province, said that the case of fainting started from the glue bag in the factory and later sent to the hospital for treatment.
When they arrived at the hospital, the doctors received treatment and examination, but what the doctors confirmed was that all the workers did not have any disease and did not find any symptoms. What they are interested in is that some workers do not allow the doctors to treat them, they try to move and shout for only bananas and boiled chicken.
