Teng Vanthoeun, an official with the Kampot Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, said that in general, Kampot durian usually begins to be harvested gradually from March to July, and the peak season is from May to June.
He said that at the beginning of the Duren Kampot season this year can sell an average of 32,000 riel per kilogram for the series, 35,000 riel per kilogram and 40,000 riel per kilogram.
He said that while there is an opening at the border of neighboring countries, Kampot Duren has to compete with durians imported from Thailand and Vietnam, which are cheaper than Kampot durians. However, it does not seem to affect the Kampot durian market much because the local durian has better quality and taste. He worries that a small number of traders cheat Kampot Duren to sell to customers, damaging the reputation of Kampot Duren products.
