(Bali, Indonesia): Mr. Hang Samoeun, Vice Chairman and Advisor to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, Representative of General Kun Kim, Senior Minister and First Vice Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management, led the delegation to attend the 7th session of Global Forum for Disaster Risk Reduction, held from 23 to 28 May 2022 in Bali, Indonesia.
Accompanying delegates to the forum included Mr. Ing Heang, Cambodian Ambassador to Indonesia, and other senior officials of the National Committee for Disaster Management.
The Global Forum for Disaster Risk Reduction has the direct participation of ministers from 31 countries. The Global Forum for Disaster Risk Reduction is an important global forum to evaluate and discuss progress on the implementation of the Sendai Framework for Disaster Risk Reduction. The event is co-chaired by the Government of Indonesia and the United Nations Disaster Risk Reduction (UNDRR).
The forum will provide a unique and timely opportunity to highlight the importance of international solidarity and cooperation, as well as discuss ways to address risks both locally and globally. In addition, the forum will explore how to strengthen disaster risk management and how to build a stronger system to manage all types of risks.
