(Phnom Penh): The Constitutional Council unanimously approved that the Law on the Amendment of Article 140 of the Law on the Administration of Capital, Province, Municipality, District and Khan is in accordance with the Constitution.
At the request of Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly, on the morning of May 25, 2022, Dr. M. Chhun Lim, President of the Constitutional Council, convened a plenary session to review the constitutionality of the Law on the Amendment of Article 140 of the Law on Manage capital, province, municipality, district and Khan administration.
After meeting and reviewing in detail, the Constitutional Council unanimously decided that the Law on the Amendment of Article 140 of the Law on the Administration of the Capital, Provinces, Municipalities, Districts and Khans was in accordance with the Constitution.
The draft law on the amendment of Article 140 of the Law on the Administration of Capital, Province, Municipality, District and Khan was approved by the Royal Government at the meeting of the Council of Ministers on April 1 and was reviewed and approved by the National Assembly on May 11. Go here. After approval, Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin asked the Constitutional Council to review the constitutionality of the draft law.
After receiving the proposal, the Constitutional Council proceeded with the proceedings. On May 24, Dr. M. Chhun Lim met with representatives of the Royal Government regarding the amendment of Article 140 of the Law on Capital, Province, Municipality, District and Khan Administration.
Amendments to Article 140 of the Law on the Administration of the Capital, Provinces, Municipalities, Districts and Khans have paved the way for increasing the number of Capital, Provincial, Municipal, District and Khan Governors.
The Law on Capital, Province, Municipality, District and Khan Administration shall be promulgated by Royal Kram No. NS / RKAM / 0508/017 dated 24 May 2008. In the old Article 140, the composition of the Board of Governors of the Capital, Provinces, Municipalities, Districts and Khans was determined as follows:
Separately, the new Article 140, which was amended, increased the number of Capital, Provincial, Municipal, District and Khan Board of Governors as follows:
* Phnom Penh Capital Board has a maximum of 11 members. * Provincial Board of Governors has 7 to 11 members. * The Board of Governors of 5 districts and 7 Khans. The actual number of the Board of Governors for the Capital, Province, Municipality, District and Khan shall be determined by sub-decree at the request of the Minister of Interior.
