(Davos-Cluster, Switzerland): At the ASEAN Strategic Response Forum, Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen, as the chair of ASEAN, emphasized that ASEAN has a clear policy of not choosing a superpower. That.
The World Economic Forum, held in Davos-Gloucester, Switzerland on the morning of May 24, 2022, opened a special discussion on "Strategic Aspects for ASEAN and Cambodia's ASEAN Chairmanship in 2022". . The talks were attended by five keynote speakers: Samdech Techo Hun Sen as ASEAN Chair and four other economic experts from Singapore, Indonesia, Malaysia and Europe.
The talks focused on ASEAN's challenges in the face of the superpower crisis, especially between China and the US, maritime disputes, food crisis, energy security, climate change and the crisis between Russia and Ukraine. Also. Each economic speaker highlighted the challenges and difficulties of ASEAN and also outlined some tips to address this.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Senior Speaker of the Forum, was given the priority to make a final joint conclusion on the topics discussed as well as to highlight some of the priorities that Cambodia will adhere to as ASEAN Chair.
Hun Sen addresses a number of key challenges, including the challenge of superpowers, Indo-Pacific initiatives, maritime disputes between China and ASEAN member states, and Russia's war of aggression against Ukraine. .
Samdech Techo emphasized that ASEAN is a community in a situation that has an impact on itself. Regarding the competition between the great powers of China and the United States, Samdech Techo stressed that ASEAN should not choose anyone.
"Geopolitical competition has made our ASEAN very difficult," he said.
Hun Sen also recalled the Indo-Pacific Initiative, an initiative to counter Chinese influence in Southeast Asia. However, Samdech Techo stressed that any initiative related to the Indo-Pacific must serve three purposes: first: to serve peace and development, second: not to oppose any country, and third: Serve the ASEAN Center.
Samdech Techo also mentioned that ASEAN also has its own initiatives related to the Indo-Pacific. Samdech requested the countries involved in this initiative to support the initiative established by ASEAN.
Regarding the maritime dispute between China and ASEAN member countries, Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that ASEAN continues to push for the implementation of the DOC Code, which was issued when Cambodia chaired ASEAN in 2002 and achieved the code. Execute COC. In particular, the promotion of dialogue between the parties to the conflict.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also mentioned that the biggest challenge for the world and ASEAN is Russia's war of aggression against Ukraine. Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that currently this war creates only an energy crisis, but in the future there will be a food crisis.
Regarding the war between Russia and Ukraine, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also said that the use of sanctions should be stopped because it is useless and affect both the sanctioned country and the sanctioned country.
At the end of the intervention, Samdech Techo highlighted that in order to resolve the crisis facing ASEAN, ASEAN will strive to promote ASEAN integration as soon as possible through agreements, especially free trade agreements.
