Cambodia, Australia vow to work together to improve health and safety in Cambodia's construction sector
The guidelines are divided into three sections and cover a wide range of topics, including responsibility for health and safety at the construction site, use of personal protective equipment, and first aid and protection of children and young workers. The guidelines also provide additional protections for female construction workers, including procedures for understanding and addressing gender-based violence and harassment at construction sites.
The approved guidelines will be a key component of Cambodia's construction law. These guidelines are essential for the construction industry in Cambodia and are being prepared at a time when the construction sector is booming.
The guidelines were developed with the support of the Australian Government's $ 51.7 million Infrastructure Investment Program (3i). In June 2022, there will be a series of outreach workshops on this guideline in Phnom Penh, Siem Reap, Sihanoukville and Sen Monorom.
