Police Arrest Woman Who Raped 5-Year-Old Child in Toul Kork District
(Phnom Penh): A woman who used brutal violence against a 5-year-old girl in Tuol Kork district and was posted on social media was arrested and sent to the Tuol Kork police station for questioning. Continue the procedure on the morning of May 24, 2022.
San Sok Seiha, a spokesman for the Phnom Penh Municipal Police, said that the suspect was arrested in connection with a case of beating his face with a hand and using a machete to hang his daughter's clothes on the 23rd. May 2022 at around 23:30 in front of 13Eo, Street 219, Group 22, Village 03, Sangkat Phsar Depot 1, Khan Toul Kork.
According to Mr. San Sok Seiha, the suspect is currently being held in custody at the Tuol Kork Police Inspectorate for questioning and further proceedings. The police handed over the girl to the Department of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation of Phnom Penh and the Department of Social Affairs of Phnom Penh to send the girl to the Phnom Penh Referral Hospital under the care of Mith Samlanh.
Separately, the National Committee for the Protection of Children of the National Council of Cambodia for Children (NCCC) strongly condemned the unacceptable acts of intentional, brutal and inhumane acts committed by Chan Thida. . At the same time, the NCDD would like to commend and thank the authorities at all levels for taking legal and timely action on this case.
The National Commission for the Protection of Children also claims that this case has caused a great deal of shock and sympathy for the poor girl who was the victim of brutal and inhumane violence and considers it a serious abuse. On the rights of the child, especially the right to protection, which Cambodia has ratified and enshrined in the Constitution of Cambodia.
In relation to this inhumane violence, the National Committee for the Protection of Children of the NCDD, as the coordinating body for child rights work, calls on and urges all levels of authorities, especially the judiciary, to take action in accordance with applicable legal procedures. And punish this suspect very strictly so that this evil act does not happen in our society again.
