Phnom Penh Capital Hall Groundbreaking Ceremony for Toilet Mud Treatment Station in Kambol District
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of May 24, 2022, Phnom Penh Capital Administration inaugurated the construction site of Toilet Waste Treatment Station, located in Sangkat Pleung Cheh Roret, Khan Kampol, under the chairmanship of Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh and Mr. Pier Beyer. Permanent Secretary of the International Association of French Mayors.
Mr. Khuong Sreng said that according to a 2001 study, the amount of toilet waste in Phnom Penh is about 26,000 cubic meters per year and has continued to increase. It is estimated that by 2035, the latrine waste of the people in Phnom Penh will increase to 330,000 cubic meters per year, which requires the proper arrangement of the latrine treatment plant in accordance with technical standards that do not Harm to the environment.
According to Mr. Khuong Sreng, Phnom Penh is currently highly developed in both breadth and depth, in which the administrative boundary has been expanded from 300 to 692.46 square kilometers, with a population of about 3 million people living and working. . Meanwhile, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, directed the development of the physical infrastructure sector in Phnom Penh to address the three congestion:
As the national economy grows, cities grow, population grows, and resources become more plentiful, the supply and demand of citizens will inevitably increase.
Mr. Khuong Sreng continued, "This is the real Cambodia", which in the past there was no need for this type of treatment station because people have a poor living standard, no food and no standard of living. But in the post-techno era, people's lives have improved and there is enough food, so the standard of living in the city must also be gradually improved.
This project will provide three main benefits, including: First, environmental benefits through proper management of toilet waste, Second: Social benefits through job creation and recycling of toilet waste into reduced organic matter The use of chemical fertilizers and third: the economic benefits through the sale of organic fertilizers produced in the agricultural market, or in other words, "waste management."
At the same time, Mr. Pierre Bayer stated that the organization of the toilet waste treatment plant is a policy to improve the lives of people in Phnom Penh with climate change. The toilet waste will turn into fertilizer for farmers and it will provide jobs for small companies.
