(Phnom Penh): Dr. M. Chhun Lim, President of the Constitutional Council, this morning, May 24, 2022, met with representatives of the Royal Government regarding the amendment of Article 140 of the Law on the Administration of Capital, Province, Municipality, District and Khan. Amending or amending this article paves the way for an increase in the number of Capital, Provincial, Municipal, District and Khan Board of Governors.
Dr. Prohm Vichet Akhara, spokesman for the Constitutional Council, told Fresh News that in accordance with the provisions of Article 21 of the Law on the Organization and Functioning of the Constitutional Council, the Constitutional Council is allowed to summon all stakeholders to comment. Make a law or amend any law when there is a request for review from the National Assembly.
Dr. Prohm Vichet Akhra said that the representatives of the Royal Government who came to clarify the amendment of Article 140 of the Law on the Administration of Capital, Province, Municipality, District and Khan this morning, led by Mr. Sak Setha, Permanent Secretary of the Ministry of Interior, who is Relevant ministries in drafting this law.
According to the spokesperson of the Constitutional Council, during the meeting, the Honorary Legal Officer, Dr. M. Chhun Lim, discussed the purpose and necessity that led to the amendment of Article 140 of the Law on the Administration of Capital, Province, Municipality, District and Khan.
Dr. Prohm Vichet Akra said that tomorrow, May 25, the Constitutional Council, chaired by Dr. M. Chhun Lim, will hold a meeting to review and decide on the granting or non-granting of the Constitution on the Amendment of Article 140. Of the Law on the Administration of the Capital, Province, Municipality, District and Khan.
The draft law on the amendment of Article 140 of the Law on the Administration of Capital, Province, Municipality, District and Khan was approved by the Royal Government at the meeting of the Council of Ministers on April 1 and was reviewed and approved by the National Assembly on May 11. Go here. Amendments to Article 140 pave the way for increasing the composition of the Capital, Provincial, Municipal, District and Khan Governments.
