Tycoon Lim Heng, vice president of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, told Fresh News from Zurich, Switzerland, that this was the first time the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce had set up a representative office of an overseas Chamber of Commerce. The first representative office of the Chamber of Commerce will open in Toronto on May 27, 2022.
He added that the opening of a representative office of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce in Canada will further boost exports of goods from Cambodia to the country, as trade between Cambodia and Canada has now grown steadily. Cambodia's exports to Canada are also large.
"After we have a representative office of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce in Canada, I believe it will boost the trade volume between Cambodia and Canada," he said. "For our past exports to Cambodia, most of our goods are textiles, garments, travel accessories, bags, shoes, bicycles, electrical equipment and some other agricultural products that we export to Canada."
He said that on May 25, he will travel to Canada to vote for 14 members of the Chamber of Commerce and President of the Chamber of Commerce in Toronto, Canada.
According to the Vice President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, after opening a representative office in Toronto, Canada, Cambodia will continue to open a second office in Japan in the near future, which has already been decided by the Royal Government.
According to data released by the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia, Canada is the fourth largest exporter of goods to Cambodia.
In the first four months of 2022, Cambodia exported more than 340 million US dollars worth of goods to this country, an increase of 22.9% compared to the same period in 2021, which amounted to more than 277 million US dollars. In April, exports to Canada were worth more than $ 53 million, up 84.3 percent.
