Court sentences stepfather to 2-year-old girl in Meanchey district to 20 years in prison
(Phnom Penh): The President of the Trial Chamber of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court on the morning of May 24, 2022, held a hearing to announce the verdict on the case of the torture and murder of a 2-year-old girl by her stepfather, and decided to convict the accused. He was sentenced to 20 years in prison for "aggravated murder in connection with the victim."
Please be reminded that stepfather Sok Ratha, 29 years old, was sent by the Meanchey district police to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court on July 2, 2021, and the perpetrator was investigated by the prosecutor, Mr. Seng Heang. And decided to charge him with "aggravated murder in connection with the victim."
Meanchey District Police arrested the suspect at a rented house on Lum Road, Russey Village, Sangkat Steung Meanchey II, Khan Meanchey, Phnom Penh on June 30, 2021 at 13:15.
