Senior Minister Ly Thuch Outlines the Royal Government of Cambodia's Commitment to Eliminate Landmines and Explosives at the Annual Meeting of UN ESCAP
(Bangkok-Thailand): On May 23, 2022, Senior Minister Ly Thuch, Chairman of the National Committee for ESCAP, made a statement on the will of the Royal Government of Cambodia to participate in international cooperation under the multilateral framework to restore Renew the socio-economic situation and promote prosperity for all at the 78th Annual Meeting of UN ESCAP.
In a statement, Senior Minister Ly Thuch said that Cambodia's commitment to international cooperation and the implementation of a common agenda was reflected in Cambodia's support for the adoption of the Sustainable Development Goals at the UN General Assembly. Nations in 2015 and the introduction of the framework for the Sustainable Development Goals of Cambodia 2016-2030, which has 18 goals and the 18th goal is "Cambodia without landmines and explosive remnants of war."
He also said that the implementation of the 2030 Agenda was hampered by factors such as the Kovid-19 crisis, geopolitical competition and climate change, which called for the international community to increase cooperation. Closer cohesion enhances efficient connectivity and increases the openness and environment of the global economy.
He said resolving these issues requires a joint decision within the framework of multilateralism, respecting international law and the sovereignty of each country, regardless of size or wealth. He stressed that Cambodia is ready to join bilateral and multilateral development partners in efforts to restore socio-economic status and promote prosperity for all.
