Phnom Penh Administration Signs Partnership Agreement with International Association of French Mayors (AIMF)
(Phnom Penh): The Phnom Penh Capital Administration has signed a partnership agreement with the International Association of French Mayors (AIMF) on disaster preparedness, disaster management, waste management strategies, and strategic roadmaps on The city is smart and sustainable.
The signing ceremony took place on the morning of May 23, 2022 in the presence of Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh and Mr. Pierre Baiyer, Permanent Secretary of the French Speaking Association (AIMF) at Phnom Penh Capital Hall.
The signing ceremony of the Partnership Agreement between the Phnom Penh Municipal Administration and the International Association of French Mayors (AIMF) includes:
* Disaster preparedness response work * Mud waste management strategies * Toilets: Strategic roadmaps on smart and sustainable cities.
The working visit of the French Speaking Association (AIMF) delegation led by Pierre Baiyer has three objectives:
* First, the approval of the work of the cooperation project between AIMF and Phnom Penh administration, especially the signing of the partnership agreement between Phnom Penh administration and AIMF in setting up a network of Southeast Asian cities using French in the cover. AIMF Strategic Partnership with the European Union Dissemination of study documents and strategic documents prepared and approved by the Phnom Penh Capital Administration.
* Second: Examining the actual project being implemented with the groundbreaking ceremony for the construction of a toilet waste treatment plant in Phnom Penh and in Siem Reap, the construction of a community center in Phnom Penh within the framework of the financing project.
* Third: Meetings and demonstrations of international partners in Cambodia: Meetings with the Ministry of Interior, the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, the European Union, donors and partners of the Phnom Penh and Siem Reap administrations, and the French Embassy in Preah Sihanouk. Kingdom of Cambodia.
Mr. Khuong Sreng said that in 2019, Phnom Penh hosted the 40th AIMF Meeting in Phnom Penh. It is an honor and a great honor for Phnom Penh to provide experience in the development of AIMF member cities and to be highly commended because Phnom Penh is a city born of a ghost town and out of zero.
It should be noted that Phnom Penh joined the AIMF in 1990 and became a member of the association's office in 2003, out of a total of 307 members, only 27 permanent members were elected as meditators. The permanent office of the association. Phnom Penh is the only member of Asia composed of this permanent office.
