TOKYO (Reuters) - US President Joe Biden arrived in Japan on Sunday for a second visit to strengthen US alliance in Asia after concluding his first visit to South Korea. This was released by the AFP news agency on Sunday, May 22, 2022.
Biden, who is visiting Asia for the first time as US president, has arrived at Yokota Air Force Base on the outskirts of Tokyo and is scheduled to meet with the Prime Minister. Japan's Fumio Kishida on Monday early next week.
