During a meeting with Cambodians living in Europe, Samdech Techo Hun Sen claimed that so far Cambodia has received a total of 52 million doses of the vaccine and 42 million doses have been used, of which 28.5 million doses are from Cambodia. Use the national budget to buy, which shows that Cambodia does not allow people to die from Kovid 19 disease.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said, "The vaccine arrived in Cambodia in 52 million doses. We released 42 million doses, of which 28.5 million doses were purchased by Cambodia itself, more than half." "It means that the government does not allow its people to die without vaccines or without treatment."
According to the Prime Minister, in addition to the vaccine, which Cambodia uses more than 50 percent of the national budget to buy, there is also assistance from friendly countries, including China, Japan, the United States, Italy, Hungary, Poland, the Netherlands, Australia and some other countries. Others have just sent the 19 Kovid vaccine to Cambodia.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stressed that the Kovid 19 vaccination program was successful because Cambodia has launched a series of vaccinations in Phnom Penh and Kandal province, then continue to inject to other provinces to spread the vaccine. The prince called this strategy the "flower approach." The prince also claimed that the vaccination process was not right and that the community was not strong enough.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen noted that some countries have vaccines, but not as strong as Cambodia, because those countries do not distribute vaccines properly, which means that those who have not been vaccinated more than those who have been vaccinated, so there is no community. Strong.
Regarding the Kovid 19 vaccine, Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasized that the vaccine not only prevents the Kovid 19 disease, but also protects the health of people from other diseases such as the flu. All this makes the Royal Government of Cambodia see that vaccines still play an important role that we must continue to work to promote this work.
