Siem Reap Provincial Commission for the Implementation of the National Employment Policy 2015-2025 Approves the Action Plan for 2022-2023
(Siem Reap): Mr. Som Chamnan, Undersecretary of State of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, and Mr. Nak Neron, Deputy Governor of Siem Reap Province, on the morning of May 20, 2022, chaired a meeting to review and approve the Action Plan 2022-2023 of the Siem Reap Provincial Committee. To implement the National Employment Policy 2015-2025
The Deputy Governor added that this action plan will be implemented jointly under the authority of the respective departments and close cooperation with the Secretariat team of the Department of Labor and Vocational Training in Siem Reap. He expressed interest in implementing this national policy together to achieve the strategic plan of the Royal Government of Cambodia, the fifth legislature of the National Assembly in the third phase.
Mr. Som Chamnan thanked the relevant departments and institutions of Siem Reap Provincial Administration and the Secretariat of the Inter-Ministerial Commission (SECC) for their efforts in drafting this action plan until it was approved.
Under the Secretary of State, if this action plan is implemented to the maximum, it will contribute to the harmony in Siem Reap by providing the people with decent and productive job opportunities, promoting the development of skills and human resources, and Strengthen labor market governance.
The Undersecretary of State stated that Siem Reap is the first province to have an action plan for 2022-2023 to implement the National Employment Policy 2015-2025 and also considered a model province for the other 24 provinces - capital model. To review and compile an action plan for their province as well.
The vision of this policy is to focus on improving the lives, dignity of the people, social harmony through the creation of decent and productive employment opportunities for all Cambodians with equity.
