Pursat Provincial Administration Celebrates National Day on May 20 to Commemorate Those Who Died During the Pol Pot Genocide
(Pursat): On the afternoon of May 20, 2022, at the Keo Vichey pagoda, Kandieng district, leaders, civil servants, youth, the armed forces, monks and people in Pursat province celebrated the National Day on May 20 to commemorate The souls of the people who lost their lives during the genocidal regime of Pol Pot.
The ceremony was attended by Mr. Mak Ra, Chairman of the Provincial Council, Mr. Chiao Tai, Governor of Pursat Province, as well as members of the Provincial Council, Deputy Governors, leaders of various departments around the province, local authorities, government officials, teachers, Ta Chi people. Grandmothers, students and young people in large numbers.
Please be informed that the National Day of Remembrance on May 20 is a memorial service for the more than 3 million victims who lost their lives during the Pol Pot genocidal regime. Every Cambodian will never forget the Democratic Kampuchea regime or the so-called Pol Pot genocidal regime (April 17, 1975 - January 6, 1979), a brutal and dark regime.
The National Day of Remembrance on May 20 was designated by the National Assembly of the People's Republic of Cambodia in 1983 as the "Day of Anger" to commemorate the Khmer Rouge regime's massacre of the Cambodian people. May 20, 1973 was the birthday of the cooperatives of the Khmer Rouge Democratic Kampuchea regime, and the war continued until it reached Phnom Penh on April 17, 1975.
