For 5 days this week, the General Department of Customs and Excise cracked down on 27 duty-free vehicles nationwide
(Phnom Penh): For 5 days from May 16 to 20, 2022, the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia cracked down on 27 duty-free vehicles throughout the country, all of which took refuge under fake license plates.
The 27 vehicles that the General Department of Customs and Excise seized in this week include:
The last deadline of the existing car tax collection campaign in the country is June 30, 2022, and from July 1, 2022 onwards, the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia is not eligible to pay vehicle tax. Already in that country, the main role is to crack down.
In the case where the duty-free vehicle was cracked down after June 30, 2022, the left-hand drive vehicle will have to pay tax according to the law in force and pay more fines. Right-hand drive vehicles, when suppressed, will be disassembled and converted into car parts, as right-hand drive vehicles are banned from importing for domestic use and can be destroyed.
Mr. Kun Nhim also called on car owners who have not yet brought their cars to pay taxes, please hurry to fulfill their tax obligations by June 30, 2022.
Please be informed that from September to December 31, 2021, the Royal Government of Cambodia, through the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia, has allowed duty-free vehicles on left-hand drive vehicles to pay taxes with a 10% tax preference. Right-hand drive vehicles (turn the steering wheel and pay taxes) will receive a 10 percent tax concession until June 30, 2022.
As of May 3, 2022, nearly 7,000 duty-free vehicles under various license plates, both left-hand drive and right-hand drive, have entered and declared and paid $ 60 million in taxes to the national budget.
Phnom Penh Capital Hall Holds a Consultative Meeting on the Final Draft of the Smart Roadmap on Smart and Sustainable Cities of Phnom Penh 2022-2035
(Phnom Penh): The Phnom Penh Capital Administration held a consultative meeting on the final draft of the Smart Roadmap on Smart and Sustainable Cities of Phnom Penh 2022-2035 at the 11th floor of Phnom Penh Capital Hall. Attended by senior technical officers of the Ministry - professional institutions and many relevant experts.
This document has passed the Committee for Study and Implementation of Phnom Penh Sustainable and Intelligent Development Project, with Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh as the Chairman of the Commission.
He added that the process of organizing a smart city is a long process that requires a lot of resources, both human resources, financial resources, as well as the commitment of leaders at all levels, however, we can start with the project. Some specific to the possibility of our capital, as well as the possibility of cooperation and support from relevant ministries - institutions.
This Smart and Sustainable Strategic Roadmap document focuses on five key priority areas, including:
* First: intelligent urban management * Second: safe and secure city * Third: intelligent traffic system * Fourth: intelligent living environment * Fifth: smart governance
For the study and preparation of this document was made in accordance with the possibility of the Capital Administration and the participation of the Association (AIMF), which in the last stage, the Capital Administration requested the participation of the relevant ministries - professional institutions to This document is more official and more comprehensive.
Today's consultation meeting on the final draft received comments and input from professional officials of relevant ministries and institutions, including: Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, Royal University of Fine Arts, University of Technology of Cambodia, Ministry Public Works and Transport, Ministry of Environment, Ministry of Economy and Finance and Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications.
