KOICA and the Ministry of Health Hold a Meeting of the National Coordinating Committee of the Maternal and Child Health Project in Northeastern Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): The Korea International Cooperation Agency (KICA) in collaboration with the Ministry of Health has organized a meeting of the National Coordinating Committee for the Maternal and Child Health Project in the northeastern province of Cambodia.
The meeting was also attended by all members of the National Coordinating Committee, such as Mondulkiri and Ratanakkiri Provincial Health Departments, National Center for Maternal and Child Health (NMCHC), National Center for Health Promotion (NCHP) to share information and collect input. On project implementation and follow-up implementation plan.
The meeting included discussions to share information on project activities and gather input from stakeholders as recommendations and suggestions for future plans for project implementation. Dr. Hok Kimchheng thanked the Customs Agency as well as the people of the Republic of Korea for supporting this project.
The Maternal and Child Health Project in the Northeastern Province of Cambodia is a four-year project (2019-2023) implemented under a grant from the Republic of Korea through a US $ 7 million agency. The project is being implemented in Ratanakkiri and Mondulkiri provinces with the aim of improving maternal and child health by improving the quality and access to maternal and child health services.
