(Phnom Penh): At more than 1 am on May 21, 2022, the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen will lead a high-level delegation to fly from Cambodia to Davos-Closter, Switzerland to participate. World Economic Forum, held from 22 to 26 May 2022.
According to the Cambodian Ministry of Foreign Affairs, Samdech Techo's presence at the World Economic Forum is now at the invitation of Professor Claus Chbab, the founder and CEO of the World Economic Forum.
According to the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of Cambodia, during his participation in this forum, Samdech Techo Prime Minister Hun Sen will deliver a meaningful speech at the closing ceremony of the dialogue with stakeholders under the theme "Strategic Perspective on ASEAN" and in Informal lunch program with world economic leaders under the theme "Restoring Peace and Order".
Samdech Techo's personal presence in this meeting is a testament to the prestige of Cambodia and the bringing of great historical honor to Cambodia.
It should be noted that in 2022, including the invitation to Switzerland, Samdech Techo Hun Sen has been invited to work abroad five times.
