It should be noted that the gifts received by 400 families were 25 kg of rice, 1 box of noodles, 1 box of fish, 1 bottle of cooking oil, 1 bottle of soy sauce and 1 stick of fish sauce.
Kampong Thom Constituency Deputies Celebrate National Remembrance Day on May 20 in Prasat Throne District
(Kampong Thom): Mr. Chea Oeung, Member of Parliament for Kampong Thom Constituency and Chairman of Prasat Balang District Field Team, on May 20, 2022, together with the people, celebrated the National Day of Remembrance in Sala Visay Commune, Prasat Balang District, Kampong Thom Province. Kampong Thom.
Mr. Chea Oeun said that May 20 was a day when the Cambodian people could not forget the massacre of more than 3 million people during the Khmer Rouge regime, Pol Pot or Democratic Kampuchea.
He said that the Democratic Kampuchea regime established a cooperative regime on May 20, 1973, during their guerrilla warfare, but that was the day the Khmer Rouge adopted a policy of killing opposition groups.
He said that this day commemorates the souls of more than 3 million victims who died in the genocidal regime of Pol Pot, and the vast majority of Cambodians know and understand the bitter tragedy that people Cambodians have gone through nearly three decades of flames of war, slaughter, destruction, forced evictions, and forced labor.
Not only that, Cambodians have to die without medicine, without enough food, without freedom, without democracy, and not even the right to life, which is a fundamental right.
He added, however, that the dictatorship collapsed on January 7, 1979, when the CPP Front Army, backed by the Vietnamese Volunteer Army, came to liberate it from the genocidal regime.
He also reminded that in 2018, the Royal Government has designated May 20 as the National Day of Remembrance. This day is designated as an official national holiday to commemorate the victims and victims of the crimes committed during the Democratic Kampuchea regime from April 17, 1975 to January 6, 1979.
Mr. Chea Oeung also called on all people to join in maintaining peace with the government under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister and President of the Cambodian People's Party, which makes the country progress in all areas.
