(Takeo): The Ministry of Rural Development has officially launched the "Rural Economic Diversification Project for Low-Income Farmers" and the "Clean Water Distribution Project for the Future Together" in Kirivong District, Takeo Province under the Special Cooperation Fund. Mekong-Lanchang.
The "Rural Economic Diversification Project for Low-Income Farmers" will focus on the implementation of activities such as the construction of community vegetable warehouses, the construction of rice barns, the construction of cold storage for vegetables, the provision of vegetable seeds and fertilizers. And agricultural equipment, the provision of processing and packaging equipment, the development of soap making skills, as well as workshops.
It should also be noted that the Mekong-Lanchang cooperation is a new type of sub-regional cooperation between the six countries along the Lancang-Mekong River (China, Cambodia, Laos, Myanmar, Thailand and Vietnam) with the common goal of economic development. - The society of the countries in the Mekong region, focusing on improving the well-being of the people, reducing the development gap in the region and building a community with a peaceful and prosperous future together.
At the same time, he said, "China and Cambodia are steel friends and a common destiny community, and the cooperation of our two countries under the framework of the Lancang-Mekong cooperation has always been at the forefront." This operation always follows the principle of "practical, high efficiency, take the project as the principle of people's livelihood first."
The Chinese Embassy said that as a good neighbor, good friend, good brother and good partner of Cambodia, the Chinese side will continue to provide as much support and assistance as possible for the socio-economic development and improvement of people's lives. Cambodians, as well as to promote the common prosperity of the Lancang-Mekong region, build a common destiny community for Asia, and build a common destiny community for humanity.
In response to the implementation of the above two projects, Mr. Sok Sokan, on behalf of the Kirivong District Field Team, expressed his congratulations and thanked the Ministry of Rural Development, the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, and all Stakeholders who have worked hard to push both projects to emerge in Kirivong district.
He continued that Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, is committed to maintaining this hard-earned peace for many generations to come, while at the same time continuing to expand opportunities to improve people's lives. More.
