IMF praises the effectiveness of the Royal Government and the National Bank of Cambodia in implementing economic and social support policies
This assessment was made during his visit to Cambodia on 16 and 17 May 2022 to strengthen cooperation between the International Monetary Fund and Cambodia.
Mr. Kenji Okamura praised the measures to control the spread of Kovi 19 in Cambodia and praised the effectiveness of the implementation of economic and social support policies of the Royal Government and the National Bank of Cambodia.
He also expressed his pleasure at seeing the benefits of the International Monetary Fund's technical assistance to Cambodia and the International Monetary Fund's support for Cambodia's development. He hailed the recovery of the Cambodian economy in 2021 and the positive outlook for economic growth for 2022 and 2023.
Mr. Sum Sanisit briefed Mr. Kenji Okamura on the development of Cambodia's economy and thanked the International Monetary Fund for its support, especially technical assistance for economic development and the banking sector in Cambodia since the early 1990s.
The Deputy Governor also pointed out that the technical assistance of the International Monetary Fund has continued to play an important role in the development of human and institutional resources, as well as strengthen the regular monitoring of Cambodia's economic health.
1. The rapid reopening of the economy and the country, which is conducive to tourism and economic activity. 2. The rapid growth of exports, especially garments. 3. The resilience of the real estate sector, especially from domestic demand. 4: Continuing to receive support from fiscal policies and macro-financial measures.
He added, however, that Cambodia was also facing a number of global influences, including: 1. The crisis in Ukraine and the decline in demand from Europe. 2. Slow Chinese economic growth due to policies to prevent the spread of Kovid-19 and the real estate sector. 3. Increased inflation, especially of oil and food-related goods and services.
At the same time, the Mission praised the results of the Capacity Development Program provided by the International Monetary Fund to the National Bank of Cambodia.
Current capacity development programs, especially those related to the National Bank of Cambodia, include banking regulations and controls, currency exchange operations, macro regulations, prudence, stress testing and national payment systems.
