Comment: Short-term changes caused by the effects of Kovid 19 will not change the trend of the Chinese economy.
BEIJING, May 16 (Xinhua) - A press conference of the National Bureau of Statistics on May 16 released key economic data for April. Affected by the tense and complicated international situation and the spread of 19 domestic Kovid, China's key economic index in April appeared to be declining.
A spokesman for China's National Bureau of Statistics said the move was "short-term" due to the impact of the 19 epidemic of Kovid, which would not change the trend of the Chinese economy. Do not change the characteristics of the Chinese economy, which has great resilience and potential and a wide development gap.
Maintaining the security, life and health of the people is a fundamental principle in the prevention and control of the 19 Chinese Kovid. While measures to prevent and control Kovid 19 will affect production and livelihoods in some areas, the reality is that only Kovid 19 can be controlled, which is a short-term problem. This can create favorable conditions for economic development.
That is why enterprises all over the world have been investing in China. From January to April this year, the actual use of foreign capital in China was 477.66 billion yuan, an increase of 20.5 percent over the same period in 2021.
What could be more convincing of foreign capital confidence in the Chinese economy than investment? It will not be able to change the steady flow of the Chinese economy, nor will it be able to shake China's commitment to expanding openness and mutual benefit and win-win with the world.
