Phnom Penh Governor Asks France to Help Build Another Wastewater Treatment Plant in Northwest Phnom Penh
(Phnom Penh): Phnom Penh Governor Khuon Sreng has asked France to help build another wastewater treatment plant in the northwest of Phnom Penh to improve the water environment before flowing into the Tonle Sap River.
Mr. Khuong Sreng made this request during a courtesy call and discussion with Mr. Zac Pele, Ambassador Extraordinary and Plenipotentiary of the French Republic to Cambodia on the afternoon of May 18, 2022. Phnom Penh Capital Hall.
Mr. Khuong Sreng said that Japan's JICA has helped many Cambodians, especially in Phnom Penh, by building several wastewater stations in Phnom Penh. In the northwest of Phnom Penh, there are no sewage stations yet. Therefore, he asked France to help Phnom Penh build this sewage station for the next generation to use. Whether in the form of a loan or a grant.
In addition, Mr. Khuong Sreng also asked the French side to help solve the problem of traffic congestion in Phnom Penh, because Phnom Penh has traffic jams every day.
Mr. Khuong Sreng also stated that for the French Embassy in the Kingdom of Cambodia, the Phnom Penh Capital Administration will help protect all security and order, and if the Embassy needs the Phnom Penh Capital Administration, the Phnom Penh Capital Administration will facilitate all the work required by the French Embassy. Also.
Mr. Khuong Sreng on that occasion also mentioned the situation of the Kingdom of Cambodia, stating that Cambodia went through the Pol Pot regime and after 1979 the country was at zero, but under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen. Make this poor country prosperous to this day.
Mr. Zac Pele on that occasion also expressed his deep appreciation for the development of Phnom Penh in recent years, with high-rise buildings with a maze of different from 1995.
He added that Cambodia is very busy with security arrangements as the Commune / Sangkat Council election is approaching on June 5. France will also hold elections on June 5. Therefore, he asked the Phnom Penh administration to help protect the security and order of the French people in Phnom Penh to vote.
