Ms. Soeur Socheata added that the directive is the participation of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports in implementing measures to ban the promotion, marketing and marketing of tobacco products, which are completely prohibited by the law on tobacco control.
In addition, Ms. Soeur Socheata claimed that this campaign is also a message to encourage young people to participate in preventing the intrusion of tobacco products in educational institutions, in any form.
Mr. Mom Kong stated that through the study of internal documents of the International Tobacco Company, the tobacco industry uses various program sponsorship strategies to: Establish relationships with individuals who have the authority to make policy decisions and build their reputation. Company. Tobacco companies also use subsidies to boost confidence, increase profits and hinder the implementation of health protection policies for the people.
