(Phnom Penh): The Federation of Education Services in Cambodia requests the state to continue tax incentives such as minimum tax exemption, income tax exemption and income tax due by the end of 2023 and request for extension of the provision Audit report from the Independent Accounting Commission to the tax administration two to three years after 2023.
In response to this request, the General Department of Taxation stated that the General Department of Taxation is a law enforcement agency that does not have the right to tax exemption, but is a key player in providing input for policy formulation related to this tax incentive.
The General Department of Taxation found that during the period when educational institutions received tax incentives through tax exemptions, educational institutions did not seem to be able to reduce the tuition fees of students.
The General Department of Taxation also said that by the end of 2023, enterprises will be required to pay annual income tax at the rate of 20% in case the profitable enterprise after tax regulation is larger than the minimum tax of 1% on annual turnover. .
In addition to the tax exemption request, the Federation of Education Services in Cambodia has requested an extension of the audit report from the Independent Accounting Commission to the Fiscal Administration for another two to three years after 2023, stating that it is not ready. Some educational institutions have businesses in the provinces and are small.
In this case, the General Department of Taxation urges all educational institutions to strengthen good governance, especially higher education institutions that provide professional training in skills such as accounting, finance or auditing, should not mention that there is no audit report.
At the same time, the General Department of Taxation requested all educational institutions to start implementing financial statements from now on and promised to send professional officers to explain and guide educational institutions that are really willing to prepare financial statements properly. To receive the audit report from the Independent Accounting Commission to submit to the General Department of Taxation after the end of 2023.
In response, the Federation of Education Services in Cambodia has recognized the importance of strengthening governance, as some institutions have in the past used audit reports to attract overseas investors and to obtain bank loans to expand their business.
According to the General Department of Taxation, according to the law, an enterprise must be registered with the Ministry of Commerce and must be taxed when there is economic activity from 15 days and have the obligation to declare tax every month. Authorized by the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports or the relevant institution in charge.
In the event that a government agency deems that a project should be tax-exempt, it will contact the Ministry of Economy and Finance to decide on the tax exemption, so the enterprise must apply for a license from the responsible ministry in order to apply for the tax exemption.
