The Minister made this call in his welcoming speech at the official launch of the US $ 150 million tourism co-financing and rehabilitation project on the evening of May 17, 2022, chaired by Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister. Minister of Economy and Finance, Chairman of the National Economic Policy Committee, Chairman of the National Committee for Tourism Development.
It should be informed that despite the gradual increase in tourism, the Minister said that as of March 31, 2022, there are 1,428 tourism businesses are still closed / suspended due to Cash flow problems and lack of financing for repairs and business operations.
That is why the Royal Government has paid close attention to the recovery of Cambodia's tourism sector by launching a $ 150 million co-financing program to restore and promote tourism with a concessional interest rate. Important and timely because tourism is still an important pillar in the development of the national economy and to help solve the difficulties of the tourism business.
The Minister strongly hopes that this co-financing project will facilitate new and medium-sized businesses (New Startup) in the tourism sector effectively, as he mentioned three important points such as starting a business. Improving and modernizing digital tourism services, expanding and diversifying tourism services to prepare for the return of national and international tourists.
The Minister called on the private sector in the tourism sector to participate in the implementation of this project actively, timely and effectively in response to the request of the recovery of tourism after the 19 crisis.
The minister also said that the number of international tourists, especially ASEAN domestic tourists, could increase further as health barriers and travel and transportation facilitation become easier.
According to Thong Khon estimates, in 2022, Cambodia will receive between 800,000 to 1 million international tourists and about 9 million domestic tourists.
