General knowledge: Which countries have the most exclusive economic zones in the world?
According to data from World Alas, the French Republic, which has many overseas territories, has the most exclusive economic zones in the world, followed by the United States and the United Kingdom. Australia.
* France The fact that France has the largest exclusive economic zone (EEZ) is due to the territorial administration of the former colonial power scattered across the oceans and on some continents.
Among those administrative territories and territories abroad, France provided more than 11,690,000 square kilometers of exclusive economic zone, accounting for about 8% of the world's total exclusive economic zone. The country's total land area is only 0.45% of the world's land area.
United States The United States has the second largest exclusive economic zone in the world, including the Caribbean, the Gulf of Mexico and three other oceans: the Pacific Ocean, the Atlantic Ocean, and the Arctic Ocean.
The US-occupied exclusive economic zone covers more than 11,350,000 square kilometers, accounting for about 7.77% of the world's total exclusive economic zone, of which Alaska is the largest. The largest of the United States, then Hawaii.
Australia Australia declared its exclusive economic zone on August 1, 1994, with an area of approximately 8,500,000 square kilometers.
