(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Cambodia, through the Ministry of Economy and Finance, has officially launched the "Tourism Co-financing Project for Tourism Restoration" in a budget of 150 million US dollars, a contribution between the Royal Government and participating financial institutions (PFIs). .
The official launch of the $ 150 million "Tourism Restoration Co-financing Project" was attended by Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Economy and Finance and Chairman of the National Committee for Tourism Development on the afternoon of the 17th. May 2022.
Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth said that this co-financing project is part of supporting the implementation of the strategic framework and programs to restore and promote Cambodia's economic growth in living with Kovid 19 in the new normal path 2021-2023 that the Royal Government Cambodia approved and officially launched on December 16, 2021.
He added that in the last decade under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, Cambodia's tourism sector has grown significantly with an average growth rate of about 12% per year of international tourists. The role is an important pillar for the Cambodian economy.
Between 2020 and 2021, tourism declined sharply due to the effects of the 19-year-old disease and caused many enterprises in the sector to reduce, suspend or close their businesses altogether, affecting tens of thousands of people. Loss of job and income.
Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth added that the US $ 150 million tourism co-financing project came from the Royal Government's contribution of US $ 75 million through the Cambodian Small and Medium Enterprise Bank and Contribution budget of participating financial institutions (PFIs) $ 75 million.
The scheme offers an interest rate of 6.5 per annum and a maximum loan of up to $ 400,000, which can be borrowed for up to seven years.
Please be informed that in 2020 and 2021, through the SME Bank mechanism, the Royal Government has already initiated and implemented two-step co-financing programs to support small and medium enterprises in the common priority areas. Including tourism affected by Kovid 19.
The first phase of the $ 100 million co-financing program.
The second phase has a total of $ 240 million to support small and medium enterprises to maintain business balance and create new jobs, as well as increase incomes for people in priority sectors, including tourism, which are affected by Crisis of Kovid 19
The two-step co-financing program has made a significant contribution to stabilizing business and creating new jobs as well as increasing people's incomes. In particular, the $ 150 million in tourism co-financing projects that will be launched at this time is focused on tourism alone to further strengthen the potential of tourism and contribute to the vision of the Royal Government in Develop the sector.
Minister of Tourism Thong Khon said that the Ministry of Tourism believes that the implementation of the $ 150 million tourism co-financing project will not only contribute to the rehabilitation of small and medium-sized businesses that are in need of repair financing. Location or quality of service can effectively support new small and medium enterprises in the tourism sector.
He called on the private sector in the tourism sector to participate in the successful implementation of this policy through the cooperation of the Bank for Small and Medium Enterprises of Cambodia and partner banks to use this financing project to rehabilitate the tourism sector and participate. Training human resources to strengthen tourism services to ensure the recovery of the second phase of tourism in 2022-2023.
