(Phnom Penh): An 84-year-old Cambodian-American woman released a video thanking the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, for donating her money and mask to Kantha Bopha Hospital to attend. Helping to save Cambodian children.
According to a video obtained by Fresh News, Do Preung, 84, now living in Lowell, Massachusetts, with her daughter, also thanked the team for allowing her to meet with Samdech Techo Hun Sen. In Washington, DC, USA recently.
In addition, she thanked Samdech Techo Hun Sen who fought to overthrow the genocidal regime of Pol Pot to help liberate her and her family and children have lived to this day.
It should be noted that in the spirit of loyalty and remembrance of the motherland, an 84-year-old Cambodian-American grandmother was encouraged to save $ 2,000 and cast 56 face masks by sending to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister. To Kantha Bopha Hospital to contribute to the cause of helping Cambodian children.
$ 2,000 and handmade masks of Mrs. Do Preung were handed over to the Kantha Bopha Children's Hospital in Phnom Penh on the morning of May 17, 2022.
Mrs. Do Preung has 6 children, 3 boys and 3 girls. She arrived in the United States in September 1980 as a refugee living in a refugee camp in Thailand.
Arriving in the United States, she lived in Virginia and moved to Lowell in 1989. She has been helping to take care of her children until now. She loved Samdech Techo very much, even though she was in a wheelchair, but she tried to stop him from meeting Samdech Techo and handed over this charitable gift to Samdech Techo so that he could donate to the humanitarian activities of Kantha Bopha Children's Hospital. .
