Cambodia participates in the 1st International Migration Forum at UN Headquarters in New York
The invitation to Cambodia is to share experiences on the implementation of the Convention on Safe, Legal and Legal Migration (GCM) at the first United Nations (UN) International Migration Governance Assessment Forum (IMR).
In particular, the Kingdom of Cambodia is included in the group of champion countries in the implementation of the World Covenant, Cambodia has implemented all the conditions and efforts to meet the priority objectives set by the World Covenant. On Safe, Tidy and Legal Migration (GCM) and participated in all the processes of preparation and implementation to achieve the goal of safe, orderly and legal migration.
Ms. Chou Bun Eng stated that migration remains a challenge that needs to be addressed collectively and effectively to ensure that migration is an option rather than a necessity.
Please be informed that the Global Covenant on Safe, orderly and legal migration (GCM) is the first comprehensive UN document adopted through intergovernmental dialogue to improve international cooperation in migration governance. Globally, it will be endorsed by the UN General Assembly, held on December 19, 2018 in New York, with 152 member countries.
The president-elect of the Philippines is the son of a former Philippine dictator who died in exile in the US state of Hawaii in 1989 after being ousted in a coup. Marcos Jr., 64, was elected the new president of the Philippines with nearly 59 percent of the vote last week and will be sworn in next month.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng Inaugurates $ 650,000 Water Forum and Other Artistic Buildings on the Lao Border in Chep District
(Preah Vihear): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, this morning, May 17, 2022, attended the official inauguration of the Water Forum and other art structures worth $ 65,000. Adjacent to the Lao border in Kampong Sralou commune, Chep district, Preah Vihear province.
On that occasion, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng thanked the authorities of Champasak Province of the Lao People's Democratic Republic for always maintaining good cooperation with Cambodia, especially the border provinces, always paying attention to cooperation to meet and resolve. Issues along the border are in line with the principles of the Royal Government as well as the Government of Laos and the principles of the Ministry of Interior and the Ministry of Security of the Lao PDR.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng strongly believes that the cooperative relations between our two countries, Cambodia and Laos, will continue to maintain the principles of border construction, friendship, peace, cooperation and development.
In particular, the Ministry of Interior and the Ministry of Security of the Republic of Laos have always adhered to the annual meeting regime, although Kovid has been disturbed, but we have found a way to meet through the video (Zoom) system to discuss the progress or the results. Of the annual cooperation and sign the cooperation of the next year without interruption.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng also thanked Mr. Vilayla Khamphoung, Minister of Security of the Republic of Laos, for his attention to qualify and strengthen cooperation between the two Ministries, especially in the fight against transnational crime. There is drug trafficking, especially synthetic drugs, which our Lao friends have tried to crack down on many cases, and Cambodia has cracked down on many cases.
As for the leaked case, which means smuggling from Laos to Cambodia, we also agreed that without cooperation, this synthetic drug would pose a serious threat to Laos as well as to Cambodia.
The provincial governor said that in addition to the construction of the Water Forum, there is also the construction of the banks of the Sangkha River, the construction of fences, gates, granite floors, gardens, the construction of residential buildings, the construction of boat huts, the construction of hermitage, the prayer on the left, five statues, and other decorations at a total cost. 2,603 million riels, equivalent to 65 thousand dollars.
