(Phnom Penh): Mr. Prach Chan, Chairman of the National Election Committee (NEC), informed the Ambassador of the European Union about the results of the 5th Commune / Sangkat Council Election 2022.
In which, the Chairman of the NEC highlighted the preparation of the 2021 voter list, which has more than 9.2 million voters, compared to the 18-year-old population on election day, as a percentage of 87.94%. . This is the result of the NEC preparing the voter list for the 5th Commune / Sangkat Council Election 2022.
Mr. Prach Chan, Chairman of the NEC, spoke about the general conduct of the National Election Committee, including the history of the election in Cambodia since 1993, organized by UNTAC, and then organized by the NEC in 1998. Myself, both general and non-universal elections have been held 17 times already. From one election to another, it was rated as better than previous elections.
The NEC Chairman also informed the EU side that 17 political parties have been recognized by the NEC in the official registration of candidates of political parties and now the NEC is ready. Prepare election equipment, which can generally be assessed as nearing completion, with little work to be done later.
The EU side raised issues related to the recruitment of election officials, the training of human resources, the delisting of candidates of a number of political parties, the work of NGOs, the election campaign forums of political parties, and the counting of ballots (p. 1102).
The Chairman of the NEC informed and answered all the questions of the EU side and which was assessed by the EU that the interpretation of the Chairman of the NEC is detailed and clear.
The European Union (EU) has requested that the NEC allow EU officials to observe the upcoming 2022 Commune / Sangkat elections, but not to register as an official election observer. The EU delegation requested permission from the NEC to observe the general election without conducting an assessment report on the atmosphere of the election process.
EU Ambassador Carmen Moreno hopes that the two sides, the EU and the NEC, will hold further meetings to strengthen cooperation in the field of elections in Cambodia.
Russey Keo District Police Inspector once again calls on the people of all 7 Sangkats to get the "A2" residence book, the "A4" family book and the free Khmer identity card
On the morning of May 17, 2022, Lt. Col. Heang Tharet, accompanied by Lt. Col. Thorn Then, Deputy District Inspector, Brigadier General Miech Noun, Chief of the 7 Police Stations and other relevant officials, continued to inspect and visit. Direct signature of "A2" residence book, "A4" family book and free Khmer identity card file in Tuol Thnang village, Sangkat Tuol Sangke II, in addition to providing to 6 other communes to the people.
According to Colonel Heang Tharet, the provision of "A2" residence book, "A4" family book and Khmer identity card, it is estimated that the number of people who have not yet done so is still large. Work will continue to provide housing for all families, such as Boreys and pagodas to all families for nearly 3 months from March 7 to May 17
In addition, Colonel Heang Tharet also appealed to work at the 7 Sangkat Administrative Police Stations where people live or to contact the Khan Police Inspectorate to meet the identification skills to ask for information and fill out forms. Provide "A2" residence book, "A4" family book and Khmer identity card.
Russey Keo District Police Inspector confirmed that the authorities could not provide immigrants with a residence permit, family book and Cambodian identity card. On the other hand, Mr. Athikar would like to apologize if there is any interruption by the service to the people who do not meet the actual needs due to some important reasons.
Please be informed that the family book, which was previously the responsibility of the Capital and Provincial Police Commission, must be dropped back to the district or Khan Police Inspectorate. Separately, the residence book that used to work at the district or khan police station must be dropped at the commune police station instead.
According to a 1997 sub-decree of the Royal Government of Cambodia, the Family Book is a reference book for identifying family members of Cambodian nationality and the family ties of each family, including spouses and adopted children. Every family that is a Cambodian citizen living in the territory of the Kingdom of Cambodia must have a family book.
The sub-decree states that every person who is the primary responsible person of each house, whether that person is the landlord or the tenant, is obliged to write in the residence book the name of everyone who lives permanently with him. Both books are also important identification documents to be used as testimonials in other necessary documents.
