Minister Prum Sokha: Implementing the policy of safe villages and communes helps to create local security as an important part of national social peace
(Chhlong-Kratie): Mr. Prum Sokha, Minister of Public Works and Chairman of Kratie Provincial Working Group, together with his colleagues, participated in a public forum to monitor the implementation of village-commune safety policy in Han Chey commune, Chhlong district, Kratie province.
After listening to the report of Mr. Tith Dimanche, Chief of Han Chey Commune, on the general situation of the implementation of the policy of safe villages and communes in Han Chey Commune, Minister Prum Sokha, Chairman of Kratie Provincial Working Group, opened the public forum, emphasizing the importance of The purpose of this forum is to understand the difficulties at the local level in order to jointly solve the challenges ahead in time for the benefit of the local people.
The Minister emphasized that "the implementation of the policy of safe villages and communes helps to create local security, which is an important part of national social peace."
On that occasion, the Minister thanked and commended the people in Han Chey commune who actively participated with the people all over the country to actively support the national movement under the noble and wise guide of Samdech Techo Hun Sen. The Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia in the fight to win Kovid-19 brought the society back to normal as it is today.
In the open program, the participants of the forum participated in discussing and solving local problems, which are concerns, some of which are directly related to the daily life of the people, including:
* Gambling and drug problems in the community
* Late issues in issuing documents or other documents to citizens, such as ID cards, land ownership documents
* Problems facilitating student traffic when entering and leaving school, etc.
These issues were explained, clarified and promised to be resolved by the Chief of Police, Commune Administration, District Land Officer, Commune Chief, Director of the Provincial Department of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction and other relevant authorities.
The Minister also encouraged working groups at all levels to continue to organize such forums in the villages and communes.
Closing remarks, Minister Prum Sokha, Chairman of Kratie Provincial Working Group, summarized the results of the public forum, which created an atmosphere of understanding and solidarity in Han Chey commune.
Cambodian People's Party (CPP) headquarters in Chamkar Andong commune, Chamkar Leu district, which cost more than 60,000 USD, was officially inaugurated.
(Kampong Cham): The CPP headquarters building, Chamkar Andong commune, Chamkar Leu district, Kampong Cham province, was officially inaugurated on May 15, 2022 under the presidency of Mr. HUN Manith, Member of the Central Committee of the Cambodian People's Party, Deputy Chairman of Kampong Cham Provincial Working Group and Chairman of the Cambodian People's Party Working Group in Chamkar Leu District.
