Rising domestic rice prices worry Thai rice exporters
BANGKOK: Thai rice exporters have expressed growing concern about the possibility of exporting rice in the second quarter of this year as a sharp rise in domestic rice prices could lead to rice importers. Involved in buying Thai rice. According to the Bangkok Post.
Rising domestic rice prices outpaced export prices, with port-to-port white rice rising just 15 percent from $ 400 a tonne to $ 460 a tonne over the same period.
Thailand has exported more than 200,000 tonnes of rice to Iraq since the beginning of the year, with the Thai Rice Exporters Association expecting the Middle East country to buy at least 400,000 tonnes, the Bangkok Post reported. In the year 2022.
