(Pich Chenda): On the morning of May 16, 2022, the Confucius Institute at the National University of Battambang and Pich Chenda High School co-organized a ceremony to award 106 first-class Chinese language certificates and launch a new second-generation course. 2 Presided over by Mr. Sok Khorn, Rector of National University of Battambang and Co-Chairman of the Board of Confucius Institute of National University of Battambang at Pich Chenda High School, Phnom Preuk District, Battambang Province.
The ceremony was also attended by Mr. Song Sopheak, Governor of Phnom Proek District, Battambang National University, Pich Chenda High School, community representatives, parents, teachers and students. The Chinese language class at Pich Chenda High School officially opened on February 21, 2022.
Mr. Pich Chhoeut, Principal of Pich Chenda High School, said: “As a former high school, as a model public service provider in the field of education throughout the country, I am very proud and pleased that the Confucius Institute at the University The nation of Battambang has cooperated in providing Chinese language training to students who wish to study the language in remote border areas.
He is optimistic that learning more Chinese will provide opportunities for young people with a deep knowledge of Chinese to pursue higher education and find better careers in the future. He also noted that both students and parents were very interested and supportive of the Chinese language training.
Prof. Dr. Yi Yongzhong, Co-Director of the Confucius Institute at the National University of Battambang, China, praised the students of Pich Chenda High School for their hard work, high confidence, good morals and strong interest in learning Chinese.
He also encouraged all the winning students to continue to learn more Chinese and instructed all parents to continue to support and encourage them to choose to learn Chinese to give them the opportunity to Continue to study through scholarships in the country and abroad and be able to find good jobs in the future.
He also thanked the co-director of the Confucius Institute, the principal of Pich Chenda High School and his colleagues for their hard work in opening this Chinese language class until it was fruitful today.
It should be reminded that the National University of Battambang and Pich Chenda High School have signed a Memorandum of Understanding on Cooperation in Chinese Language Training under the auspices of the Government of the People's Republic of China, exchange of study visits, especially the provision of life skills to students in the project Stem Partnership and the World Bank-funded Higher Education Improvement Project. Summary of important news events for May 16, 2022
