Speaking on the occasion of meeting with Samdech Techo's group of young volunteer doctors at the Chroy Changvar Gallery this morning, May 17, 2022, Samdech Techo Hun Sen said: "This is not a small matter, let the United States "Think carefully, if we consider violence in the form of assault with shoes, it is considered a right of expression, then in this world there will be no law and no law in Cambodia."
Regarding this case of violence, Samdech made it clear that he would not allow the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and the Cambodian Embassy in the United States to appoint an ambassador for the United States to take action against this person, but any action would depend on US law itself.
"If the United States considers this act of freedom of expression, perhaps it will happen in all countries, including Cambodia, then all Hun Sen's opponents are ready to wear shoes," he added. He said that his supporters knew who in Phnom Penh was allies with the shoemaker, which was not a threat but an analysis of the legal and political aspects.
However, he said that those NGOs, which they could sometimes accuse the Royal Government of Cambodia of inciting violence, were interpreting the legal aspects of politics.
Although the prince did not ask the United States to take action, if the United States punished him for attempting to commit violence, he could be deported to Cambodia after his conviction, as did other Cambodians. This person may be in danger if he arrives in Cambodia.
However, Samdech Techo Hun Sen does not believe that the United States does not take action, which Samdech concludes that the country may be investigating the case, but Samdech just explained to the public and reminded the US administration that he did not demand Punishment, but what the US law has to do is an American thing.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen reiterated that if the United States considers the case of throwing shoes at people as a right of expression, do not blame Cambodia if there is a similar case. Samdech also asked some NGOs to be careful in making wrong comments because in Cambodia, they are very angry and ready to explode.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen called on his supporters, both inside and outside the country, to remain calm while waiting for US action.
