Mr. Sou Socheat: Big companies in Cambodia like Chip Mong are looking at and ready to enter the securities market
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Sou Socheat, Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of the Securities Regulator of Cambodia, said that many large companies in Cambodia are looking for opportunities and ready to enter the securities market after seeing the profit. And the steady growth of the securities sector.
Mr. Sou Socheat made the remarks at the National Conference on the Cambodia Securities Exchange "A Decade of Development of the Cambodia Securities Market and its Way Forward" held on May 16, 2022.
Mr. Su Socheat said, "I think now that big companies have been looking at the stock market, a few months ago I just met with Chip Mong Bank about plans to join the securities sector. "Big companies are starting to look at the securities sector one by one because investing in the securities sector is a lucrative investment."
Mr. Hong Sohour, the Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of the Cambodia Securities Exchange, said that the Cambodia Securities Exchange expects that large companies in Cambodia will be able to enter the securities market in the future. Due to the small size of the stock market, the number of shares sold is still small and the one-time issue is just over $ 20 million.
Mr. Hong Sohour said that at present, the SET has 16 listed companies, 9 of which are listed as shares and 7 of which are listed as securities, and these 15 companies have raised about 1,122 B from the securities market. Million Riels ($ 281 million).
He stated that in 2021, due to the efficiency and intelligence of good situation management by the Royal Government of Cambodia has returned to the path of growth, with the trade volume increased to more than 1 billion riels ($ 270,000). And in the first four months of 2022, we achieved amazing results, with the trading volume increased to more than 4 billion riels ($ 1 million) per day due to the trading activity on ACLEDA shares.
