Ms. O Vandin Holds a Workshop on Law Enforcement in Combating Counterfeit and Substandard Medicines
(Kep): Dr. O Vandin, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health, opened a workshop on law enforcement related to the fight against counterfeit and substandard drugs to exchange experiences and strengthen the capacity of drug control officers to prevent, research and take action. Law on Combating Counterfeit and Substandard Medicines, which took place from 16 to 18 May 2022 at the Rock Royal Hotel, Kep Province.
In the current context, counterfeit and substandard medicines are a public health problem, both locally and globally. Currently, the Ministry of Health is promoting the sale of drugs online, which is a worrying issue for health effects, because some of those drugs are drugs with no clear source, not properly registered with the Ministry of Health and may be. Counterfeit or substandard medicines as well.
In order to participate in the fight against counterfeit and substandard medicines, the Ministry of Health has established drug control mechanisms in the Kingdom of Cambodia, such as:
* Require visas to register medicinal products in accordance with technical standards before allowing these products to be marketed and to educate the public not to use drugs without a visa number or registered by the Ministry of Health. Regularly distribute and sell drugs on the market. * Take legal action related to drug and cosmetic offenses.
