The recommendations of the Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth with remarks on the growth of the Cambodia Securities Exchange and the significant progress over the past 10 years include:
First, continue to increase the dissemination through new mechanisms and means of technology about the benefits that the Royal Government of Cambodia has been providing to listed companies, especially tax incentives for the securities sector and favors. Tax liabilities for companies that issue and list public securities.
Third, to organize with all relevant actors of the securities market detailed activities in the context of the current global economic situation as well as the rapid development of this financial technology for the development of the securities market for the next 10 years through the preparation and The launch of a 10-year strategic plan for the development of the securities sector, which I have already introduced to the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia, to lead this work.
According to Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth, according to economic theory, the securities sector can contribute to the development of the national economy by increasing the efficiency of mobilizing and allocating capital from economic agents with financing capacity (meaning the ability to save money) to economic agents. With financing requirements.
The securities sector in Cambodia is supposed to have started with the introduction of the Law on the Issuance and Trading of Public Securities in 2007 and the launch of the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia in 2008 and its players. Subsequent securities.
Separately, the Cambodia Securities Exchange was established as a joint venture between the Royal Government of Cambodia, represented by the Ministry of Economy and Finance, and the Korea Securities Exchange in 2010 and launched its first securities trading on April 18, 2012. With the listing of securities trading of a number of public enterprises, the Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority.
He said that in order to develop the securities sector, the Royal Government of Cambodia, with the Ministry of Economy as its staff, always pays attention to supporting this sector through tax incentives for issuers and investors to pay attention to protection. The public interest and the preparation of regulations that are conducive to securities activities.
Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth emphasized that the Royal Government will continue to pay attention to this as well as consider additional mechanisms so that this market can fulfill its role in attracting capital and promoting investment in the wider national economic activities. And more efficient.
According to Mr. Hong Sohour, the Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of the Cambodia Securities Exchange, the Securities Exchange has 16 listed companies, nine of which are listed as shareholders and seven are listed as bonds, and these 15 companies have raised capital from The securities market is about 1,122 billion riels ($ 281 million).
The Cambodian diplomat made the request during a bilateral meeting with US Secretary of State Anthony Blinken during the ASEAN-US Special Summit on 13 May 2022 in Washington DC. .
"The Deputy Prime Minister requested that the United States reconsider the unjust visa restrictions regarding the repatriation of Cambodian-American citizens, assuring their US counterparts of cooperation," the State Department said in a statement. Cambodia's full on this process.
Regarding bilateral relations, Deputy Prime Ministers Prak Sokhon and Bling Ken noted with satisfaction the good cooperation between Cambodia and the United States in many areas, such as increased economic, health, education, demining and demining. Counter-terrorism, peacekeeping, protection of cultural heritage, the search for the remains of American soldiers lost in the war and captivity, and the transformation of people and people.
The Deputy Prime Minister highlighted that trade is an example of the best positive cooperation between the two countries and expressed the hope that the Generalized System of Preferences (GSP) for Cambodia will be renewed to Further support for economic development and Cambodian workers in the garment and footwear sector, mostly women.
The Deputy Prime Minister also reiterated Cambodia's gratitude to the United States for continuing to support Cambodia's development in many areas, most recently the fight against Kovid-19. Anthony Blinken expressed the United States' readiness to further support Cambodia's development and to work actively with Cambodia to enhance political, security, economic and socio-cultural cooperation.
The two Foreign Ministers expressed their joint commitment to work more closely to promote friendly relations and fruitful cooperation between Cambodia and the United States in all fields.
In 2017, the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, announced that the agreement between Cambodia and the United States regarding the repatriation of illegal Cambodians will continue without repeal, but the Cambodian side will request that Re-amendment for humanitarian and human rights reasons. Samdech Techo Hun Sen expects the United States to understand this issue as a humanitarian and human rights principle.
In addition, on the morning of May 12, 2022, during a meeting with more than 2,000 Cambodians living in the United States and Canada, Samdech Techo Hun Sen reiterated this, stating that it was a tragedy. The Cambodian people who are sent back to Cambodia will be separated from their families, wives and children. Samdech continued that there are still more than 100 Cambodian citizens who violated the law to be sent back.
