(Phnom Penh): The General Department of Prisons of the Ministry of Interior has come out to clarify the case of the dissemination and distribution of videos in which many detainees play mobile phones in Pailin Provincial Prison in exchange for a monthly payment of $ 500 to $ 1,000. Prison Chief and Prison Officer.
In this case, the General Department of Prisons of the Ministry of Interior confirmed that after carefully examining three video clips that have been posted and shared on some social media sites recently, General The Department of Prisons of the Ministry of Interior took immediate action and requested the following public comment:
* All 3 videos were actually taken from Pailin Provincial Prison by a group of detainees, but it is an old case where the General Department of Prisons has taken administrative action against the relevant officials and has already applied discipline to the detainees involved. In accordance with the prison regulations in force
* The incident happened before the 2nd General Superintendent Roth Ty took over as the director of Pailin Provincial Prison, but was posted by a small group of opportunists in order to attack the windows of honor of the leadership as well as the unit. Pailin Provincial Prison
In order to ensure the full implementation of internal regulations, procedures and laws on prisons aimed at improving work efficiency and eliminating inactivity among officials, the General Department of Prisons will continue to monitor the development of the situation in Pailin Provincial Prison through monitoring and evaluation. And inspect as well as promote some necessary measures on stakeholders
Please be informed that this issue has already been addressed by the General Department of Prisons and will continue to monitor the progress of the situation, and also would like to remind some individuals who are in the process of posting and distributing false information that causes damage to honor as well as dignity. Of entities or public individuals may face the law on the media, as well as criminal offenses, defamation or incitement to commit crimes, etc.
