Mr. Ley Sopheap mentioned the Royal Government's attention to the network marketing business through the adoption of the e-commerce law and the consumer protection law to support the network marketing business in Cambodia to promote and Protect legitimate businesses, prevent illegal businesses.
"After the reopening of the country by the Royal Government, even though the members of the association are less capable, as long as there is solidarity and close cooperation, the possibility of successful business still has a chance to grow," he said. "More."
He went on to advise network marketers to have an in-depth understanding of recognized businesses in order to operate legally and to attract people to participate in their business with confidence and equality. All bases.
Mr. Ley Sopheap did not forget to call on each company to have a clear sales-purchase policy to monitor the progress of their business. Not only that, there must be a policy to develop human resources, both business and technical skills, especially to be diligent to meet together to exchange experiences from each other and cooperate to move people to have more support and stronger.
In addition, he urged members and companies to have internal discipline. He gave an example that if there is a problem or mistake, please do not argue to find the right, you must look at the institution or the company as a whole, not just the individual who made the mistake, because A prosperous institution always comes from the efforts of internal unity.
