(Phnom Penh): Mr. Hong So Hour, the Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of the Cambodia Securities Exchange, said that the growth of the securities sector will encourage Cambodian private companies to grow through the acquisition of large capital to expand business as planned. Their business.
Although these companies grew before they were listed on the stock exchange, they could not raise billions of dollars from investors to become companies if they did not have a stock exchange and no stock exchange. For investors to sell shares to withdraw and make a profit.
Mr. Hong Sohour made this statement at the National Conference on the Cambodia Securities Exchange "A Decade of Development of the Cambodia Securities Market and its Way Forward" on May 16, 2022.
"If you want to have companies in Cambodia that grow as fast as others, please join us to grow our securities market like them," he said. Please join so that potential companies can raise capital to use according to their qualifications, please join so that Cambodian companies can compete with foreign companies in Cambodia or abroad.
He said that the securities sector in Cambodia is growing, with the participation of all parties to create a common dream is to create a securities market with a trading volume of $ 50 million per day for the next 6 to 7 years. In order for listed companies to be able to sell hundreds of millions of dollars in stocks and make a profit on the stock market.
Please be informed that currently, the Cambodia Securities Exchange has 16 listed companies, of which 9 companies are listed as shares and 7 are listed as securities, and these companies have raised about 1.122 billion Riels from the securities market. Or about $ 281 million.
