Ministry of Environment, WCS and related partners Joint Press Release on Zero Trap Campaign in Preah Vihear Province
(Preah Vihear): WCS has partnered with the Ministry of Environment, Preah Vihear Provincial Department of Environment, Preah Vihear Provincial Administration, Prey Lang Baitong Project and the International Conservation Organization (CI) to launch a zero-trap campaign in Preah Vihear to eliminate all types of traps in protected areas. All over Cambodia.
The Zero Trap Campaign was launched in Preah Vihear Province, the second destination after Stung Treng Province, which was held on 16 May 2022 in the Thmat Bei Thoeun Krasang Ecotourism Community in the Kulen-Prohm Tep Wildlife Sanctuary. Choam Ksan, Preah Vihear Province, chaired by Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment, with the participation of Preah Vihear Provincial Administration, district authorities, partner organizations and community members.
This is the third of eight "Zero Trap" campaigns, the first organized by the Ministry of Environment in Phnom Penh on March 3 and the second by Stung Treng, organized by WWF in collaboration with the Department. Environment of Stung Treng province, CI, WEA and Prey Lang Baitong project in early April.
The Zero Trap Campaign calls for the implementation of urgent measures to enhance law enforcement and review relevant regulations in order to prevent illegal wildlife hunting and end the trap crisis that is threatening Cambodia's wildlife. Louder.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra emphasized: “From the people in the village to the delivery service providers, the food vendors in the market in the city and town to the restaurant owners and customers, the participation of the people in the community plays an important role in "Safe for the survival of all species of wildlife in their natural forest habitats and in participating in stopping the use and trapping of wildlife sanctuaries."
The Ministry of Environment calls on all people to stop eating wild animals or buy other wildlife products.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra appealed: "We strongly urge all people in Cambodia to say no to wildlife and participate in the conservation of natural resources of the Kingdom of Cambodia to be sustainable."
Dr. Ken Serey Ratha, Director of WCS, said: “Preventing trapping activities in Cambodia will not be successful without the participation of the public. "This campaign is an effective mechanism for all of us to spread the message to the public to stop the use of wildlife products in a timely manner."
Dr. Serey Ratha added, "WCS urges all stakeholders to comply with this call, both those who create demand for wildlife products and those who trade in wildlife meat." Wildlife is an important part of the ecosystem. "Your participation today will ensure the survival of wildlife in the future."
The next campaign will be held in Kratie, Mondulkiri, Kampong Thom, Ratanakkiri and end in Phnom Penh.
