Mr. Neth Pheaktra: More effective protection and conservation of wildlife biodiversity will greatly benefit local people
(Preah Vihear): Mr. Net Pheaktra, Secretary of State and Spokesperson of the Ministry of Environment, emphasized that the more effective protection and conservation of wildlife biodiversity will greatly benefit the ecosystem and help the livelihood of local people through Make money from eco-tourism.
On that occasion, the Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment said that every day our precious wildlife is killed because hunters use all kinds of traps and processed bullets to be used as food for families and for sale on Market to those who like to eat wild meat.
Dr. Ken Serey Ratha, Director of WCS, said: "Preventing trapping activities in Cambodia will not be successful without public participation. "This campaign is an effective mechanism for all of us to spread the message to the public to stop the use of wildlife products in a timely manner."
It should be noted that the Zero Trap campaign, which is planned to be held in 6 provinces in 6 months, will continue in Kratie, Mondulkiri, Kampong Thom, Ratanakkiri and end in Phnom Penh in October 2022.
