The lunar eclipse can be seen in parts of Europe, Africa and the Americas, while the entire South American region can be observed from beginning to end. A lunar eclipse occurs when the earth is between the sun and the moon, with our planet blocking the sun's light and casting a shadow over the moon's surface.
