Cambodia Exports Cambodian Food and Products in Sihanoukville to Promote Coastal Tourism Potential
(Preah Sihanouk): Cambodia organized an exhibition of Khmer food and products in Sihanoukville from May 13-15, 2022 under the theme "Support Khmer food, preserve national culture" in order to promote and promote traditional Khmer food. In particular, coastal food promotes progress and tourism potential.
The exhibition also aims to strengthen cooperation between the public and private sectors to promote and attract tourists to Sihanoukville.
The exhibition of Khmer food and products was attended by tour operators, restaurants, canteens, food vendors at 139 booths, including 17 coastal tourism association booths, 51 instant food booths, 21 hotels, restaurants and ice cream stalls. And 8 Khmer cakes, 6 drinks, tea, coffee, 5 fresh fruits, 3 souvenirs and 28 local products.
Acting Minister Tith Chantha said that the exhibition of food and Khmer products is a contribution to promote traditional Khmer food and tourism potential of the coastal area, especially tourism in Sihanoukville really contributes to promote socio-economic development, environmental protection And the well-being of the people in Sihanoukville.
On the morning of the 14th, the event organized a cooking and drinking competition and knowledge on tourism, environment, prevention of Kovid-19 with the participation of students from 5 universities, Faculty of Law and Economics, Don Bosco Vocational Training School, National University of Management, Mekong University And Build Bright University. For the food and beverage competition, the winners will be selected from 1st to 3rd place with a trophy and a prize money of $ 1,000 and then $ 300.
On the morning of the 15th, a friendly cycling race under the theme "Improving the environment and public hygiene to participate in the Clean City-Clean Beach Campaign" 15 km along the coast with 146 participants.
