BEIJING (Reuters) - The US Federal Reserve recently announced a 0.5 percent rate hike and will begin cutting its balance sheet in June in response to record-breaking inflation. Over the past 40 years, through the monetary tightening policy. This has caused general concern in the international community and the global economy and financial markets will face another attack.
Whether zero interest rates and QE policies have caused commodity prices to rise sharply in the past or now tight monetary policy, the United States has turned the crisis around the world through its dollar hegemony. All of this has had a profound effect on the world's emerging economies, which are struggling to make ends meet after the end of Kovid 19.
As the largest economy in the world, as long as the US economy slows, it will also pose a significant risk. This is a risk that the whole world must prevent at all times.
Interestingly, as the US economy slumped, some Washington politicians did not take into account their negligence in responding to the crisis, but rather played a role. Old games of blaming to divert conflict to the outside. This is irresponsible to the American people and irresponsible to the world.
Those Washington politicians who insist on pursuing "America as a priority" should put an end to their illusions, turn the crisis around and blame arbitrarily, as well as pursue more responsible macroeconomic policies. Urge them to take concrete measures to help the global economy recover from the Kovid 19 outbreak soon.
President of the Cambodian Pharmacists Association calls on health workers to be hospitable to patients to avoid emotional distress
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Ley Sopheap, President of the Cambodian Federation of Medical, Pharmacological and Dental Associations and President of the Cambodian Pharmaceutical Sellers Association, introduced a number of good tips to its members to help professionals practice medicine together. To serve the people, especially to be hospitable to the people, to avoid hurting the patient's mind.
Mr. Ley Sopheap said this during the handing over ceremony of basic certificates for pharmacists in pharmacies, which are about 500 members of the Cambodian Pharmacists Association on the morning of May 15, 2022.
On that occasion, the President said that in each province began to see the value of education in the field of medicine. For the Cambodian Pharmacists Association, training is always provided and the winners are awarded to the trainees as well as the general health service providers to confirm their education, training and skills. He said that these certificates are equivalent to legal documents.
He said that the above training will give trainees who are drug sellers to understand the external and internal health effects of consumers, the legitimacy of the products they sell to consumers.
He suggested that pharmacists, nurses, doctors, midwives, doctors, assistants, doctors, cosmetics sellers, general staff, etc. must go through education and vocational training.
He called on all stakeholders, especially pharmacists in pharmacies, sellers of cosmetics, food and beverages, to come and receive training with the Cambodian Pharmaceutical Federation Association to ensure proper use, safe distribution and health to understand the law. Management. Be aware of good health care. Must serve the people with love, should think about time, time.
He went on to suggest that members must be hospitable to patients because patients are already very anxious and need to take care of the people who come to receive health services. These tasks are necessary as a health care provider for the people.
Mr. Ley Sopheap continued to call on members to work closely with local authorities at all levels on cooperation to serve the people.
He further suggested that the sale of medicines to the people must be regulated after obtaining this certificate. There must be financial management, income-expenditure plan, because if the service provider is poor, providing services to consumers is also difficult, that is, there must be a decent standard of living.
