He thanked the party's observers for their past efforts and urged all observers to be more active in fulfilling their roles as they are an important part. For the party. Preah Vihear is the second destination after Stung Treng in organizing zero trapping campaigns in protected areas
(Preah Vihear): Preah Vihear Province is the second destination after Stung Treng Province in organizing the Zero Trap Campaign in the Cambodian Nature Reserve, which was initiated and led by the Ministry of Environment and with the participation of various conservation partner organizations.
Mr. Pheaktra said that Cambodia's wildlife resources are at high risk due to the ongoing hunting and trapping crisis caused by the illegal use and trafficking of wildlife. To address this crisis, relevant government agencies and international partners in the field of environment came together today to launch a zero-trapping campaign in Cambodia's protected areas.
The main goal of this campaign is to eliminate the use of all kinds of traps in Cambodia's protected areas. In 2021, the Ministry of Environment and its partner organizations removed a total of 61,611 traps from 72 protected areas and other biodiversity corridors in Cambodia. On average, a total of more than 40,000 traps are removed from these protected areas each year.
Secretary of State for the Ministry of Environment calls on all people to stop eating wild animals and buy products from other wildlife.
At the same time, "Mr. Net Pheaktra called on the authorities at all levels to participate in preventing and cracking down on the crime of trapping, hunting and collecting all kinds of wildlife eggs and the crime of trafficking in wildlife and wildlife samples to participate. Protect and conserve wildlife and biodiversity of all kinds to survive and thrive for generations to come. Open letter: "Candlelight Party policy completely copied from CPP"
(Phnom Penh): The seven-point policy of the Candlelight Party, which Mr. Son Chhay, the former spy agency of Prime Minister Hun Sen, announced in its congress on Sunday morning, May 15, is nothing new, that is, the principle The CPP-led government has long pursued a policy. Practical:
* Point 1: On the authority: Allowing people to participate in giving opinions to commune councils is a policy that the government led by the Cambodian People's Party has implemented for many mandates. Citizens have the right to attend or be invited to Commune / Sangkat Council meetings or to participate in public forums organized by national and commune officials to listen to the decisions of local authorities and to provide input to councils.
* Point 3: On security: No drugs, no evil deeds. The commune safety policy, which has been announced for many years, aims to make the commune safe and free from drugs and mischief. However, the drug problem is a global challenge that no country can completely eradicate, including the great powers.
* Point 4: Protecting land ownership and improving the lives of the people is the main priority of the CPP government. After leaving the Khmer Rouge regime, the Khmer people had no private property, including land ownership. But it was Prime Minister Hun Sen who led the reform of private ownership and land ownership until now.
And when it comes to improving people's lives, no one can do it like the CPP. From bare hands, no shoes, no bicycles to the Cambodian people have been living in abundance, traffic jams on the road like today is the work of the Cambodian People's Party.
Speaking of mutual funds, there are almost all institutions. As for the poor people, they always get the help from the authorities, the Cambodian Red Cross and the local relief team, the volunteer doctors, etc.
* Point 6: Free Medical Cards: The CPP government has long implemented the provision of equity cards to the poor and the issuance of "BOSS" cards to private sector employees and Civil servants, armed forces, teachers to receive free medical treatment. In addition, there is also a group of volunteer doctors to treat people for free to the local.
* Point 7: On the same opportunity for education, the government of the Cambodian People's Party has long launched under the slogan "Education for all, all for education". Education reform is also achieving satisfactory results and is welcomed by people from all walks of life.
In summary, the seven points of the Candlelight Party's policies are completely copied from the policies of the CPP, that is, the Candlelight Party does not have the human resources to write new ideas to campaign. This is why many activists and candidates and reserve candidates for the commune council elections of the Candlelight Party have left the party and returned to live with the CPP.
