Minister Lim Kean Hor Continues to Inspect Irrigation Systems in Battambang and Banteay Meanchey Provinces
(Battambang): On May 15, 2022, which is the second day of the mission to inspect the water situation in the Northwest Zone at the beginning of the 2022 rainy season, Mr. Lim Kean Hor, Minister of Water Resources and Meteorology, accompanied by leaders. The Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology of Battambang and Banteay Chey Provinces, as well as technical officers, inspected a number of irrigation systems in Battambang and Banteay Meanchey provinces.
This mission has three main objectives, including:
* Second: Introduce techniques to improve the shortcomings in the construction of modernization projects on the Kamping Puoy Basin Irrigation System in Banan District, Battambang Province, which is actively promoting the construction work. So far, pepper has reached about 80% of the plan.
* Third: Inspected the situation of flooding of farmers' fields in Rohat Teuk commune, Mongkul Borei district, Banteay Meanchey province, which was recently flooded due to excessive rainfall from Malai district.
The Minister immediately ordered the use of heavy machinery to cut off the canal, which has been rehabilitated and widened, but has not yet been cut off due to the heavy rains. Immediately open the waterfront to loosen the waterfall down towards the Tonle Sap Lake. Samdech Techo Hun Sen Leads a Delegation to Return to Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, led a delegation to return to Cambodia at 7:45 pm on May 15, 2022, after successfully completing his mission in the United States. And full of ultimate honor.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen led a delegation to Washington, DC, on May 10 at the invitation of US President Joe Biden to attend the ASEAN-US Special Summit to celebrate the 45th anniversary of relations. ASEAN-US Dialogue Partners.
During his mission in the United States, in addition to co-chairing the ASEAN-US Special Summit with the US President, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also attended the ASEAN-US Business Forum and led ASEAN leaders to attend. With US Vice President Kamala Harris and discuss work as a US Congressman.
In addition, Samdech Techo also met with the Prime Minister of Vietnam and met with the leaders of some US companies.
During this mission in the United States, Samdech Techo also met with about 2,000 Cambodians in the United States and Canada.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen's current mission in the United States has been noted to bring significant fruitful results for the ASEAN framework in improving ASEAN-US relations.
In addition, Samdech Techo's current mission in the United States is also seen as a fruitful result in the improvement of bilateral relations between Cambodia and the United States. His Majesty's presence in the United States is also seen as the proudest and most honorable for the entire Cambodian nation.
