Duke Kith Meng invites US Chamber of Commerce delegation to visit Cambodia and encourages US companies to set up factory in Cambodia
(US): Taking the opportunity to accompany Samdech Techo Hun Sen to the ASEAN-US Summit, Duke Kith Meng, President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce and Chairman of the ASEAN Business Advisory Council 2022, met with Mr. John Goy. On the afternoon of May 13, 2022 in Washington, USA, we are the CEO of the American Chamber of Commerce for Southeast Asia.
Discussions focused on cooperation between the two chambers of commerce and the promotion of US-Cambodian business and investment.
Neak Oknha Kith Meng, President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce and Chairman of the ASEAN Business Advisory Council 2022, briefed John Goyer on the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce's business visit to the United States and business meetings with US companies.
On that occasion, Duke Kith Meng requested the American Chamber of Commerce to consider the possibility of signing a memorandum of understanding between the two chambers, inviting the US Chamber of Commerce to organize regular business visits to Cambodia and from Cambodia to the United States. Duke Kith Meng asks the US Chamber of Commerce to cooperate and support the organization of the ASEAN Business and Investment Summit to be held in November.
In addition, Duke Kith Meng proposed joint activities between the two chambers of commerce to promote business and investment between the two countries to be stronger and more prosperous. The duke invited a US Chamber of Commerce delegation to visit Cambodia and encouraged US companies to set up factories in Cambodia that could export their products to the world market or the US market at lower tariffs under the FTA. Multilateral and bilateral.
Mr. John Goyer welcomed the remarks made by Duke Kith Meng and stated that the United States intends to diversify its production in ASEAN countries and that Cambodia is an important destination not only for lower costs but also for More high quality.
He said that therefore, Cambodian enterprises should strengthen their capacity to be able to connect to the high value-added chain. The US Chamber of Commerce will examine the possibility of signing a memorandum of understanding with the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce to help boost economic ties between the two countries. Have to say no to drugs! Nationwide drug crackdown on May 15: 22 cases cracked, 47 arrested
