ASEAN chair urges resumption of comprehensive political dialogue on Ukraine-Russia crisis to end hostilities and restore peace
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and chair of ASEAN in 2022, called for the resumption of comprehensive political dialogue on the Ukraine-Russia crisis to end hostilities and restore peace.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen's remarks were made on the occasion of the ASEAN-US Special Summit to be held in Washington DC on May 12-13, 2022, with Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and Jo US President Biden serves as co-chair of the meeting.
A statement from the Cambodian Ministry of Foreign Affairs on the outcome of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's working visit to attend the ASEAN-US Special Summit in Washington stated that: "Regarding regional and international issues, Samdech Techo "Cambodia's position is relevant to the Ukraine-Russia crisis and urges the resumption of a comprehensive political dialogue to end hostilities and restore peace."
The Royal Government of Cambodia has also expressed its full support for the Secretary-General's efforts to resolve the humanitarian crisis and to find a peaceful solution to the conflict. This is according to the additional confirmation of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs.
In the past, the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia has declared his strong opposition to any country that uses military force to invade other countries.
The United Nations on March 2 convened an emergency assembly to vote on a resolution condemning and demanding that Russia withdraw its troops from Ukraine. Of the 141 member states, five voted against the resolution, while 35 voted against.
Cambodia is among the 141 countries that support the resolution and is also a co-founder of the UN General Assembly Resolutions Special Session on the Situation in Ukraine.
In this regard, the United States Government expresses its appreciation and gratitude to the Royal Government of Cambodia for its support of the recent United Nations General Assembly Resolution on Ukraine.
Spokesman of the Ministry of Justice clarifies two points in the case of Mr. Kem Sokha after misleading interpretation of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's speech
(Phnom Penh): Chin Malin, spokesman for the Ministry of Justice, confirmed that the Cambodian court continued to charge Kem Sokha with "conspiracy with a foreign state" but did not charge any foreign state in the case.
The reaffirmation of the spokesperson of the Ministry of Justice of Cambodia comes after a misinterpretation of the speech of the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen in the United States recently, which Kem Sokha's lawyer tried to pull. Foreign states to appear in this case, or say that if not charged, the court will end the case of Mr. Kem Sokha as soon as possible.
Recently, Mr. Sokha's lawyers asked the court to summon foreign ambassadors for a hearing on Mr. Sokha's peace deal with a foreign state. Jean Malin considers this to be a ploy by the accused to push a foreign state into the case with him and use a foreigner to get him out of this criminal case or from the court proceedings through Foreigners exert pressure on Cambodia.
He asserted that the latest case, as described in the past, would not affect the court's proceedings as long as the court already had solid evidence in the case.
