ASEAN-US leaders vow to strengthen ties to become indispensable
(Washington, USA): As planned, on May 13, 2022, the ASEAN-US Supreme Leader, led by Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen and chair of ASEAN, and US President Joe Biden opened the summit. In particular, to discuss strengthening relations and launching cooperation to strengthen ASEAN-US relations to become stronger and stronger.
The Special Summit was held at the US State Department in Washington, D.C., with the release of the Joint Statement on the Joint Vision of the ASEAN-US Special Summit.
On the occasion of the 45th anniversary of the ASEAN-US Dialogue Partnership in 2022, the leaders of ASEAN and the United States are committed to jointly strengthening joint efforts to establish a comprehensive ASEAN-US strategic partnership. By meaning, content and mutual benefit and create a new era in ASEAN-US relations.
In support of sub-regional development, all leaders continued to support ASEAN's achievement and ASEAN unity in promoting ASEAN sub-regional development. In particular, further commitment to promoting stability, peace and prosperity and sustainable development in the Mekong subregion through initiatives under the Mekong-US Partnership Framework.
The use of technology and the promotion of innovation ASEAN-US leaders have pushed for greater cooperation in the fields of biotechnology, smart agriculture, climate resilient agriculture, food science, meteorology, microelectronics, marine science, energy and space.
On tackling climate change, ASEAN-US leaders emphasized the need to strengthen partnerships to strengthen ASEAN's capacity for resilience to disasters and adaptation to the effects of climate change, such as climate change. Rising sea levels, more frequent floods, droughts and other severe weather events increase the risk of water, energy and food insecurity and devastating storms.
On maintaining peace and building trust, ASEAN-US leaders reaffirmed the responsibility of all parties to uphold the principles of mutual respect for the sovereignty, territorial integrity and equal rights of all nations.
With the rapidly evolving momentum towards common interests, Samdech Techo invited US President Joe Biden to attend the 10th ASEAN-US Summit to be held in Cambodia in November. .
