Top Cambodian officials meet US lawmakers to seek investment opportunities and boost trade
(Washington, USA): Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, and Minister of Commerce Pan Sosak met with US Congressmen to explore opportunities for expanding investment and promoting trade between Cambodia and the United States. Even better.
The Senior Minister briefed the two US lawmakers on Cambodia's progress, progress and development potential of the transport, port and logistics infrastructure. In particular, Mr. Pan Sosak mentioned the current investment and trade environment related to industry, mining, energy and oil, as well as the garment sector, especially the Cambodian Investment Law, which is one of the best open in Asia.
At the same time, Ron Estes mentioned the technology of aircraft production, automobiles and other manufacturing industries for export. Carol Miller focused on the energy industry, such as coal, oil and gas, with the main purpose of strengthening trade and investment cooperation to boost trade between the two countries. More.
