For 5 days, the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia cracked down on 16 duty-free luxury cars nationwide
(Phnom Penh): For 5 days from 9 to 13 May 2022, the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia cracked down on 16 duty-free luxury cars throughout the country, all of which took refuge under fake license plates. .
The 16 vehicles that the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia seized during this week include:
The last deadline of the existing car tax collection campaign in the country is June 30, 2022, and from July 1, 2022 onwards, the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia is not eligible to pay vehicle tax. Already in that country, the main role is to crack down.
In the event that the duty-free vehicle is cracked down after June 30, 2022, the left-hand drive vehicle will have to pay taxes according to the law in force and pay more fines. Right-hand drive vehicles, when suppressed, will be disassembled and converted into car parts, as right-hand drive vehicles are banned from importing for domestic use and can be destroyed.
Mr. Kun Nhim also called on car owners who have not yet brought their cars to pay taxes, please hurry to fulfill their tax obligations by June 30, 2022, with less than 60 days left. No.
Please be informed that from September to December 31, 2021, the Royal Government of Cambodia, through the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia, has allowed left-hand drive tax-free vehicles to pay taxes with a 10% tax preference. Right-hand drive vehicles (corrected after paying the tax) receive a 10% tax preference until June 30, 2022.
(Battambang): The time of the 5th Commune / Sangkat Council Election is approaching, the movement of the Commune / Sangkat Council candidate of the Candlelight Party has decided to change its political position and walk away from this opposition party to surrender with The Cambodian People's Party.
On May 13, 2022, seven commune council candidates of the Candlelight Party in Thmor Koul district, Battambang province, decided to leave the Pleung Tean Party and return to live with the Cambodian People's Party. In addition to the seven commune council candidates, 145 other leaders and activists of the Candlelight Party have decided to leave the Candlelight Party to engage in political activities with the CPP.
The team of Mr. Mearly Samet, Advisor to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian People's Party, met and welcomed the presence of the 152 candidates of the Commune Council, leaders and activists of the Candlelight Party.
Mr. You Serey Vuth, Representative of Duke Ly Samet, warmly welcomed the presence of Commune Council candidates, leaders and activists of the Candlelight Party in Thmor Koul District.
Mr. You Sereyvuth considered that the decision of the candidates, leaders and activists of the Candlelight Party is the most correct decision to participate in activities to serve the nation and the people of Cambodia. In particular, take action to win the Commune / Sangkat Council Election on June 5, 2022.
