(Siem Reap): 550 former members of the National Rescue Party and candlelight vigils from various districts in Siem Reap City, Siem Reap Province have decided to join the Cambodian People's Party.
Speaking at the New Member Recruitment Ceremony on the morning of May 13, 2022 at the Cambodian People's Party (CPP) in Siem Reap, Duke Ly Samet called the personal adviser of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian People's Party (CPP). Samdech Techo Hun Sen and warmly welcomed the presence of new members in Siem Reap.
He added that the presence of these 550 new members from the former opposition party in Cambodia as a new driving force and a new support force for the CPP to continue to move forward vigorously towards victory in the council elections. Commune / Sangkat on June 5, 2022, as well as the National Assembly election in 2023.
Mr. Ly Samet thanked all the new members who gave the truth about the merits of the Cambodian People's Party under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, as well as all the leaders and members of the nation and people. In the past.
Mr. Tea Seiha, President of the Cambodian People's Party in Siem Reap, expressed his happiness to see the decision of the former members of the former National Rescue Party and the Candlelight Party to decide to live with the Cambodian People's Party in Siem Reap.
Mr. Tea Seiha also asked the members to look at the positive points that the CPP has made in the past and to look at the many achievements that the CPP has built.
Former CNRP member Ros Samnang, who represents nearly 600 members, said the decision to live with the CPP now comes after careful monitoring of the CPP leadership. Cambodians.
"We believe that only the Cambodian People's Party, which has the right ideals, has great merits for the motherland," he said. Therefore, we, who have always supported the former CNRP in the past, are disappointed and dissatisfied with the leadership of Sam Rainsy. Minister Pan Sosak: ASEAN-US Business Council employs more than 14 million people
(Washington, USA): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and President of ASEAN and other ASEAN Member States, on May 12, 2022, met with US business leaders co-organized by the Business Council. US-ASEAN and US Department of Commerce.
The meeting was organized to discuss and exchange business ideas between ASEAN member countries and the United States in order to learn more about the potential and opportunities for trade and investment in the ASEAN region, as well as to further strengthen and expand economic and trade cooperation. As for the economic recovery from the Kovid-19 crisis.
Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce, accompanied Samdech Techo Hun Sen to participate in this important meeting. He noted that since 1984, the US-ASEAN Business Council has been an important organization for US corporations, actively operating in ASEAN.
Globally, the US-ASEAN Business Council has about 180 member companies, generates nearly $ 7 trillion in revenue and employs about 14.5 million people, he said.
The council said the council now has members from major US companies doing business in ASEAN, from start-ups to companies that have been operating in Southeast Asia for more than 100 years. Eleven students of Hun Sen Pochentong Secondary School were sent to the emergency room immediately after fainting without knowing the reason
