The NEC continues to maintain the use of indelible ink by Indian companies for this Commune / Sangkat Council election.
(Phnom Penh): The National Election Committee (NEC) held a meeting with stakeholders to test the indelible ink to be used for the 5th Commune / Sangkat Council Election 2022, which was held. Under the chairmanship of Mr. Hal Sarath, Member of the NEC and chaired the meeting on the morning of May 13, 2022.
There are some suggestions and suggestions from the parties involved in the meeting regarding this indelible ink that should not be reserved at the Capital / Provincial Election Commission, should be sent back to the Commune / Sangkat Election Commission and should be reserved. Store properly.
In this case, the NEC stated that the reserve at the Capital and Provincial Election Commission was commensurate with the amount of ink left over from the distribution to 23,602 polling stations. 2 bottles. In the distribution, the NEC has a list of correct traces for inspection and security.
As for the request for an indelible ink test in the polling station, the NEC will consider this request for the next election.
This is the 5th meeting with the parties related to the election for the 5th Mandate Commune / Sangkat Council Election 2022, and the composition of the meeting was more than 60 people from various ministries and institutions such as the Constitutional Council, the Senate, the Ministry of Interior Ministry of Information, National Police General Commission, Disability Action Council, Indian Embassy representatives, political party representatives, NGO representatives, as well as journalists.
Discussion between Documentation Center of Cambodia, Preah Vihear Provincial Operational Area Commander and Choam Ksan District Governor on Health and History Project
(Preah Vihear): The working group of the Documentation Center of Cambodia, including Ms. Kim Sovandani, Mr. Som Bunthon and Mr. Phat Seila, met with Mr. Chan Sopheaktra, Commander of Preah Vihear Provincial Military Operation Area and Mr. Phan Samen, Commander of Choam Ksan District Military Operation Area to discuss On the work of the Khmer Rouge History and Health Project on May 12, 2022.
The objectives of the History and Health Project are:
* (1): Improving the health status of Khmer Rouge survivors in accordance with the set goals * (2): Raising awareness of public health and access to health services for survivors From the Khmer Rouge regime * and (3): Conduct research on the health status of Khmer Rouge survivors, especially in remote communities, to provide information on future development assistance to these people and communities. .
In May 2022, the Documentation Center of Cambodia team continues to recruit and train the fifth generation of volunteers from provinces across Cambodia. In Preah Vihear province, the Documentation Center of Cambodia team has identified Choam Ksan district as a priority destination to continue its work because most of the people in this district live in remote areas, are poor and need health care.
At the end of the meeting, Mr. Vuth Dara, Governor of Choam Ksan District, and Mr. Yung Hourn, Choam Ksan District Councilor, welcomed the working group of the Documentation Center of Cambodia to select Choam Ksan District as a target to conduct research related to the history of the Khmer Rouge and to assist In terms of health, because the survivors of the Khmer Rouge regime are getting older.
The meeting, co-hosted by the United States, Belize, Germany, Indonesia, and Senegal, with the participation of 14 other countries and institutions, was held to discuss end efforts. Epidemic COVID-19 and ready to respond to future health threats.
