All three suspects and exhibits are currently being held in custody at the Kratie City Police Inspectorate to build a case file.
Kantha Bopha Foundation of Cambodia in collaboration with ARDB uses the bank's services to raise and receive charitable donations
Memorandum of Understanding on the Use of Services of the Rural Development Bank and Agriculture for the Collection and Receipt of Charitable Contributions to the Kantha Bopha Foundation of Cambodia.
The ceremony was presided over by Dr. Kao Thach, Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of the Bank for Rural Development and Agriculture, and Dr. John Narith, Undersecretary of State, Ministry of Economy and Finance and Chairman of the Secretariat of the Kantha Bopha Foundation of Cambodia.
The MoU aims to provide financial support for the sustainability of Kantha Bopha Hospital through the use of digital banking services by the Rural Development Bank and Agriculture.
The use of banking services to collect charitable donations from the public will make it easier for the public to contribute to Kantha Bopha Hospital to ensure the sustainability of the hospital's services to improve the well-being of mothers, infants and children, which is an important foundation in building A sustainable workforce in line with the government's vision.
Dr. Kao Thach said that the signing of the Memorandum of Understanding with the Kantha Bopha Foundation of Cambodia now is a task that reflects the vision as well as the mission of the Bank for Rural Development and Agriculture.
In addition, Dr. Kao Thach emphasized that Cambodia is a low middle income country that will reach a high middle income country, and today's task is to help Cambodia to reach a high income country. Medium, advanced.
Dr. John Narith said that the signing of the MoU will make it easier for people to donate to Kantha Bopha Hospital, especially clients of the Rural Development Bank and Agriculture directly.
The signing of this memorandum is a testament to the participation of the Rural Development Bank and Agriculture in supporting and cooperating with the Kantha Bopha Foundation of Cambodia to contribute to saving the lives of Cambodian children.
In addition, the management and staff of ARDB Bank have volunteered to make monthly donations from the date of signing this Memorandum.
On this occasion, the Bank for Rural Development and Agriculture donated 25,052,000 Riels, which was donated by Dr. Kao Thach and Mrs. and all the management and staff to the Kantha Bopha Foundation of Cambodia.
