The US President made the remarks at a reception for Samdech Techo Hun Sen and ASEAN leaders on the evening of May 12 (Washington time) at the White House. In this ceremony, Mr. Jo Biden welcomed Samdech Techo Hun Sen and other ASEAN leaders with warmth and closeness.
During the ceremony, the President of the United States of America said that the ASEAN-US Special Summit coincides with the 45th anniversary of the ASEAN-US Dialogue Partnership. "The special summit is being held in Washington, DC, and is a new page and a new era in US-ASEAN relations," Biden said.
"ASEAN is at the heart of the United States in the Indo-Pacific framework, and not only that, the United States is pleased to upgrade its strategic partnership to a comprehensive strategic partnership between the United States and ASEAN, and this dinner is to celebrate "In strengthening and promoting good cooperation and relations with ASEAN." This is the confirmation of Mr. Joe Biden.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen, on behalf of the ASEAN Chairmanship, thanked the President of the United States for his warm hospitality to the Prince and other ASEAN leaders during his stay in the United States, and in particular A great restaurant wash.
He also stressed that this year marks the 45th anniversary of the ASEAN-US Dialogue, and that this is an appropriate time for ASEAN and US leaders to gather at the White House to commemorate the historic event of the United States. Long-term partnership.
"Indeed, our cooperation, which is based on a strong and firm foundation of mutual respect, has maintained a common good through a long and special period of time," he said. Overcome obstacles successfully.
On that occasion, Samdech Techo also shared his condolences with the United States for the loss of American lives due to Kovid 19 disease.
He said ASEAN and the United States now have the opportunity to reflect on the long-term process that ASEAN and the United States are working together to strengthen in all areas.
Samdech Techo also emphasized that as the chair of ASEAN in 2022, Cambodia has chosen the theme "ASEAN together to solve all challenges" based on this spirit, ASEAN has been working together to maintain peace and stability. As well as promoting the implementation of sustainable and inclusive prosperity, in fact, we recognize the positive role of ASEAN's external partners, especially the United States, in this whole process.
He added that ASEAN appreciates all that the United States has done. On behalf of the Prince himself, the Prince would like to express his deep gratitude to the President and the people of the United States for supporting Cambodia's role as ASEAN Chair this year.
Samdech Techo continued that with the rapidly evolving momentum towards the common good, Samdech would like to take this opportunity to invite the President to attend the 10th ASEAN-US Summit to be held in Cambodia. This coming November.
"In fact, we recognize the positive role of ASEAN's external partners, especially the United States, in the whole process," he said in front of ASEAN and US leaders. "ASEAN really appreciates what the United States has done for the region."
In particular, the President of Indonesia, as the chair of the ASEAN-US Dialogue, said that ASEAN and the United States will now continue to strengthen ties as well as cooperation, which will be upgraded from a strategic partner to a comprehensive strategic partner. This means that this is the highest level in the ASEAN framework.
Samdech Techo also emphasized on that occasion that the United States is playing an important role in the world, and this role, if the US economy is good, the world economy is also good. In addition, the United States has played a key role in the fight against Kovid 19 in the production of vaccines.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Sou Sannisith, Deputy Governor of the National Bank of Cambodia, co-chaired the meeting with the Ministry of Economy and Finance of Cambodia, the Ministry of Finance of China and the Central Bank of China to chair a meeting of the Minister of Finance and the Governor of the Central Bank of ASEAN + 3 25th online.
The meeting aims to review and discuss the progress of regional financial cooperation and provide guidance to the technical working group to strengthen the ASEAN + 3 Financial Security Network.
The meeting discussed the current situation and perspectives for the regional and global economy, key risks and challenges, and the implementation of response policies. ASEAN + 3 financial cooperation has played an important role in contributing to regional macroeconomic and financial stability to support sustainable and sustainable development.
In this regard, the Minister of Finance and the Governor of the Central Bank of ASEAN + 3 agreed to strengthen the capacity of the ASEAN + 3 Macroeconomic Research Organization (AMRO) to monitor and evaluate the macroeconomic situation of member countries and support the process of multilateral agreements. Chiang Mai Initiative (CMIM), a financing mechanism among member countries at risk or facing economic crisis to prevent and resolve crises.
In addition, the meeting also supported the development of the local currency bond market to mobilize savings and use of regional capital through the Asia Securities Exchange Initiative (ABMI).
The meeting also continued to promote the development of new future initiatives of ASEAN + 3, including financing of infrastructure construction, development of long-term financial instruments, prevention of natural disasters, and policy coordination. Towards technological advances, digitalization, finance and green financing support to strengthen financial stability and boost regional economic growth.
