"AFD supports the promotion of sustainable growth through the construction of quality infrastructure, strengthening soil resilience to climate change and environmental growth," said Ophelly Buris, AFD Country Director for Cambodia. "With 75% of the projects benefiting the climate, AFD strives to meet the needs of the Royal Government of Cambodia by incorporating climate concerns into our overall strategy."
The program will contribute to raising awareness and awareness of air quality, as well as better monitoring of air quality in the territories of ASEAN countries, as well as strengthening local capacity and designing programs or public loans that can lead to Reduce pollution.
Please note that AFD is an institution in the AFD group that implements French policy in the field of development and international solidarity. AFD provides assistance to the public sector and non-governmental organizations and supports research, publication and training on sustainable development, etc. Overall, AFD provides funding to support and promote the transition to a more accurate and resilient world.
With its partners, AFD seeks solutions that are shared with and for the people of the South. The AFD team works on more than 4,000 projects in 115 countries and territories in crisis for common property: climate, peace, gender equality, education and health. Through this, AFD joins the commitment of the country and the people of France to achieve the goal of sustainable development for a united world.
