(Washington, USA): Duke Kith Meng, President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, led a delegation from the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce to meet with the American business community to explore joint investment opportunities and showcase investment potential in Cambodia.
During the ceremony held on the morning of May 12, 2022 in Washington, DC, the intervention of the Cambodian business and economic environment from the delegation of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce to present business and investment opportunities in Cambodia. To the American business community.
Neak Oknha Kith Meng, President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, told the American business community about the potential for more American companies to invest in Cambodia as the Royal Government of Cambodia opens its economy to national and international investors.
The duke also told the American business community that the Royal Government of Cambodia's efforts to vaccinate 93 percent of Cambodia's 16 million people are a good sign for investment in Cambodia. In addition, Duke Kith Meng also mentioned that free trade between Cambodia and friendly countries is a good opportunity for investors to export goods to the world.
Mr. Rubar Sandi, Representative of the American Business Community, welcomed the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce delegation to the United States, which is a good opportunity for investors to meet and focus on investment in infrastructure, water technology, and financial technology. Business, special rights, real estate and intellectual property, etc.
Representatives of the American business community also expressed interest in the investment potential in Cambodia and look forward to working with Cambodian investors to find investment opportunities.
It should be noted that with the high permission of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, Duke Kith Meng, President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, led a delegation of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce to pay a business visit to the United States from May 8 to May 15, 2022 and accompany Samdech Techo to the ASEAN-US Special Summit.
The Bank of Thailand closely monitors the baht, the lowest value in five years
The Bank of Thailand (BoT) said on Thursday that the baht's move has had a "limited impact" on inflation and the Thai economy after it weakened to its lowest level in a year. Five years against the US dollar on Thursday.
She added that it was not necessary to use interest rates to control the baht, as the currency was fluctuating in line with the local currency and had no significant impact on inflation or the economy.
