The following is the announcement of Kampong Thom Provincial Administration: Senior Minister Osman Hassan attends the Interfaith Common Values Forum in Riyadh, Saudi Arabia
(Saudi Arabia): On the afternoon of May 11, 2022, Dr. Osman Hassan, Senior Minister in Charge of Special Missions, Member of the Supreme Council of the Organization of the Islamic Organization (RABITA), participated in the Interfaith Values Forum. Held in Riyadh, Saudi Arabia.
The forum aims to develop a civilized view, to cultivate values of centralism in the human community, and to strengthen friendships and cooperation among people of different religions, as well as to raise awareness of the definition of peace and harmony. Between religious leaders. The forum provides effective and influential ideas in society for maintaining the values of peace and harmony between nations and religions.
On that occasion, Dr. Osman Hassan also exchanged views with religious leaders around the world on racial and religious harmony.
Dr. continued to mention the achievements of the Cambodian Muslim community from the Royal Government of Cambodia, such as the government has allowed representatives of the Khmer Muslim community to be leaders in the Senate, National Assembly, Royal Government, Secretary of State, Undersecretary of State, senior diplomats, national authorities and lower levels. National Armed Forces of all kinds and civil servants.
In addition, the government allows, in principle, Muslim men to wear a bag and Muslim women to wear a passport, make ID cards or take photographs for administrative documents.
Muslim female students can wear traditional attire and wear a krama while studying at both public and private educational institutions. In addition, the Royal Government has included about 1,500 Khmer-Muslim teachers in the framework of teachers of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, and 180 contract officials.
The forum is also attended by more than 100 religious leaders from more than 100 countries around the world, including Islam, Buddhism, Judaism, Christianity.
