Following is a press release from the Office of the Spokesperson of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training: ACLEDA Becomes Cambodia's First Commercial Bank to Provide Securities Services in the Securities Sector
(Phnom Penh): ACLEDA Bank Plc. Has been officially approved by the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia to certify securities agents in the securities sector.
This is the first time that the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia has approved this certification so that ACLEDA Bank can play a more active role in contributing to the development of the securities sector in Cambodia by attracting large foreign investors to invest in the securities sector in Cambodia. Cambodia.
Speaking at the Accreditation Ceremony of ACLEDA Bank Plc. As a Securities Agent from the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia on 12 May 2022, Dr. IN Channy, Chief Executive Officer of ACLEDA Bank Plc., Said that ACLEDA Bank is a commercial bank. The first in Cambodia to be listed on the Cambodia Securities Exchange (CSX) on May 25, 2020.
In 2022, the Bank has achieved new achievements by obtaining the "Certificate of Accreditation of ACLEDA Bank as a Securities Agent in the Securities Sector" from the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia (NCCC), which has made ACLEDA Bank a commercial bank. The first in Cambodia to provide security services in the securities sector.
He added that Securities Securities Agency is a new service of ACLEDA Bank to provide securities security services to investors and the public. The main functions of this service include: Cash Securities Account, Securities Securities Account and Securities Securities Agent Service.
"We see that the securities sector in Cambodia has been growing remarkably, which is an important driver that led ACLEDA Bank to take a step in providing this service," he said. In our country, if there is a securities agency, the securities sector has all the elements that enable foreign investors as an institution to invest because they need this agency.
Mr. Sou Socheat, the Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of the Securities Regulator of Cambodia, said that the Securities and Exchange Commission is the custodian of both bonds and equity securities. Securities brokers are an important service that large foreign investors looking to invest in the securities sector need to get the agency to do some work in the securities sector on their behalf.
He said that the conditions for obtaining the certificate must be from a banking institution, and he welcomed other banks to apply for the certificate, securities agencies in the securities sector.
