US household debt rises to nearly $ 16 trillion, but mortgage and car loans fall
Mortgage loan debt reached $ 11.18 trillion by the end of March, Reuters reported, citing the US Federal Reserve's quarterly household debt report released in New York on Tuesday. Which now accounts for 71% of total household debt, the highest share in about a decade.
But new lending for both home loans and refinancing for existing real estate loans fell 17 percent to $ 859 billion, the lowest level since the second quarter of 2020. However, that number is still $ 100 billion larger than before the outbreak of Kovid-19 in the fourth quarter of 2019.
Car loans also fell, the third straight quarter of declines to $ 177 billion. Credit card balances fell to $ 841 billion from $ 856 billion, and student loans rose to $ 1.59 trillion from $ 1.58 trillion. According to Reuters.
Fuel crisis in Laos worsens as Vientiane runs out of fuel
Faced with losses due to a weakening local currency and a lack of foreign reserves, oil importers are unable to continue buying oil. In fact, importers say they can supply only 20% of Laos' total fuel demand.
Reports indicate that Laos needs about 120 million liters of oil per month, with importers currently able to import only about 20 million liters.
The Lao state-owned company informed its resellers, regretting that it had reached a point where it "could no longer meet the needs of its customers."
The Lao government has made several attempts to resolve the fuel crisis, with the Lao National Assembly agreeing to reduce fuel tariffs after an emergency meeting on Monday and the Ministry of Finance trying to control the exchange rate.
The National Bank of Cambodia, the Microfinance Association of Cambodia, the Association of Banks in Cambodia, and the CPPCC have jointly initiated the "Save My Life" blood donation campaign.
(Phnom Penh): The National Bank of Cambodia, the Cambodian Microfinance Association, the Banking Association of Cambodia and the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia have partnered with the National Blood Transfusion Center to launch the "Save My Life" blood donation campaign to raise blood donations from staff in the banking and financial sector. Stakeholders and the public to save the lives of those in urgent need of blood.
