(Phnom Penh): The National Election Committee (NEC) has issued a notification reminding that the Commune / Sangkat Council election campaign will start from May 21 to June 3, 2022. Campaigning is a series of public actions to persuade voters to vote for a candidate or political party.
In a statement received by Fresh News on May 12, 2022, it was stated that this period is not yet the day of the 5th Mandate Commune / Sangkat Council Election Campaign. The NEC calls for the immediate cessation of political parties acting in violation of the election law and campaign-related rules and procedures.
The National Election Committee (NEC) has already issued Notification No. 042 NEC dated 30 April 2022 to all political parties that have registered their candidates for the election. Official ban on activities as stated in Article 68 of the Law on Commune / Sangkat Council Election (CEC) before the deadline as stated in Article 70 of the Law on Commune / Sangkat Council Election .
The NEC considers that all election campaign activities contrary to Article 70 shall be punished under Article 184 of the Law on Commune / Sangkat Council Election.
Any of the above-mentioned activities of a political party that has officially allowed the registration of candidates of a political party to stand for election shall be considered as election campaign activities. This election campaign lasts for 15 (fourteen) days and all campaign activities must stop 24 (twenty-four) hours before the election day in accordance with Article 70 of the Law on Commune / Sangkat Council Election.
The NEC calls on all political parties that have registered as candidates of official political parties and candidates to abide by the laws, regulations and procedures of the election and the code of conduct set by the NEC.
