Thailand's Phuket aims to attract 1 million tourists in Q4
BKK: Phuket aims to attract 1 million foreign tourists in the fourth quarter of this year and a total of 3.5 million this year as tour operators on the island see positive signs after easing. Recent travel restrictions. According to the Bangkok Post.
About 328,004 tourists visited Phuket in the first four months of this year.
The Bangkok Post reported that the second largest group of foreign tourists visiting Phuket came from Australia, which numbered about 10,000 in April. That number is expected to reach 15,000 a month. Other leading markets for Phuket are the United Kingdom, Singapore, Malaysia and Saudi Arabia.
According to the Bangkok Post, in 2019, before the outbreak of Kovid-19, Phuket received 10 million international tourists, including 3 million from China.
