Activists have warned that the military's interests in the economy, including banking, oil, agriculture and tourism, mean that tourist spending will help the military government, even if they avoid hotel accommodation and controlled transportation. By the military, but they will contribute through visa fees, insurance and other value-added taxes.
Myanmar closed its border to tourists in March 2020, when the first Kovid 19 plague broke out to prevent the spread, and the closure continued after a coup overthrew the former leader. Aung San Suu Kyi in February 2021.
