Cambodia's insurance sector is expected to grow by more than 10% this year, while last year insurance premiums amounted to $ 297 million, up 9%
(Phnom Penh): In 2021, the gross premium in the insurance sector in Cambodia will increase to 297 million US dollars, an increase of 9% compared to 2020.
At the same time, Mr. Bou Chanphiro, Director General of the Insurance Regulator of Cambodia, expressed his strong hope that in 202222, the premium in this sector will increase by more than 10 percent.
Mr. Bou Chanpiru's remarks were made on the occasion of participating in the introductory seminar on "Basic training materials for insurance agents and sales staff of insurance companies" held on May 12, 2022.
"The insurance sector is still growing well, despite the fact that Cambodia is facing an epidemic of 19 cases of measles. In fact, by 2020, the insurance sector will increase by 8% and by 2021, it will increase by more than 9%," he said. "In 2022, there will be an increase of more than 10 percent."
He said that the Cambodian insurance market has grown rapidly with an average annual increase of 18% in the last five years. The insurance market in Cambodia is still small compared to the regional market, in which the premium rate contribution in the economy is only 1.1%.
He stressed that while the public's awareness of insurance services and benefits remains low, insurance sales should not be limited to lobbying or promotion, such as sales of general consumer products, but frontline staff. Have clear insurance knowledge to be able to incorporate consumer education ideas in it to attract customers to use insurance with confidence for a long time.
Through today's workshop, all trainees who are trainers for each insurance company will have a better understanding of the content of this joint curriculum, which will enhance the quality of training of insurance agents and sales staff of each company according to the program. Study clearly.
Mr. Huy Vatharo, President of the Insurance Association of Cambodia, mentioned the need to increase the knowledge and capacity of the insurance profession of the insurance staff in each insurance company, especially frontline staff.
Please be informed that the Insurance Association has prepared a basic training course for insurance companies to use in training their agents and insurance sales staff in accordance with the guidelines on professional training of agents issued by the Insurance Regulator of Cambodia.
The purpose of this workshop is to provide a guide on the content and how to use this tutorial to the participants who are the instructors of each insurance company to use effectively and consistently in teaching insurance agents and their sales staff. The King issues a Royal Decree appointing and appointing two advisors to the President of the Constitutional Council
