(Phnom Penh): Nowadays, advances in technology and social media have led to the production of many films or short videos to serve the entertainment of people of all ages. But along with this growth, there are also a few videos posted on social media have a negative impact on society.
In this context, what are the important roles of producers and artists in promoting the morality of Cambodian society and preventing violence against women and children? Her Excellency Dr. Pheung Sakona, Minister of Culture and Fine Arts, told Cambodia-China Friendship Radio in a recent interview at the Ministry that producers and artists are considered important public figures in promoting education to society. Especially young people.
She states that the promotion of various products, writers, directors or sellers of products online has many ways to attract viewers with social interests.
Voice: "What needs to be advertised must be real, not just sold out, regardless of the social impact!" "There are a lot of arts and crafts. We should not take the traditional cultural identity, national values and jokes for our own benefit. We should learn what can be disseminated without degrading the moral values and national identity."
She emphasizes that artists have a very important role to play in spreading the word, because each of them has millions of followers on social media, so if they act as a messenger to promote the national values of Cambodian culture will make Has a positive impact on society.
Sovann Rithy, also known as Ta Victor, a producer, told Cambodia-China Friendship Radio that producers and artists really play an important role in promoting the morality of Cambodian society. He stressed that producers, artists, artists, before producing a story or video, must think about ethics, social law, educational values, social values, women and children.
Voice: "Incorporating ethics is very beneficial for the audience, especially children, it is a role model because children can not get an education without a model, so if we do it just to attract them It is not right to make tea, that it is made to eat, but to eat it is not nutritious. "Any program for broadcasting is the same, we have to think about morality, culture, traditions and know ourselves as Khmer."
In order to promote this social value, Mr. Sovann Rithy also asked the sponsors to know the value of the program or the story, the meaning, the content, not the pool of money to support, otherwise the support will be lost. The value of women will affect the society.
At the same time, Mr. Susarun alias Santa KH, a short video producer and comedian, also considers that he, like other artists, is a well-known person in society, if not broadcast easily, it will have an impact. Society and visitors. Therefore, he is only committed to learning and producing a lot of new videos by incorporating educational messages related to social values, promoting the values of women and children, especially educational messages on drugs, alcohol and so on.
Voice: "Basically, making my funny videos in public, and further, we will increase the inclusion of educational messages, and after listening to Mr. Oum Chumteav, he said that makes us more reminiscent of what to create. "New and educated."
Social watchdogs in Cambodia see that those who cause social pollution affect the values of women, most of the cultural traditions are not professional artists, but rather social media players, such as: Facebook Tik Tok YouTube and posing as a star and some are an online seller, some of whom dress inappropriately, like to publish family stories in public, leading to social pollution and so on.
Overall, producers, artists, and writers all play a very important role in incorporating short educational content related to the promotion of social morality and women's values into their films, songs, feature films, series or videos. Adhere to a culture of non-violence and promote a civilized life worthy of a country of peace, development and a country with moral values, good society, left by our Cambodian ancestors for generations.
