(Phnom Penh): A group of 5,000 active youth members of the Phnom Penh Economic Youth Local Party Committee, under the auspices of Ley Sopheap, have voted to vote for the Cambodian People's Party (CPP) to join the peace process with the CPP and the Cambodian people. Across the country.
This commitment was welcomed by Mr. Khuong Sreng, Member of the Central Committee of the Cambodian People's Party and Chairman of the Committee of the Cambodian People's Party in Phnom Penh during a meeting with youth activists of the Phnom Penh Local Economic Youth Committee in the afternoon. May 11, 2022 at Koh Pich Theater.
The decision of these youth groups is because they want to participate in protecting the hard-earned peace, because peace is the most important cause that every nation has always aspired to. These young people have seen the value of peace through the Russian-Ukrainian war, which has wreaked havoc on the people, according to their representatives.
On that occasion, Mr. Ley Sopheap, Chairman of the Standing Committee of the Phnom Penh Economic Youth Local Party Committee, announced that approximately 5,000 active members of the Phnom Penh Economic Youth Local Party Committee have already registered to vote and are ready to vote. Voting for the Cambodian People's Party, especially for the upcoming 5th Commune / Sangkat Council Election 2022, as well as the 2023 general election.
Mr. Ley Sopheap and the 5,000 active youth groups also announced their full support for Samdech Techo Hun Sen as the Prime Ministerial candidate and the election of Mr. Hun Manet as the future Prime Minister candidate.
Mr. Ley Sopheap continued, "The election for the Cambodian People's Party is a contribution to maintaining peace for the future, which we find difficult."
