Regarding bilateral issues, Dr. Kao Kim Hourn, Minister accompanying the Prime Minister, said that Samdech Techo Hun Sen and the Prime Minister of Vietnam discussed the fight against Kovid 19, tourism, trade, elections and border affairs.
On the issue of smallpox 19, Samdech Techo Hun Sen briefed the Vietnamese Prime Minister on Cambodia's success in controlling smallpox 19 until there were no new infections five days ago, and Cambodia is prioritizing students to get vaccinated. Well. For Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the successful management of Kovid 19 has been making Cambodia better on economic management.
The Vietnamese Prime Minister congratulated Cambodia on its good results in controlling the Kovid 19 epidemic. He also felt that the successful management of Kovid 19 would make a significant contribution to the recovery of the Cambodian economy.
Regarding the election issue, Samdech Techo Hun Sen informed the Vietnamese Prime Minister that the atmosphere of the election process in Cambodia is improving. Samdech Techo highlighted that the democratic process and political stability in Cambodia are good, which is an important point for investment.
In this regard, the Vietnamese Prime Minister also agreed with Samdech Techo Prime Minister to ensure that the two countries fully reopen tourism, both by land and air.
In this meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Mr. Pham Minh Chinh also discussed the border issue between the two countries, which will reach 6% in 2022 after three years of negotiations. The two countries plan to sign the 6% border agreement in 2022. So far, the border issue between Cambodia and Vietnam has reached 90 percent.
The Prime Minister of Vietnam also expressed his intention to visit the King of Cambodia, His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni and Queen Norodom Monineath Sihanouk to pay a royal visit to Vietnam, as well as to invite Samdech Techo to visit Vietnam to strengthen ties. Between the two countries.
