These two locations include: at Mlup Svay Restaurant (old location) in Pen village, Leach commune, Phnom Kravanh district, and location 2: at the suspect's house in Boang Puoy village, Leach commune, Phnom Kravanh district, Pursat province.
Lieutenant Colonel Hem Mony, Deputy Commissioner for Anti-Drug Planning, told Fresh News Agency in Pursat province this morning, May 12, that the operation to crack down on the two major drug trafficking sites was based on confessions. Of the suspect named Dy Rithy.
Currently, the two suspects, along with exhibits, were forcibly brought to continue the proceedings for legal action.
China's successful rural development experience is a good lesson for developing countries
(Beijing): Unlike many countries that focus on development only on investing in major cities and urban areas, China has focused primarily on rural areas. So far, China has made remarkable achievements in rural development, such as poverty eradication and significant growth in agricultural productivity and productivity.
China has become the first developing country to achieve the first of the 17 Sustainable Development Goals, lifting nearly 800 million Chinese people out of poverty, three-quarters of the population. People are being lifted out of poverty all over the world.
Despite these great achievements, the Chinese government continues to focus on rural areas, with Chinese leaders believing that poverty eradication is not the end goal, just a new starting point. The goal is to bring rural areas back to life.
Developing countries can learn, understand and learn from the successful experience of China's rural development. Among the many factors, there are a number of major factors that contribute significantly to China's success in rural development. In addition to the strength of the Chinese people, the strong political will and the wise and firm leadership of the Chinese government are indispensable factors leading to the achievement of all these outstanding achievements.
At the same time, the central government is well prepared to provide all the necessary support to make implementation effective. So far, the central government has provided billions of dollars to support the implementation of measures to reduce poverty and develop rural areas.
He added that demining is our job, which requires the participation of all stakeholders, including development partners, the private sector and philanthropists, in order to end the mine threat in Cambodia.
On that occasion, the Senior Minister praised and appreciated the forces of the NPMEC National Center for participating in turning Prey Veng into a demining province, which proves that the leaders of the NPMEC National Center not only sent peacekeepers Abroad, not only under the auspices of the United Nations, but also contributing to the peace in Cambodia through demining work.
