Rural Rehabilitation and Development Strategy is a national policy to strengthen China's poverty alleviation achievements to improve the living standards of farmers
China is a major agricultural country after achieving the goal of eradicating hunger by increasing food production. Not only its 1.4 billion people, but also to supply food to needy countries in order to achieve common prosperity in line with the Chinese President's "Global Development" initiative.
2020 can be said to be the time when China faces the biggest test ever in history, as it is the last year that the Chinese party and government have promised the Chinese people that it will eradicate poverty in all its forms. While fighting the spread of Kovid-19, it must also work to achieve the goal of eradicating poverty in accordance with its 13th Five-Year National Development Plan.
Therefore, poverty alleviation work can not be suspended because the people have just been lifted out of poverty, in this sense, the problem before the Chinese government to solve is after getting out of poverty, what can be done? Prevent poor people from falling back into poverty and have a better life?
In line with Xi Jinping's vision of "Green Mountains, Clear Water, Golden Mountains, Silver Mountains", the conservation of natural resources has achieved remarkable achievements that not only beautify nature but also eco-tourism. Rural income as well.
The Ministry does not recognize the Kovid 19 vaccination card issued by a private company and claims that the certificate is free of charge.
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Health on May 12, 2022 issued a press release confirming that it does not recognize 19 Kovid vaccines issued by private companies or individuals other than the Ministry of Health or the Ministry of National Defense. This is according to the announcement of Mrs. O Vandin, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health and Chair of the Commission for the 19-Kovid vaccination program nationwide.
The commission's denial of such work follows previous announcements on social media of private companies and individuals claiming that it had cooperated with the Ministry of Health in obtaining a new Kovid-19 vaccination card or possibly issuing it. Kovid-19 vaccination certificate for citizens for use abroad.
The Commission on the Nationwide KV-19 Vaccination (CPV-19) completely rejects the announcements of companies and individuals and calls for an immediate end to all such propaganda activities. At the same time, CEC-19 calls on all citizens to stop believing in these scams to avoid losing money and causing anarchy in society that undermines the policies of the Royal Government. .
