Cambodia to Attend 15th ASEAN Health Ministers' Meeting and Related Meetings May 11-15 in Indonesia
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health, on May 13, 2022, will lead a delegation of the Ministry of Health to attend the 15th ASEAN Health Ministers' Meeting and related meetings to be held from 11 May 15, 2022 in Bali, Indonesia.
The ASEAN Health Ministers' Meeting and related meetings are the highest level meetings in the health sector, usually held every two years in the rotating chair. The 15th meeting will be attended by the Ministers of Health of the 10 ASEAN Member States, ASEAN Plus Three (China, Japan and the Republic of Korea) and the United States.
The five-day meeting will consist of several meetings: 1: Preparatory Meeting of ASEAN Health Ministers 2: 153rd ASEAN Health Ministers' Meeting: 94th ASEAN Plus Three Ministerial Meeting on Health 85th ASEAN-China Health Ministers: 16th ASEAN-Korea Health Ministers' Meeting: Special Meeting of ASEAN-US Health Ministers.
The Minister will address a number of interventions according to the theme of each meeting. The meeting will also issue a number of joint statements on the commitment of all member countries and dialogue partners to promote the health of the people in the region as well as the world as a whole, especially in promoting economic recovery. After the Kovid-19 crisis.
