(Washington, USA): Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen has stated that it is only in the Second Kingdom that relations between Cambodia and the United States have improved compared to the previous regime. The Prime Minister wants to improve on some of the differences to improve Cambodia-US relations.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasized this during a courtesy meeting and working discussion with Ms. Sena Dummaker, US Senator, on the morning of May 11, 2022 (Washington time).
According to Dr. Kao Kim Hourn, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister, during the meeting, the US Senator shared her condolences with the Prime Minister, as well as his family and relatives on the death of His Excellency Tep Nhean Hun Neng.
Dr. Kao Kim Hourn also said that in this meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen mentioned the difficult situation of Cambodia in the past and the progress of Cambodia today after the complete cessation of the flames of war in 1998.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also highlighted the relationship between Cambodia and the United States. In that, Samdech Techo said that the relationship between Cambodia and the United States under the leadership of the Royal Government by Samdech is the best time compared to the past. Especially before the 1970s, there were tensions that led to the burning of embassies, the brief severance of diplomatic relations, and the eventual severance of the Democratic Kampuchea regime.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen reminded of the search and assistance of Samdech so that the US Embassy has a clear embassy location near Wat Phnom Penh. This is a demonstration of Samdech's efforts to improve relations between Cambodia and the United States.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also highlighted the improvement of economic, trade and investment relations between Cambodia and the United States. In 2021, despite the global Kovid 19 crisis, Cambodia-US trade volume increased by about 30 percent, and in the first quarter of 2022, trade volume between the two countries increased by about 40 percent.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also mentioned the better investment climate in Cambodia. This improved investment climate has made many American companies investing in Cambodia. In connection with this investment, Samdech Techo asked the US Senator to further promote US investment in Cambodia.
At the same time, Cambodia has cooperated well with the United States in the search for the remains of American soldiers who died during the war, so far only 49 cases remain.
In addition to the positive development of bilateral relations, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also mentioned that the election against Russia's aggression on Ukraine at the United Nations.
Raising the above issues, Samdech Techo, the head of the Royal Government, would like to highlight the improvement of the relationship between Cambodia and the United States, which arises from the attention of the Royal Government of Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech himself.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also raised a number of issues that hinder the strengthening and expansion of relations between Cambodia and the United States. According to Samdech Techo, the issues that Samdech considers to be differences between Cambodia and the United States include the agreement to send Cambodians back to the country when they are convicted, the conditions for visas for diplomats, and so on.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen asked the US Senator to consider mediation on this issue.
Mr. Kao Kim Hourn quoted Samdech as saying, "Our country is not under any country, our country is independent and sovereign. So we do not need foreign troops on Cambodian territory. "Whether it is the Chinese army or the army of any country."
Samdech Techo stated that currently, the port of Sihanoukville welcomes Chinese, American, Japanese, Indian and Australian ships to dock at Cambodian ports without discrimination.
Samdech Techo also highlighted the democratic process in Cambodia. Samdech Techo stated that Cambodia will organize the election campaign of the 5th Commune / Sangkat Council Election on May 21 and the election will be held on June 5, with 17 parties competing.
Samdech Techo claimed that this is a good process of democracy in Cambodia.
