Samdech Techo Hun Sen: Cambodia wants to be friends with the United States, but can not choose between China and the United States
(Washington, USA): Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen has noted that the relationship between Cambodia and the United States, which has lasted 72 years, is reaching an unprecedented level in history. Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasized that Cambodia really wants to be a friend of the United States, but can not determine Cambodia to choose between the United States and China.
Dr. Kao Kim Hourn, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister, said that in this meeting, Samdech Techo and former senators welcomed each other with friendliness and brotherhood. In addition to welcoming each other, former US Senator Donald Benton also asked Samdech Techo about the purpose of his current visit to the United States.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen pointed out that there are two important tasks to be done during his visit to Washington. The first important issue is the ASEAN-US issue and the second is the relationship between Cambodia and the United States.
According to Dr. Kao Kim Hourn, regarding the bilateral relationship, Samdech Techo Hun Sen highlighted the importance of the relationship between Cambodia and the United States for the past 72 years. Samdech Techo noted that relations and cooperation between Cambodia and the United States are evolving to an unprecedented level in history.
Mr. Kao Kim Hourn quoted the Prime Minister as saying, "In this 72-year relationship, we have reached an unprecedented level between the two countries. Cambodia really wants to be a friend of the United States and Cambodia can not choose between the United States or China. Cambodia has a neutral policy enshrined in the Cambodian Constitution. "So Cambodia wants to be friends with all countries, including the United States."
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that through this good relationship, the volume of trade and investment between Cambodia and the United States is also growing significantly.
Regarding ASEAN-US issues, the Prime Minister also highlighted the important role between ASEAN and the United States. Samdech Techo Hun Sen called the ASEAN-US Special Summit a rare opportunity for ASEAN-US to strengthen and expand ASEAN-US trade and investment relations.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also informed the former US Congressman that he would like to see the relationship between ASEAN and the United States move from a strategic partner to a comprehensive strategic partner, which is a top-level relationship.
