General Department of Taxation Meets Private Sector to Solve 15 Challenges
(Phnom Penh): The General Department of Taxation on May 11, 2022 organized a meeting between the working group of the General Department of Taxation and the private sector, the meeting raised 15 challenges and solutions to the private sector. The meeting was chaired by Mr. Kong Vibol, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Director General of the General Department of Taxation.
The General Department of Taxation listened carefully to the challenges raised by the private sector and discussed solutions such as:
1: Interest rates on loans between related parties: The General Department of Taxation has accepted the request of the private sector to revise the requirement to provide supporting documents to implement zero interest rates on loans between related parties.
2. Disposal of Assets: The General Department of Taxation has promised to prepare additional guidelines, including some of the points requested by the private sector in response to the concerns of taxpayers.
3. Customer guarantee: The General Department of Taxation has confirmed that all business guarantees and compensation are not subject to VAT.
6: Refund of Refund: The General Department of Taxation has promised to promote the refund of refunds to enterprises by the time specified in the Prakas of the Ministry of Economy and Finance and requested the enterprise to request a refund as soon as possible and the General Department of Taxation It was also clarified that the General Department of Taxation could not refund taxes from bills that occurred over a long period of time and could not be verified.
7. Cambodia Off-Border Sales Transaction: The General Department of Taxation has accepted a request for further study on Cambodian off-border sales operations to attract more investment to Cambodia.
10: Certificate of Fiscal Compliance and Certificate of Accreditation: The General Department of Taxation has accepted the request for inclusion of Fiscal Certificate with Certificate of Accreditation for enterprises with compliance level. The gold category automatically receives a minimum tax exemption, which encourages taxpayers to better abide by the law.
