Speaking to Fresh News, Mr. Thuon Sinan, President of the Asia-Pacific Tourism Association of Cambodia, emphasized that the number of international tourists will increase further after the recent reopening of the Cambodia-Thailand border, which will make it easier for tourists to cross. Along the land border.
He said that the association is currently working with the Vietnamese and Thai sides to organize tour packages and exchange tourists, which will be fruitful in July to attract international tourists to boost growth. Tourism to Cambodia.
He said there were a number of obstacles to the flow of tourists from the three countries, such as the limited number of flights, the high cost of airfare and the high paperwork requirements of officials at the three countries' border crossings. Difficult to get in and out.
According to a report by the Secretary of State for Civil Aviation, in April 2022, the number of passengers passing through the three international airports was more than 12.3 million, an increase of more than 500% compared to the same period in 2021, which was just over one. Only 90,000 people. As of April 2022, there were 1,712 flights, an increase of 112% or 806. The fastest growing routes are Phnom Penh-Bangkok and Phnom Penh-Singapore.
However, Mr. Thuon Sinan said that despite the wide opening, the tourism sector in Cambodia has not been able to return to the status of 2019.
According to the Ministry of Tourism, in the first four months of 2022, Cambodia received more than 220,000 international tourists. Through the growth and recovery of the tourism sector, the Ministry estimates that Cambodia will be able to receive 800,000 tourists by the end of 2022.
The Ministry of Tourism expects Cambodia to achieve further tourist growth through the promotion of vaccinated tourism, as well as based on changes in new tourism trends, focusing on intra-ASEAN tourism and short-haul tourism. Travel between 4 to 5 hours to Korea, Japan, India, Australia.
