(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Cambodia is preparing to share experiences of implementing the Convention on Safe, Legal and Legal Migration (GCM) at the United Nations International Migration Governance (IMRF) Assessment Forum this month. May 2022 in New York, USA.
This was confirmed by Ms. Chou Bun Eng, Permanent Vice President of the National Committee for Combating Human Trafficking (NEC) and Secretary of State of the Ministry of Interior on May 11, 2022 at the Phnom Penh Hotel. Techniques for reviewing voluntary evaluation reports on national GCM implementation to prepare for participation in the IMRF. She said the IMRF will be held from May 17 to 20, 2022.
The Global Covenant on Safe, orderly and legal migration (GCM) is the first comprehensive UN document adopted through intergovernmental dialogue to improve international cooperation in global migration governance and to Agreed by the UN General Assembly, held on December 19, 2018 in New York, with 152 member countries.
