(Washington, USA): Despite being tired because it took up to 20 hours to fly from Cambodia to Washington, USA, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, when he arrived in Washington, he still met Cambodians in the United States. Analyze social issues on Facebook.
Khmer is an analyst on social media in the United States, which Samdech Techo allowed to meet more than 10 people, led by Mr. Mak Horn and his wife. Mak Horn is a social analyst who always presents the realities of problems in Cambodian society. In all social media posts, Mr. Mak Horn always mentions both positives and negatives in Cambodian society.
Yong Noy, also known as Brady, is a Cambodian-American living in Long Beach. He was originally a former CNRP activist and often posted on Facebook criticizing and severely attacking Samdech Techo and the Royal Government of Cambodia.
In this meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed his warm welcome to Cambodians in the United States and also expressed his happiness and longing for them. Samdech Techo thanked the Cambodian people in the United States for always participating in disseminating the reality of the problems in Cambodian society and always appreciating the Royal Government's national development efforts.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen encouraged the dissemination and provision of information to make the communication between Cambodians abroad and Cambodians at home closer and better together.
