Please be informed that Samdech Techo Hun Sen led a high-level delegation of the Royal Government of Cambodia to leave Phnom Penh at 7:45 am on May 10, 2022 to attend the ASEAN-US Special Summit.
The special summit will be held from May 12 to 13 in Washington to celebrate the 45-year ASEAN-US Dialogue Partnership. This is the second special summit since 2016 and the first face-to-face meeting for ASEAN-US leaders since 2017.
The presence of Samdech Techo Hun Sen at the ASEAN-US Special Summit, as well as other ASEAN member countries, was made at the invitation of US President Joe Biden. The presence of Samdech Techo Hun Sen is very important in the meeting as the chair of ASEAN, who will co-chair the meeting with Jo Biden.
During the historic summit, ASEAN and US leaders will set out the future direction of ASEAN-US relations and promote a strategic partnership for mutual benefit. Mutual integration of the people of ASEAN and the people of the United States.
ASEAN leaders will also meet with US business leaders to discuss economic cooperation. ASEAN leaders will welcome and hold a meeting with US Vice President Kamala Harris for a plenary session with US Secretary of State on climate change measures, clean energy and sustainable infrastructure.
The Ministry of Foreign Affairs also said that Samdech Techo Prime Minister Hun Sen will have a bilateral meeting with Mr. Pham Minh Chinh, Prime Minister of the Socialist Republic of Vietnam and leaders of some ASEAN member countries.
It should be noted that during his visit to the United States, Samdech Techo Hun Sen will also meet with Cambodians living, working and studying in the United States to visit and express their condolences. . Meeting and conversing with Cambodians abroad is a habit that Samdech Techo always takes when he is invited to work abroad, no matter how busy he is.
According to a press release issued by the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, Prime Minister Hun Sen was accompanied by Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation Sun Chanthol, Senior Minister of Public Works and Transport and Minister of Commerce Pan Sosak. Dr. Hang Chuon Naron, Minister of Education, Youth and Sports and other senior officials of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
