Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng Attends a 7-Day Nursing Ceremony for the Body of Samdech Udom Tep Nhean Hun Neng
(Kampong Cham): On Tuesday morning, May 10, 2022, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, attended the 7-day Nursing Ceremony dedicated to the late Samdech Udom Tep Nhean Hun Neng, Member of Parliament for Kampong Cham Constituency. Permanent member of the National Assembly and Chairman of the Fourth Committee of the National Assembly.
Samdech Udom Tep Nhean Hun Neng passed away on May 5, 2022 at the age of 72. The 7-day anniversary ceremony dedicated to the late Samdech Udom Tep Nhean was held at the home of Samdech and Lok Chumteav in Village 7, Sangkat Kampong Cham, Kampong Cham City, Kampong Cham Province.
In his condolence message to Ms. Leav Vouch Chheng Hun Neng, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister, emphasized that Samdech Udom Tep Nhean Hun Neng is an outstanding Cambodian and a hero with a strong spirit and patriotic will who sacrificed his strength. Body and mind, mind, struggle, not afraid to get tired, participate in the cause of the nation, the motherland and the people.
Samdech Krala Hom considers the death of Samdech Udom Tep Nhean Hun Neng to be not only the loss of her beloved husband, father and grandfather, the incomparable love of Lok Chumteav Leav Vuoch Chheng and her family, but also the loss of The last condolences of a high-ranking official.
He emphasized that Samdech Udom Tep Nhean has always served the nation, religion, and the King, and has contributed to the creation of many achievements and achievements, contributing to the restoration and development of the society for decades to the end of life.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng and Lok Chumteav Nhem Sakhorn Sar Kheng and their families, as well as leaders and officials of the Ministry of Interior, dedicated their lives to pray for the body of Samdech Udom Tep Nhean Hun Neng to go to heaven in peace.
It should be noted that the body of Samdech Udom Tep Nhean Hun Neng was presided over by the family under the presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen. May 2022. Samdech Techo Hun Sen Calls for 5 Points on the 28th Anniversary of the International Family Day 2022
