(Phnom Penh): In an interview with VOD on the afternoon of May 8, Chhim Sithor, known as the expired union leader at NagaWorld, said that NagaWorld refused to accept the union's request to 200 workers returned to work as an intention to dissolve the union. Not only that, this political activist even accused and painted the Ministry of Labor as a compromise for the NagaWorld boss who achieved his goal.
Now let's take a look back at the root of the problem at NagaWorld. The company has announced the layoffs of some employees it deems necessary to cut costs in the wake of the Kovid-19 crisis, which has hit the company hard.
Legal organizations that understand the law require employers to provide reasonable compensation under the labor law in the event of a layoff. However, Chhim Sithor's union refused to resign when his employer fired him and refused to accept legal compensation. This is the core of the problem that has dragged on the controversy to this day.
According to the media, in fact, the Ministry of Labor has tried to facilitate the talks almost 10 times, but the solution is still not possible due to the false proposals and demands of the union led by political activist Chhim Sithor. You.
The political activist also said that the 200 employees could replace the 300 workers who volunteered to leave. "Can any company in the world allow unions to recruit people to replace their employees?"
This is the result of a former union leader who is ignorant of the law and mentally retarded.
