More than 4 km of concrete line connecting Preah Ponlea commune to Koh Pong Sat commune, Serey Sophorn city, donated by Deputy Prime Minister Ke Kim Yan
(Banteay Meanchey): A concrete road with a length of more than 4 km connecting Ta Tong village in Preah Ponlea commune to Angka Bos village, Koh Pong Sat commune, Serey Sophorn city will be officially opened this morning, May 10, 2022, as a gift Deputy Prime Minister Ke Kim Yan, Chairman of the National Authority for Combating Drugs and Chairman of the Royal Government Working Group to Assist Banteay Meanchey Province and his wife.
The groundbreaking ceremony was presided over by Mr. Oum Rath, Governor of Banteay Meanchey Province, and was attended by Mr. Hul Raya, Governor of Serey Sophorn City, as well as some relevant departments and institutions.
According to Mr. Oum Rath, this concrete road will be completed before the rainy season.
On the occasion of the opening of the road construction site, Mr. Oum Rath also instructed the technical team and the construction contractor to work hard to complete the work according to the set plan.
On the opening day of the concrete road construction site, the people living in both districts of Serei Sophorn City expressed their deep gratitude to Deputy Prime Minister Ke Kim Yan and his wife for taking care of the well-being and living conditions of the people. "There is a way, there is hope," he said. Good young people unite to support drug eradication! Nationwide drug crackdown on May 10: 22 cases cracked, 48 arrested
