NEC: 17 Political Parties Deploy More Than 80,000 Agents to Observe Commune / Sangkat Council Election
(Phnom Penh): According to the report from the Capital and Provincial Election Commission, the official results of the political party agents requesting to register to observe the election process and the counting of ballots for the 5th Commune / Sangkat Council Election 2022, a total of 88 , 050 people, of which 26,155 were women. This is according to the press release received by Fresh News on May 10, 2022.
According to the NEC, according to the regulations and procedures for the 5th Mandate Commune / Sangkat Council Election 2022, political parties that have been recognized to register as agents to observe the election process and count the ballots have the right to change. Its agents until 17:30 the day before election day.
Commune / Sangkat councilors, candidates, village chiefs, assistant village chiefs, village guards and the armed forces are not allowed to act as agents of political parties, observe the election process and count the ballots.
It should be noted that the political party agents who observe the Commune / Sangkat Council election process must respect the relevant laws and regulations in force and adhere to the code of conduct for political parties, candidates and agents of political parties in the election process.
Land disputes lead to violence! Brother-in-law and sister-in-law seriously injured in Romduol district, Svay Rieng province
(Svay Rieng): The story of a family land dispute led to the use of violence by a brother who cut his sister and brother-in-law, a French man, causing injuries at 8:30 pm on May 9, 2022 At Thna village, Thna Thnong commune, Romduol district.
Eyewitnesses said that before the incident, the suspect and his sister were seen having a verbal dispute over land, leading to violence.
At that time, the suspect pulled out an ax, cut his brother-in-law and sister-in-law, woke up the family and the villagers, came out and detained them, then reported to the police to intervene and detained the suspect for questioning.
Currently, the authorities have sent the suspect to the district police inspectorate for legal action. Mr. Oknha Ou Chhay, Honorary Vice President of the Cambodian Red Cross Branch in Phnom Penh, donated 20,000 USD on the occasion of the 159th Anniversary of the World Red Cross and Red Crescent Day, May 8, 2022
