(Phnom Penh): Cambodian students in the People's Republic of China organized a talk and solidarity meal to celebrate the 5th anniversary of the founding of the Cambodian Students Association in the People's Republic of China (May 11, 2017 - May 11, 2022) under the chairmanship of Mr. Yok Nguy, Secretary of State Dr. Hang Chuon Naron, Minister of Education, Youth and Sports, Mr. Lin Ruihua, Cultural Adviser of the Embassy of the People's Republic of China in Cambodia.
The event was also attended by a total of 230 Chinese companies, Chinese friends, Chinese friends, alumni and alumni, which was held at the headquarters of the Khmer-Chinese Association in Cambodia.
Ms. Hor Reaksmey, President of the Student Association of the 5th Mandate, read the report on the activities and achievements of the Student Association in the past. She also expressed her interest in local students' online study for the past five semesters and encouraged Cambodian students to continue their studies for their own future and to be a part of it. Building our nation.
Mr. Ou Vuthy, Founder and Chairman of the Board of the Student Association, spoke about the history of the establishment of the Student Association with some achievements and achievements, especially the contribution of the Royal Government in the fight against Kovid 19 through joint vaccination. Prevent Kovid 19 by the Cambodian-Chinese Friendship Youth Volunteer Doctors Association of the Student Association.
At the same time, the Chairman of the Board also highlighted the role of the association that has been implemented:
Mr. Ou Vuthy, on behalf of the Founders of the Students' Association, also thanked the Prime Minister, Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, President of the Senate, Dr. Hun Manet, and the Chinese Embassy in Cambodia. China, Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation and the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce to support the activities of the student association in the past.
Lin Ruihua, Cultural Adviser of the Chinese Embassy in Cambodia, praised the student association, which is made up of a group of young people who are energetic and creative.
He highly valued the student association, which is gradually becoming the backbone of Cambodia's economic and social development, and the builder and promoter of Sino-Cambodian friendly relations in the new era.
He also brought great attention from Chinese and Cambodian leaders, supported the work of the Cambodian Students Association in China and promoted exchanges between the two countries' youths, helped young entrepreneurs and pledged to continue. Create more opportunities for Cambodian students to study in China.
At the same time, the Embassy of the People's Republic of China hopes that the Student Association will organize more activities to promote cultural exchanges between China and Cambodia, as well as contribute to further enhancing understanding and friendship between the two peoples.
He supported and encouraged the association to continue its activities, such as disseminating information more widely, so that all Cambodian students, both scholarship and paid students who go to study in China, know and participate in registration. Members of the Association. Good communication with Chinese people, especially investors who are willing and able to invest in Cambodia.
He also shared the well-being and experience of members who face difficulties or difficulties in studying and staying in China to help all students successfully complete their studies and take that knowledge together to develop the nation. Share and provide information to the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports and other relevant institutions in case of problems affecting our students (such as the case of the outbreak of Kovid 19).
He also thanked the Government of China for helping to train human resources in Cambodia and continue to provide scholarships to more and more Cambodian students from year to year, and thanked the Chairman of the Board, President of the Cambodian Students Association in the Republic. The Chinese people celebrated the five-year anniversary. Duke Kith Meng shows investment potential in Cambodia to US business community
(Phnom Penh): Duke Kith Meng, President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, led a delegation from the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce to organize a Cambodia-US business meeting between representatives of the American business community and a delegation from the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce on the afternoon of May 9. May 2022 in New York, USA.
The event also included interventions on the Cambodian business and economic environment by a delegation from the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce to present business and investment opportunities in Cambodia to the American business community.
At the same time, the American Business Community also prepared an intervention on US business and investment opportunities for the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce delegation.
Duke Kith Meng told the American business community about the many potential that US companies can invest in Cambodia as the Royal Government of Cambodia opens its economy to national and international investors.
The tycoon also told the American business community that the Royal Government of Cambodia's efforts to vaccinate more than 93 percent of Cambodia's 16 million people are a good sign for investment in Cambodia.
In addition, Duke Kith Meng also mentioned that Cambodia has free trade with some countries, which is a good opportunity for investors to export goods to the world.
Representatives of the American business community also welcomed the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce delegation, which was a good opportunity for investors to meet. Representatives of the American business community also expressed interest in the investment potential in Cambodia and expressed willingness to work with Cambodian investors to find investment opportunities.
With the permission of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, Duke Kith Meng led a delegation from the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce on a business visit to the United States from May 8 to 15, 2022. Accompanying Samdech Techo Hun Sen to the US-ASEAN Summit and related summits to be held in Washington DC, USA.
