Ministry of Environment Continues Training for Judicial Police Officers and Law Enforcement Officers of Kampot and Kep Provincial Departments of Environment
(Kampot): The Ministry of Environment continued to provide training to 45 judicial police officers and law enforcement officers of the Department of Environment of Kampot and Kep Provinces on Guidelines on Standard Procedures and Procedures for Investigation and Preparation of Cases Offenses and money laundering offenses within the jurisdiction of the Ministry of Environment.
The training course will be held on May 10, 2022 at Kampot Provincial Department of Environment under the chairmanship of Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Secretary of State and Permanent Deputy Chairman of the Anti-Money Laundering and Terrorist Financing Working Group of the Ministry of Environment, with a presentation by officials. Related Skills
On that occasion, the Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment said that this training is very important for judicial police officers and law enforcement officers of the Ministry of Environment to strengthen the capacity to participate in the fight against money laundering and terrorist financing in the original crime related to resource crimes. Nature, especially crimes related to forestry and illegal wildlife trade.
Mr. Pheaktra said that judicial police officers would be prosecuted for money laundering and terrorist financing in the event that there were clues related to money laundering in the original case related to natural resource crimes.
The training provided judicial police officers and law enforcement officers of the Department of Environment with legal documents and gained experience in case-building related to money laundering as well as case investigation procedures.
Mr. Pheaktra said that according to the plan, more than 1,200 judicial police officers and law enforcement officers of the Ministry of Environment will be trained to strengthen this capacity.
