China calls G7 concerns over Hong Kong election's interference in internal affairs
BEIJING: A Chinese Foreign Ministry spokesman said on Tuesday that G7 concerns over Hong Kong's election process were interfering in China's internal affairs. This is according to the publication of Reuters on Tuesday, May 10, 2022.
In a statement issued on Monday, the G7 stressed "serious concerns about fundamental freedoms in Hong Kong, especially the election of a new leader of Hong Kong, which is in stark contrast to the purpose of the election." Globalization will further undermine the rights of Hong Kong people to make decisions to elect their leaders.
But Chinese Foreign Ministry spokesman Zhao Lijian told a daily news conference that "a number of Western countries and institutions have deliberately conspired to pollute Hong Kong's presidential election. "This is interference in China's internal affairs, and China must strongly oppose and strongly condemn." He added that those countries were not paying attention to the improvement of Hong Kong democracy.
