Youth group: Increasing tobacco tax as a contribution to help the nation to collect taxes and reduce deaths due to tobacco
(Phnom Penh): A group of five winners claim that the increase in tobacco tax is not a reason for tax evasion, but rather a contribution to the Royal Government and the collection of state tax revenue to help Support the country's economy and reduce deaths due to tobacco use.
The youth group also claimed that the tobacco tax increase was not the reason for the smuggling of cigarettes, that is, the idea that the tobacco tax increase would lead to the smuggling of cigarettes was just a claim by tobacco companies to deceive. The public and policymakers only aim to prevent tax increases.
The increase in tobacco taxes has enormous benefits, with the government benefiting from state tax revenues to support the country's economy, especially after massive expenditures for the prevention of Kovid-19, and raising tobacco taxes. Mortality caused by reduced tobacco use, as well as contributing to protecting the environment from tobacco production and use.
According to a UNDP study, if Cambodia raises the tariff to 75% of the retail price of cigarettes in accordance with the recommendations of the World Health Organization and the World Bank, Cambodia will receive an additional $ 235 million in income tax. Over the next five years and 933 million US dollars over the next 15 years and help reduce the death rate, illness and disability of the people, this is the additional proposal of the candidates.
The five youths also stated that the use of tobacco products is a burden for the government to solve because the use of tobacco products causes people to get sick and die, of which about 15,000 Cambodians died due to smoking. Not only that, tobacco use costs about 649 million US dollars, equivalent to 3 percent of Cambodia's gross domestic product.
