Minister Suy Sem Inaugurates Power Transmission Lines in Koh Kong, Kampong Cham and Kratie Provinces
(Koh Kong): Mr. Suy Sem, Minister of Mines and Energy, on May 10, 2022, led a delegation to inaugurate the transmission and distribution projects in Koh Kong, Kampong Cham and Kratie provinces within the framework of concessional loans from the French Republic and Grant from the European Union through the French Agency for Development.
The ceremony was also attended by Mr. Jacques Bolle, French Ambassador to Cambodia and Ms. Mithona Phuthong, Governor of Koh Kong Province, as well as government officials from all institutions, teachers, students and people.
Speaking on the occasion, Mr. Suy Sem said that within the framework of Cambodia's economic development policy, the Royal Government of Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen has been promoting full development in all areas, including infrastructure development projects and development projects. Local equipment factories to develop power supply in Cambodia.
The Minister said that the development of the above power sector is to develop Cambodia into a country with sufficient electricity supply, sustainable, reliable, high quality and affordable for all types of consumers everywhere in the country. It is the main and most necessary factor to support the economic and social development as well as to provide the well-being of the people.
In this regard, the Royal Government has entrusted the Ministry of Mines and Energy and Electricity of Cambodia to develop energy sector development plans and raise funds from development partners as well as the private sector for the construction of electricity infrastructure to ensure adequate and efficient electricity supply. Quality, stability, sustainability, affordability and minimize the impact on the environment and society.
At the same time, Mr. Jacques Baller said that as the French Ambassador to Cambodia, he was proud of France's participation (AFD) in the energy sector, which is one of the key events of our power transmission and distribution project. It was officially inaugurated today with the aim of improving reliable energy in three provinces.
He added that the project shows the good long-term relationship that the Ministry of Mines and Energy and Electricity of Cambodia has built AFD in the coming years to support Cambodia's electricity strategy, development and strengthening of the element network. To improve access to electricity for the benefit of all Cambodians. He also thanked the Royal Government of Cambodia and the French Republic for their excellent cooperation.
