United States proposes UN Security Council meeting on North Korea
The United States has called for a UN Security Council meeting this week to discuss North Korea as Washington pushes for a top body, US officials said Monday. The 15-nation bloc has strengthened sanctions against Pyongyang. This is according to a quote from Al-Jazeera on Tuesday, May 10, 2022.
North Korea has stepped up its missile launches in recent months, raising concerns in neighboring countries and the United States, and as chair of the Security Council for May, Washington is considering proposing A meeting on North Korea has been scheduled since last week, set for Wednesday the 11th at 3pm (New York time).
North Korea has been under UN sanctions since 2006, and the US-backed Security Council has stepped up efforts to cut off funding or aid against Pyongyang's nuclear and missile programs.
