Ministry of Foreign Affairs issues press release on Samdech Techo Hun Sen to lead high-level delegation to ASEAN-US Special Summit in Washington
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation on May 9, 2022 issued a press release on Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Chair of ASEAN 2022 and will lead a high-level delegation to participate and co Chairman of the ASEAN-US Special Summit to Commemorate the 45th Anniversary of the ASEAN-US Dialogue Partnership in Washington, DC, May 12-13, 2022
Prime Minister Hun Sen was accompanied by Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation Sun Chanthol, Senior Minister of Public Works and Transport, Minister Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce Dr. Hang Chuon Naron. Minister of Education, Youth and Sports and other senior officials of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
During the summit, Prime Minister Hun Sen, along with other ASEAN leaders, will be welcomed and invited to a luncheon with US lawmakers from both Republicans and Democrats. Nancy Pelosi, Speaker of the U.S. House of Representatives, will be welcomed and invited to a dinner hosted by White House President Joe Biden at the White House.
ASEAN leaders will also meet with US business leaders to discuss economic cooperation. ASEAN leaders will welcome and meet with US Vice President Kamala Harris for a plenary session with US Ministers on climate change measures, clean energy and sustainable infrastructure.
Discussions, exchanging views on regional and international issues and taking the ASEAN-US partnership to the next level are the main topics of the summit.
Prime Minister Hun Sen will also hold bilateral meetings with Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh of the Socialist Republic of Vietnam and leaders of other ASEAN member states.
Samdech Techo Prime Minister Hun Sen will also meet with Cambodians living in the United States.
