(Preah Sihanouk): The construction of Wat Kiri Chulsa Koh Rong Temple has started the construction process according to the decision of Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior "On the establishment of the construction committee of Wat Kiri Chulsa Koh Rong" On May 9, 2022, Mrs. Nhem Sakhorn Sar Kheng, Chairman of the Construction Committee, presided over the groundbreaking ceremony.
Please be reminded that "Wat Kiri Chulsar Koh Rong" was built during 1993 on an area of nearly 5 hectares in Prek Svay village, Koh Rong commune, Koh Rong city, Sihanoukville province, on Koh Rong, a tourist island. One of the many tourist attractions of Sihanoukville. As of 2022, Wat Kiri Chulsa (Koh Rong) is 29 years old and has seven chief priests.
But what is interesting is that this pagoda only has a wooden pavilion for monks to live in, there is no church, synagogue, fence, gate, mortuary, as well as other achievements to be as beautiful as other temples. . On the other hand, this pagoda is a temple for more than 900 families living on Koh Rong to perform rituals.
Mr. Cheam Him, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Rural Development, said that the construction of "Wat Kiri Chulsar Koh Rong" must be completed 100 percent as planned and canceled or left. The purpose of this construction is to promote and support Buddhism and the development of tourism for Koh Rong, Sihanoukville. In addition, the construction also considers the history of the area as well as increase the attraction of both national and international tourists to visit.
