Kratie Provincial Working Group Continues to Participate in Public Forum on Safe Village-Commune Policy in Svay Chres Commune, Snoul District
(Snuol-Kratie): Mr. Prum Sokha, Minister of Public Works and Chairman of Kratie Provincial Working Group, together with his colleagues, participated in a public forum to monitor the implementation of safe village-commune policy in Svay Chres Commune, Snuol District, Kratie Province.
This forum was held on the morning of May 6, 2022 at Svay Chreah Commune Hall, Snoul District, Kratie Province, with the participation of you, the Chairman of the Provincial Council, the Chairman-Deputy Chairman of the Provincial Working Group to assist the 6 communes in Snuol district, provincial and district competent officials, commune councilors, commune chiefs, clerks, 16 village chiefs in Svay Chres commune, as well as local authority officials, a total of more than 200 participants.
After listening to the report of Mr. Khieu Sokha, Chief of Svay Chres Commune on the general situation in Svay Chres Commune, Minister Prum Sokha, Chairman of Kratie Provincial Working Group, opened the public forum, emphasizing the importance of organizing this forum with the purpose of understanding From the difficulties at the local level to work together to solve the challenges ahead in time for the benefit of the local people.
The Minister thanked and appreciated the active participation of the people in Svay Chres commune with people across the country in full support of the Royal Government under the wise guide of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister. Of the Kingdom of Cambodia, which led the national movement to fight Kovid-19 can bring the society back to normal as it is today.
At the same time, Minister Prum Sokha also encouraged all people to come and receive the third and fourth doses, which are the boosting dose to continue to strengthen community immunity, support the strong sustainability of socio-economic launch. Our nation goes to the future.
In the open program to participate in discussions to solve local problems that are concerns, prejudices directly related to the daily lives of the people, the forum received some suggestions during that time, including:
1. Delays in the provision of public services in the commune, especially in relation to civil registration, identification, family books and other documents
2. The quality of health services at the commune health center has not fully responded to the necessary requests of local people.
3. The impact of public road transport caused by many marble companies on people's daily lives has not been well addressed.
4. Effectiveness in cracking down on drug and gambling crimes in villages and communes is limited
The above issues were explained, clarified and promised to be resolved by the director of the health center, the commune chief, the police chief, the commune administration, representatives of private companies and other relevant authorities.
Closing remarks, Minister Prum Sokha, Chairman of Kratie Provincial Working Group, praised the results of the current public forum, which served as a bridge between the state and the people in contributing to the relief of problems. In particular, some concerns and prejudices of local people around the implementation of the policy of safe villages and communes.
