Today, Cambodia-Thailand reopened through Choam International Gate in Anlong Veng District, Oddar Meanchey Province after being closed for more than 2 years due to Kovid disease
(Oddar Meanchey): Choam International Gate in Cheung Phnom Village, Trapeang Prey Commune, Anlong Veng District, Oddar Meanchey Province was reopened for people to cross at 11 am on May 9, 2022. This one was temporarily closed by the Thai side for more than two years due to the global spread of Kovid 19 virus.
The official reopening of the Choam International Gate was held in the presence of Mr. Pen Kosal, Governor of Oddar Meanchey Province, and Mr. Vath Tha Navutthichat, Governor of Sisaket Province, Thailand, and other relevant officials of the Armed Forces of the two countries.
It should be noted that before reaching the reopening of the Choam International Gate this morning, the Cambodian-Thai side, led by the provincial governors of the two countries (Oddar Meanchey-Sisaket), met to discuss the principles and Some conditions are in accordance with the instructions of the heads of government of the two countries.
Regarding the principles and conditions set by the Thai side for Cambodians wishing to enter Thailand, Mr. Pen Kosal also requested the Thai side to help reduce and add some points.
Please note that the opening of the international border checkpoint today, Cambodia-Thailand has been identified as a temporary test opening, if the opening of this checkpoint goes smoothly without any problems, the Thai side will cancel some other conditions in order to The influx of people from both countries has returned to normal, as before the Kovid-19 crisis.
