China says it is conducting military exercises near Taiwan (Video inside) (Shanghai): The People's Liberation Army (PLA) said on Monday that its forces held military exercises near Taiwan last week to develop operations. Fighting broke out after Taipei claimed that several Chinese warplanes had flown into its air defense zone. This is according to the publication of the news agency on Monday, May 9, 2022.
The navy and air force held joint military exercises from Friday to Sunday this weekend in the eastern and southern parts of the country, the commander of the Eastern People's Liberation Army (PLA) said in a statement. Southwest of Taiwan. "The exercise is designed to test and improve the joint combat capabilities of the Chinese navy and air force," the statement added.
According to the Taiwanese Ministry of Defense, China has deployed bombers, fighter jets and anti-submarine aircraft, but there has been no actual test firing, and Chinese warplanes have not flown into its airspace. Fly into the Air Defense Identification Zone (ADIZ).
For the past two years, Taiwan has strongly opposed the frequent Chinese military action near its territory in the face of repeated warnings from Beijing that it will not hesitate to do so. The use of military force on Taiwan if necessary.
