Mr. Sbong Sarath and Mr. Steng Sokhom inaugurated the new headquarters of the Cambodian People's Party in 2 communes and talked with about 1,400 party members in Kamchay Mear district
The party headquarters is an important location for party leaders and members in each commune to serve the party and the people. Kamchay Mear district has 8 communes through the party working group led by Mr. Steng Sokhom, so far these 8 communes have already built the party headquarters.
The newly inaugurated party headquarters in North Smaong and Daun Keung communes cost nearly $ 140,000. This budget is used to buy land, build buildings and equip other facilities.
At the inauguration ceremony, Mr. Sbong Sarath and Mr. Steung Sokhom welcomed the presence of the two new party headquarters and thanked Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng for providing support for the construction of both party offices.
Mr. Sbong Sarath and Mr. Steung Sokhom called the presence of the CPP headquarters a testament to the strength of the CPP at the grassroots level and provided a suitable location for its leaders and members for its operations. Party that is beneficial for the nation and the people as well.
In this conversation, Mr. Steng Sokhom brought a message from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian People's Party and Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Vice President of the Cambodian People's Party to all party members who participated in Ceremony.
Mr. Steng Sokhom also highlighted the efforts of the Royal Government of Cambodia led by the Cambodian People's Party to lead and build the nation. In particular, efforts to control and combat the spread of Kovid 19 have been so successful that there were no Kovid 19 cases on May 7.
Mr. Steng Sokhom emphasized that this success did not happen by itself, but was a result of the launch of a clear and quick measures and plans of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and his staff. In particular, the launch of the Kovid 19 vaccination campaign.
"Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian People's Party and the leaders of the Cambodian People's Party, which is leading the Royal Government, he worked very hard to achieve such results. This result is highly appreciated both nationally and internationally. "It is our pride to have leaders who take our physical and mental well-being into account." This is the emphasis of Mr. Steng Sokhom.
Mr. Steng Sokhom also outlined the political line as well as the policy of the Cambodian People's Party in providing services to the people as well as local development in the past four terms. Through this policy, administrative services have been accelerated and local development, such as the construction of roads and the construction of various irrigation systems, has facilitated travel and access to irrigation, farming and cropping. Other.
The chairman of the working group of the Cambodian People's Party in Kamchay Mear district highlighted that through these policies, the lives of the people have been improved and the people have been given more confidence in the leadership of the CPP. Cambodians. Mr. Steng Sokhom affirmed that the policy of local development and promoting the well-being of the people is still a priority of the Cambodian People's Party.
Separately, Mr. Sbong Sarath raised the issue of the 5th Commune / Sangkat Council Election, which will be held on June 5, 2022. Mr. Sbong Sarath instructed the leaders and team leaders in each commune to pay attention and hold on to the information of the members in the commune.
Mr. Sbong Sarath also instructed party members in each commune to be ready to go to the polls on June 5. In particular, prepare documents for the election, such as ID cards.
According to the election results, John Lee received 1,416 votes, more than enough to become Hong Kong's new head of government. Hong Kong's election law stipulates that in order to run for Hong Kong's chief executive, a candidate must garner 750 or more votes, half of the 1,500-member commission.
After being appointed by the Beijing government, John Lee will be sworn in as Hong Kong's new chief executive on July 1, with a five-year term from July 1. 2022 to June 30, 2027. Carrie Lam, current Hong Kong chief executive, also sent a congratulatory message on John Lee's victory.
In 2019, Lee was promoted to head of Hong Kong security under the administration led by Kerry Lam as Hong Kong faced student-led protests and later became the second most influential person in Hong Kong after Kerry. Lam in 2021.
John Lee is one of a number of senior Hong Kong officials on the US blacklist who have accused him of contributing to the destruction of Hong Kong's autonomy and democracy by cracking down on it. Demonstrators support democracy. But Lee has denied the allegations and said that what he did was to fulfill his role as a security guard.
