Taiwan hopes international sanctions on China if invaded
Speaking to reporters in Taipei during the European Day event, Wu said it was important to stand with them in condemning the aggression in Ukraine as well as sanctions on Russia and Belarus.
"In the future, if we are threatened by China or invaded, we certainly hope the international community can understand and support Taiwan and punish such acts," he added. This. Wu stressed that this is why Taiwan now stands with the international community in imposing sanctions on Russia.
In the past, Taipei has joined Western-led sanctions on Russia for invading Ukraine, and Taiwan also imposed sanctions on Belarus on Friday. However, Taiwan's actions appear to be symbolic, with little direct influence, as Taipei has a low level of direct trade with Russia and Belarus.
Since the start of the war in Ukraine, Taiwan has stepped up its vigilance amid fears China could seize similar actions on the island, but so far the Taipei government has reported no. No sign of a Chinese attack.
Regarding the question of how the international community will react to China's attack on Taiwan, no one can predict for sure, as most countries, even the United States and all EU members, have ties. Official diplomacy with Beijing is not with Taipei, and unlike Ukraine, they do not consider Taiwan a country.
