There are three major results that Myanmar has achieved after the ASEAN Humanitarian Assistance Meeting initiated by Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia and Special Envoy of the ASEAN Chair on Myanmar, and Mr. Lim Chok Huy, Secretary-General of ASEAN in the role of ASEAN Humanitarian Coordinator, co-chaired the meeting. Consultation on ASEAN Humanitarian Assistance for Myanmar in person in Phnom Penh and on video.
A press release issued by the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of Cambodia, Fresh News stated that the meeting discussed three main topics, including: 1) ASEAN Humanitarian Assistance Framework, 2) Addressing Challenges Humanitarian assistance operations; and 3) the framework for the management of the Kovid-19 vaccine in Myanmar.
The Ministry of Foreign Affairs confirmed the results of the three main talks that are of interest to Myanmar:
Regarding the first point, the ASEAN Humanitarian Assistance Framework, the Meeting agreed that the ASEAN Coordinating Center for Humanitarian Aid on Disaster Management (AHA), in close consultation with the Myanmar Working Group on Humanitarian Assistance Will determine the location of states and regions for the implementation of this framework. Those states and territories include Kayah, Kayin, Macedonia, and Pago.
The meeting also welcomed the commitment of the Myanmar Humanitarian Assistance Team to allow the AHA to assess the joint needs and implement the second phase in hard-to-reach areas.
