Battambang Police Arrest Two Drug Dealers and Two Weapons
(Battambang): Anti-Drug Bureau of Battambang Provincial Police arrested two drug suspects and some exhibits to the provincial court for legal action after the crackdown on May 6, 2022 at the village. Takuy, Sangkat Kdol Daun Teav, Battambang Municipality, Battambang Province.
Colonel Sok Nimol, Director of the Anti-Drug Bureau, led the force under the guidance of Major General Sat Kimsan, Provincial Police Commissioner, in cooperation with the Anti-Crime Intervention Team to crack down on drug trafficking cases. Actual offenses.
Authorities identified the suspect as 36-year-old Hout Savy, a resident of Sous Ey village, Peam Ek commune, Ek Phnom district, Battambang province. At that time, the specialized force searched and found exhibits including 8 bags of methamphetamine (ICE), 1 mobile phone, 1 scale for weighing drugs for sale and 1 bag for sharing drug ports and equipment. Some drugs.
Through the investigation and with the coordination of Mr. Keo Socheat, Prosecutor of the Battambang Provincial Prosecutor's Office, on the same day, the specialized police continued the operation to arrest another accomplice named Seng Sovannara alias Tou, 33 years old, temporarily staying in the village. Romchek 4, Sangkat Rattanak, Battambang City, Battambang Province, confiscated 2 firearms (rubber bullet), 1 mobile phone and some drug paraphernalia.
The two suspects and the exhibits are currently being processed by the Anti-Drug Bureau and sent to the provincial court on the morning of May 7 for legal action. Croatia is interested in investing in the electric vehicle processing industry Development of international ports and tourism in Cambodia
