After the ceremony, Mr. Dy Rath Khemrun brought the budget of the working group to give 116 party members 20,000 Riels each. Cambodia, Australia hold 3rd high-level consultation
(Phnom Penh): The third High-Level Consultation between Cambodia and Australia was held on May 5, 2022 in Canberra, Australia, with Ms. Tuot Panha, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia; Katrina Cooper, Under Secretary of State for Foreign Affairs and Trade of Australia, co-chaired the meeting.
A statement from the Cambodian Ministry of Foreign Affairs stated that both sides expressed satisfaction over the long-standing and mature relationship, which was overshadowed by the two peoples' satisfaction as the two countries celebrated their anniversary. 70 of the establishment of diplomatic relations this year.
In terms of development cooperation, the Australian side reaffirmed its commitment to provide official development assistance to Cambodia in support of infrastructure, agriculture, education and health, which contribute to Cambodia's socio-economic development.
The two sides also agreed to continue to enhance people-to-people contacts through the New Colombo Plan and the Australian Volunteer Program, which strengthen mutual understanding and exchange of experiences. Recognizing that Cambodia is a popular destination for Australian students to intern and recognizing that Australia is a popular destination for Cambodian students to continue their studies, both sides agreed to encourage such a trend further.
In addition to bilateral relations, the two sides also exchanged views on regional and international cooperation of common interests and concerns, including the Russia-Ukraine issue, the Myanmar issue and the South China Sea issue.
For the Mekong-Australia Partnership, Cambodia values Australia's long-term vision for the Mekong region by promoting human resource development, economic resilience, trade and investment, environmental resilience and internet and technology capacity building. Important as stated in the Mekong-Australia Partnership.
For ASEAN cooperation, the Australian side reaffirmed its support for Cambodia's ASEAN chairmanship in 2022. Cambodia is grateful for Australia's unwavering support for ASEAN Community Building Efforts, Regional Economic Recovery Assistance in the wake of the Kovid-19 Crisis, and commitment to the ASEAN Community through Australia's active participation in the mechanism. ASEAN-led.
The two sides welcomed the entry into force of the Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement in January this year and are ready to implement it. The two sides look forward to concluding negotiations to upgrade the ASEAN-Australia-New Zealand Free Trade Agreement soon.
The meeting was held in a cordial atmosphere, with honest discussions and mutual understanding, reflecting the common desire to strengthen and expand cooperation between Cambodia and Australia in both bilateral and multilateral frameworks. . The Cambodian and Australian sides have agreed to hold the fourth Senior Ministerial Consultation in 2023 in Cambodia.
Ministry of Foreign Affairs issues press release on the outcome of the ASEAN Humanitarian Assistance Consultation Meeting for Myanmar
The Consultative Meeting, held on 6 May 2022, was initiated by Cambodia as the chair of ASEAN in 2022 in cooperation with the ASEAN Secretary-General as part of the implementation of the Agreement. 5 points unanimously.
The meeting was attended by Ms. Joy Sam Suya, UN Under-Secretary-General for Humanitarian Affairs and Deputy Coordinating Officer for Emergency Relief, and senior representatives from all ASEAN member countries, including the Myanmar Working Group. Humanitarian Charter, UN Specialized Agency, ASEAN External Partners and relevant international organizations in Myanmar.
A press release from the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of Cambodia stated that the meeting discussed three main topics, including: 1) the ASEAN Humanitarian Assistance Framework, 2) addressing challenges related to humanitarian assistance operations, and 3 ) Framework for the Management of Kovid-19 Vaccine in Myanmar.
The Myanmar Humanitarian Assistance Team will also work with the Solidarity and Peace Building Committee to ensure that humanitarian aid is delivered to communities in Myanmar, including areas of ethnic armed groups. A more detailed plan to implement this framework will be prepared by the AHA Center and the Myanmar Humanitarian Assistance Team.
The AHA, in consultation with the Ministry of Health of Myanmar, will identify and verify areas and locations for Kovid-19 vaccination, as well as identify operational partners to support vaccine management in Myanmar. The meeting also welcomed the Myanmar Ministry of Health's commitment to tax exemptions and facilitation of vaccine imports into Myanmar.
