Russey Keo District Administration and Phnom Penh Land Management Department Announce Systematic Land Registration Judgment Area to Prepare for the Issuance of Title Certificates to Sangkat Chrang Chamres I
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Ek Khun Doeun, Governor of Russey Keo District, and Mr. Peng Ratana, Director of the Department of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction of Phnom Penh, presided over a ceremony to declare a systematic land registration area to prepare for the issuance of title deeds to residents in Phnom Penh. In the village 1-2-3-4 of Sangkat Chrang Chamres I, Khan Russey Keo on the morning of April 6, 2022.
Please note that the land registration and the issuance of title deeds have two procedures: registration at the request of the landowner, which is called "separate registration" and registration of one commune at a time. The government's definition of so-called "registration is systematic."
After the fall of the Khmer Rouge regime, all land titles throughout the country were lost. The law provides for the abolition of all pre-1979 ownership regimes. In order to prepare for the construction of land registers and the re-issuance of land titles nationwide, the law sets out to establish a special procedure for "systematic land registration."
Systematic land registration is the registration of land that comes from a government initiative without the need for a landowner. The government determines which villages or communes are required to register land. This systematic land registration procedure is divided into five main stages, including:
* Third: Disseminate the authority to make public the cadastral plan and the list of land owners so that the relevant people can inspect and protest for correction if there is a wrong place.
However, in the registration process, if there is any dispute, such as a border dispute, the parties to the dispute can ask the Administrative Commission to help resolve and mediate without having to go to court.
* Fourth: Judging and deciding this stage is relevant only to state institutions. After the 30-day protest period, the competent official shall examine the cadastral plan and the list of land owners to be registered in the land register. Any land that is not in dispute and does not belong to the state will be registered in the land register and the director of the provincial / municipal land department will sign the final title deed.
* 5th: Card distribution is the last stage. After the authorities sign and issue the cards, these cards will be distributed to the landowners. The landowner has to go and get the title in person, and this title is a final title deed.
Please be informed that although the systematic registration has not been completed nationwide, separate registration at the request of the landowner is still possible at the same time.
NEC Introduces Ballot Printing Process to Political Parties
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of May 6, 2022, Mr. Prach Chan, Chairman of the National Election Committee (NEC), inspected the ballot printing process for the Commune / Sangkat Council Election. 5 2022 at Navin Printing Ek Printing House, located at # 9, Street 345, Sangkat Boeung Kak I, Khan Toul Kork, Phnom Penh.
Mr. Prach Chan confirmed that today, the NEC has invited all parties involved in the election to observe and observe the process of printing ballots directly. He added that as with previous elections, the NEC always invites all political parties, observers and journalists to inspect and observe the ballot printing process on the spot.
After all parties involved in the election inspected the production line of the ballot printing, Mr. Hang Puthea, Member of the NEC and Chairman of the NEC Spokesperson, informed the media that the ballots were correct. Published 1,652 types, equivalent to 1,652 communes, because each commune has a different number of political parties standing for election.
There are 17 political parties running in the election. Of the 17 political parties, some have registered more than 1,600 communes and some have registered less than 1,000. Therefore, there are different types of ballots depending on the number of political parties registered as candidates and the results of the draw determine the order of the political parties on the ballot.
Mr. Hang Puthea added that there were 9,205,681 registered voters, 23,602 polling stations, and about 11 million ballots to be printed, with about 1 million reserve ballots. Ballots are printed in groups of 50 ballots each.
Mr. Hang Puthea added that the printed ballots were so unique and confidential that no one could falsify them, and that companies bidding through financial procedures had to ensure the security of the NEC. To print ballots.
In this ceremony, representatives of 8 political parties participated in inspecting and observing the chain of ballot printing at the printing house, including the Cambodian People's Party, FUNCINPEC, the Khmer Patriotic Party, the Cambodian Nationality Party, the Cambodian Youth Party, the Khmer Will Party. , Kampuchea Niyum Party, Raksmey Khemara Party and representatives of 9 associations and many journalists, a total of about 40 people.
