18 families in Sangkat Chreav, Siem Reap City ask the authorities to open the road while the landowners are building a fence
(Siem Reap): 18 families, a total of more than 40 people in Phum Khnar, Sangkat Chreav, Siem Reap City, asked the authorities to help solve the problem of opening the sidewalk, while the temporary sidewalk is currently being fenced off by landowners.
According to the complaint of the above group of people, which is being prepared to be submitted to the Siem Reap City Hall, the owner of the plot of land No. 17100602-3139, located in Phum Khnar, Sangkat Chreav, Siem Reap City, has issued an infringing title. On the land of the original road of the people.
With the coordination of the authorities, people were allowed to walk on the road temporarily at the eastern location instead of the central road used since 1984, but at that time, the authorities did not measure the road for the people, claiming that it was just a walkway. Temporary only.
In 2021, fencing began on the road above, but the people living in the back did not ban it, thinking that the authorities and the landowners were already aware of the dispute. Recently, the owner of the land above put up a sign telling people to go in and out, asking to close this road.
The above complaint states that the road closure will affect the traffic in and out, such as going out to do business, go to work, go to school, etc. Citizens ask the mayor to help resolve this chronic dispute and open the way for citizens to get in and out normally.
Regarding this issue, Mr. Kdob Ron, Chief of Chreav Commune, said that this dispute is beyond his capacity and he is waiting for the people's thumbs and other documents to be sent to the mayor to help solve it.
He added that the last owner left the road temporarily and waited for 5 months and there was no solution before they started to announce the closure of this road.
However, on behalf of the authorities, Mr. Kdob Ron asked the relevant parties to understand and tolerate each other to find a good solution for all. Tycoon Un Yuthy and Lok Chumteav Donate $ 2,000 on the Occasion of the 159th Anniversary of the World Red Cross and Red Crescent Day, May 8, 2022
