(Kampong Speu): Lt. Gen. Di Vichea, Deputy Commissioner of the National Police and Director of the Central Security Department, requested the Internal Security Police and the Road Traffic Police to perform their duties professionally to participate in the implementation of the strategic plan as well as National Police Reform Mechanism and the Ministry of Interior Strengthening.
At the Closing Ceremony of the Road Traffic Skills Training and Internal Security Skills Training at the Cambodia-Vietnam Friendship Police School in Kampong Speu Province this morning, May 5, 2022, Lt. Gen. Di Vichea said that on behalf of We, as a force to serve security and order to the people as well as the whole nation, must do something to respect their discipline and professionalism, as in accordance with the reform of the Ministry of Interior as well as the Royal Government.
Lt. Gen. Di Vichea said that the fact that the General Commission of the National Police as well as the Ministry of Interior has provided various training courses to all police forces is to increase skills, competence and professionalism in maintaining security and order to the people. People and the whole nation. In addition, the training is also to better understand the legal basis of the police force.
At the same time, Lt. Gen. Di Vichea also praised all the police forces in the past for their efforts to maintain security and order for the people and the country, especially in the last two years. Work day and night to work with the Royal Government to prevent the spread of Kovid-19 virus successfully from the beginning of the closure until the reopening of the country.
At the Closing Ceremony of the Road Traffic Skills Training and Internal Security Skills Training, Lt. Gen. Di Vichea, Deputy Commissioner General of the National Police and Director of the Central Security Department, also provided some work experience to the trainees. And the maintenance of security, order, research and investigation, and many other tasks assigned by the General Commission of the National Police as well as the Ministry of Interior.
