General Ith Sarath instructs the army not to wear uniforms to participate in the commune council election campaign.
(Kampong Speu): General Ith Sarath, Deputy Commander-in-Chief of the Joint Chiefs of Staff of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, instructed all troops not to use army uniforms to participate in the 2022 5th Mandate Commune / Sangkat Council election and to do the opposite. From the law to make the election fair and just.
This statement was made by General Ith Sarath on the occasion of presiding over the closing ceremony of the training course for the 10th generation of Army officers and the first generation of Chinese language officers at the Army Institute (Tlok Ta Sek), Kampong Speu Province. This morning, May 5, 2022.
General Ith Sarath also reminded the 10th generation Army cadets, the first generation Bachelor of Chinese language training trainees and all generations of cadets who are continuing their internships at the Army Institute. Absolutely loyal to the nation, religion, the King will dare to make all kinds of sacrifices for the cause of defending the motherland for life.
On that occasion, General Ith Sarath continued that the win-win policy set by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia is a great legacy for the nation and the people of Cambodia, and through this win-win policy that has brought A new light of life and society full of development and progress.
General Ith Sarath stated that for the past 23 years, Cambodia has put an end to the civil war in Cambodia and regained peace and national unity after more than 500 years of division in the history of Cambodia.
General Ith Sarath continued that if we compare after the liberation on January 7, 1979 to the present, Cambodia has developed in all areas under the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, built since Yes, empty hands, under the win-win policy of Samdech Techo's national unification, without a winner, there will be no losers, all will win.
General Ith Sarath instructed all officers to remember and understand the words, "Thank you, peace!" Thank you, politics wins! "I am grateful to the founders, the guides and the victorious political operators who bring complete peace and national unity!"
At the same time, General Ith Sarath also stated that peace is invaluable, whether today or the day after. Therefore, it must be protected at any cost.
Mr. Kong Vibol, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Director General of the General Department of Taxation, congratulated the launch of the Nam Samnang Invoice Program and considered the launch of the "Samnang Invoice" program to increase information collection and strengthen the strategy. Collect revenue.
Mr. Kong Vibol said, "The introduction of the Lucky Billing Program is one of the first steps in the implementation of tax measures to strengthen compliance and strengthen sustainable revenue collection." "For this program is like an arrow that shoots more animals by strengthening revenue collection, strengthening the implementation of the bill introduced by the Ministry of Economy and Finance and Tax."
He stated that the introduction of the billing program is for the purpose of collecting information as well as strengthening the compliance already stated in the revenue collection strategy. The Lucky Billing Program will contribute to the potential collection of taxes.
He added that for this lucky invoice, whether people have shopped in shops, whether small or large in Cambodia, have the right to send invoices to participate in this lucky invoice program.
He added that for people who have received invoices from shops with the correct name but not registered for tax, people can still send in the tax invoice program and get a lucky draw. In this case, it is like collecting information for the General Department of Taxation to go to those who have not come to register with the General Department of Taxation to register.
Please be informed that Opennet has faced a debt problem that can not be resolved, so an interim governor has been appointed to take over the company. But now it has been transferred to the Ezecom company of Duke Kith Meng as the owner instead. Ministry of Environment and Administration of Battambang Province Celebrates National and World Environment Day 5 June
(Battambang): The Ministry of Environment and Battambang Provincial Administration celebrated the 29th National and Global Environment Day on June 5, 2022 under the theme "Caring for the Planet for Our Health" on the morning of May 5, 2022 at Neak Santepheap Park. Battambang city.
The ceremony was presided over by Mrs. Prum Sophy, Undersecretary of State of the Ministry of Environment, Representative of Minister Say Sam Al, and a delegation accompanied by Mr. Thou Phea, Deputy Governor of Battambang Province, Representative of Governor Sok Loo, with the participation of leaders, civil servants, departments around the provincial administration. Battambang youth, commune councilors and citizens also participated.
Ms. Prum Sophy said that the Ministry of National and World Environment Day is always celebrated on June 5 every year, especially this year was done ahead of schedule because there is still a lot of work to be done, so the Ministry decided to do it today. In collaboration with the sub-national provincial administration, also facilitated.
She said that this year, the Ministry has set a goal to take Battambang as the venue for this celebration, while Battambang has won the Clean City for consecutive years, and most recently, Battambang has won the ASEAN Clean Place.
