The dollar remained at a 20-year high, dampening interest in overseas gold as 10-year Treasury bond yields rose 3 percent on Monday. For the first time since December 2018.
The Federal Reserve's Federal Open Market Committee will begin its meeting to discuss interest rates and is expected to raise borrowing costs by 0.5 percent when announcing its decision. Wednesday. The US Federal Reserve raised its policy rate by 0.25 percent, or 25 basis points, in March. According to Reuters.
