Ministry of Labor signs MoU with partner organizations to implement projects to promote health, nutrition and infant and child feeding in factories
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training this morning, May 4, 2022, signed a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) with Hepten Keller International and the German Cooperation Agency on the implementation of pilot pilot projects. Health, nutrition and feeding of infants and children in factories (MUSEFO).
The project focuses on 18 factories with a total of 21,166 workers. By providing training on the importance of promoting health, nutrition and infant and child rearing to employers or their representatives, workers of reproductive age and workers who are pregnant and breastfeeding.
Ms. Ginnett Coates stated that Hepten Keller is currently piloting a project to improve the health and nutrition of women and children in a number of factories through the GIZ-MUSEFO project to jointly promote health, productivity and the Cambodian economy.
She added that the project will provide educational materials, as well as equipments such as refrigerators, tables, chairs, fans, breast pumps, hand towels and hand soap to the existing breastfeeding room in the factory. Each goal.
Mr. Ith Sam Heng also praised Hepten Keller for establishing programs related to hygiene, child nutrition in factories, enterprises, especially women, in line with the policy of the Government of Cambodia, as well as the strategic plan of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training. Which is being implemented in factories and enterprises in Cambodia.
The Minister considered this project as an important contribution to further improve the health care of women and children, while the Ministry of Labor is developing its services and issuing new regulations. More effective.
