This morning, the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia held a press conference on the progress of tax collection on existing duty-free vehicles in the country under various license plates.
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of May 4, 2022, the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia held a press conference on the progress of tax collection work on existing duty-free vehicles in the country under various license plates under the chairmanship of Mr. Kun Nhim, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Director General of the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia.
Please be informed that from September to December 31, 2021, the Royal Government of Cambodia, through the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia, has allowed duty-free vehicles, left-hand drive and right-hand drive vehicles (modified and paid for tax) to enter the tax With 10% tax preference. During the grace period, more than 5,000 vehicles came in to pay taxes, earning nearly $ 50 million in taxes.
The Minister stated that for left-hand drive vehicles, owners can still come to pay taxes until June 30, 2022, but do not receive the same 10% tax preference as before. For right-hand drive cars, the owner can come and make a deposit equal to 10% tax and take his car to adjust the steering wheel from right to left. The deadline for the end of the campaign to collect taxes and duties on existing vehicles in the country and take refuge under various license plates is June 30, 2022.
