(Phnom Penh): Lt. Gen. Ey Sok Khi, Deputy Commissioner General of the National Police, on the occasion of closing the 36th Private Security Agency Training Course on May 3, 2022, issued six guidelines to private security agencies. Receive training to enhance the ability to participate in maintaining security, order and social security.
Lt. Gen. Ey Sok Khi stated that at present, in order for private agencies to be fully capable, the National Police General Commission has been taking care to ensure that all private security agencies have the capacity to know the professional ethics in order to promote To this sector to make continuous progress. In addition, all private security agencies must:
* First, have the attitude to participate in the work by taking what is right after receiving professional training from trainers who have experience as judicial police officers and national police leaders.
* Second: Respect the qualifications as a private security agent, must have discipline, ethics, use private security uniforms and adequate equipment.
* Third: Private security agencies not only work for companies or establishments, but also play an important role in maintaining security, safety, public order, especially the protection of property and lives of citizens.
* Fourth: To establish cooperation with the authorities and local authorities: good citizens and good people, an important support force to the competent authorities, good cooperation, timely response. When they see or suspect any illegal activity, whether in their standing position or where, they must immediately report to the competent authority or to the department directly through the telephone number to jointly prevent and suppress the crime. Offense on time.
* 5th: Jointly implement the policy of the Royal Government, the policy of safe villages, communes and sangkats
* Sixth: Private security agencies, especially targets of casinos, condominiums, apartments, hotels, guesthouses and special economic zones, must have fire prevention and fighting skills training and surveillance of suspects who intend to commit crimes at their targets. In particular, care must be taken to cooperate with the competent authorities on a regular basis.
According to the report of Lt. Gen. Lim Sokharasmey, Director of the Private Security Management Department, up to now, 36 private security agency training courses have been conducted by the Deputy Chief of National Police of the Department of Private Security Management and the Phnom Penh Municipal Police. A total of 121 participants (6 females) and a total of 6,408 participants.
