After continuous rain and fear of flooding, Kampong Speu Provincial Department of Water Resources decided to open water gates in some dams and reservoirs to avoid flooding
(Kampong Speu): Director of Kampong Speu Provincial Department of Water Resources and Meteorology, Mr. Nhanh Cheab Hong, said that due to continuous rain in the province, some reservoirs were opened on the morning of May 3, 2022 to prevent The dams eventually collapsed, while some dams were also at alarming levels.
Mr. Nhanh Cheab Hung confirmed that many sluice gates were opened in this province, including the northern part of Stung Kraing Ponlei in Kampong Speu province, 5 sluice gates were opened and 5 Anlong Chrey sluice gates (Kampong Chhnang province opened 3 sluice gates) Kampong Speu opens 2 doors). In the central part of the Chanthnal Dam in Kraing Chek commune, Udong district, heavy rains also forced the opening of five sluice gates.
Meanwhile, the condition of Stung Prek Tnaot, with continuous rain in the upper part, also caused the flood in this river to increase, which forced the experts to decide to open a water gate with a height of 0.5 meters.
The director of the Department of Water Resources added that while many doors were open, four small hydropower plants would also be opened as the Mai Samoeun Reservoir was opened to avoid the risk of flooding and eventual dam collapse. On the other hand, in the southern part of the province, for Kong Pisey and Boseth districts, some sluice gates were opened while two automatic sluice gates were leaking and officials are working on the case.
