Mr. Hun Manet: The press is the fourth power that plays a very important role in developing the country and strengthening democracy (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Dr. Hun Manet, the candidate for the Prime Minister for the future, said that the press is the fourth power In Cambodia, which plays a very important role in contributing to the development and strengthening of democracy.
Mr. HUN Manet made the remarks on the occasion of his visit to Cambodia on behalf of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, to celebrate the 29th World Press Freedom Day 2022 under the theme "Digital Press under Pressure" at the Hotel. Sokha Phnom Penh and Residence on May 3, 2022.
Mr. HUN Manet stated that journalists have a very important role to play in monitoring the actual activities of all stakeholders, including the authorities, the people and the journalists themselves. He said that if our country wants to grow and be a democracy based on the rule of law, we must join together, there is no impunity for anyone.
He added that the media profession has played an important role in the development of the country and the strengthening of democracy, and the government has already recognized and strived to open up space for journalists. Journalists are the fourth power to play the following roles:
First, to participate in the development of the nation and democracy on the basis of law.
Third, journalists are educators through research, gathering information from all angles for the public to know, for the Royal Government to know.
Fourth: Journalists monitor and monitor any event and balance transparency. Journalists are the guides or binoculars when someone does something wrong. The fourth power of the press is not to be tied down anywhere. But it is a revelation to the public that someone is doing wrong or bad in society.
He said that information in battle is like a weapon, so weapons in battle can kill people in that battle. False information in society can also be harmful to the society, but if the information is true from all angles, time is like the best medicine for our society.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen's eldest son also stated that the fourth power, journalists must use "power not to be afraid, but power to be respected to be sustainable." If you want to be respected, you have to value yourself, you have to maintain a clear professional ethics. Be the one to retrieve and disseminate information professionally so that leaders, the public and the people know to take action to solve problems, not create problems.
However, he stressed that the value of the press can not be protected by anyone but the journalists themselves. Being in the law is one thing, but acting conscientiously and professionally is important.
