Minister of Information: Some reports criticizing Cambodia for restricting freedom of the press are written by donors (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Mr. Khieu Kanharith, Minister of Information, criticized the reports of some associations and institutions that support journalists Write and publish that the Royal Government of Cambodia has restricted the freedom of the press.
The Minister considered that the report was written by the donors only and was not accurate, while the Ministry of Information received more in-depth information on cases encountered by journalists.
He continued: "In a report that said that the license is closed, we did not close, just hung up, because the kidnapping story continues ... So the report should understand this a little deeper, so please report this "Let go a little deeper because the Ministry of Information goes deeper on that issue because the Ministry of Information knows journalists better than the report writers."
Around this point, Mr. Khieu Kanharith also explained that the reason why the Ministry of Information decided to cancel or suspend the information license, unless any institution to demand money from the people until there is a complaint to the Ministry.
In this case, the Minister stated that in the past, seven journalists had come to extort money from a company, and the Ministry had repeatedly instructed them before revoking or suspending the licenses of those organizations. In return for their misconduct.
The Minister of Information of Cambodia stated that the freedom of the press and expression in Cambodia has improved compared to other countries in the region, such as Thailand, which has shut down more than 100,000 news websites, but has not announced any restrictions on freedom. In addition, Cambodian journalists are proud that the Royal Government has given priority to 19 vaccines against Kovid, equivalent to doctors, the armed forces, civil servants among ASEAN countries and the world.
