Samdech Techo's announcement was made on the occasion of meeting and giving incentives to 1,753 A-level students in the academic year 2020-2021.
Samdech Techo stated that the priority of students to get 19 vaccines is to increase community immunity and ensure the education of students.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen praised the Ministry of Education as well as teachers across the country for their efforts to overcome the difficulties caused by Kovid 19.
Samdech Techo also reminded of the Royal Government's decision to close schools in the past during the outbreak of Kovid 19 because there was no vaccine at that time, which requires the Royal Government to make a decision to Protect the lives of people as well as teachers and students from Kovid 19.
The head of the Royal Government stated that without timely measures, Cambodia could have suffered a tragedy due to the deaths of its people. As a result of measures and vaccinations for people across the country, Cambodia has been able to reopen schools and reopen the country.
During the invitation, Samdech Techo Hun Sen spoke for more than two and a half hours, the following are the main contents:
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen congratulated the A-level students and their parents who became outstanding students.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen also congratulated and praised all the students who passed the exam in 2021.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen also expressed his condolences to the students who failed the exam. Samdech Techo hopes that they will continue their studies in 2022 to retake the exam or continue to acquire professional skills in various technical training schools.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen recommends research on the reasons why some A-level students have not yet entered college.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen praised the Ministry of Education as well as teachers across the country for their efforts to overcome the difficulties caused by Kovid 19.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the Royal Government decided to close schools during the 19 epidemic of Kovid to ensure the lives of students and teachers.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen has declared students across the country as a priority group to receive vaccinations in addition to civil servants and the armed forces.
* The Minister of Education informed Samdech Techo Hun Sen that A-level students have not yet entered college, they are waiting for the medical school entrance exam.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen praised the parents who took good care of their children during the Kovid 19 outbreak and helped them continue their education. Samdech Techo considers this a matter of pride for the Cambodian nation.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that starting from the introduction of priority policies in the field of education, attention has been paid to education by authorities at all levels.
