Please be informed that vaccination against Kovid 19 is an important option in the strategy to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 and protect the lives of people from Kovid 19 attacks. Based on this strategy, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Commander-in-Chief of the Battle of Kovid 19, promoted vaccination and vaccination as quickly as possible.
Cambodia received its first vaccine on February 7, 2021 and started the first vaccination on February 10, 2021. At present, Cambodia is vaccinating the basic dose of children from 3 to 5 years of age and is also vaccinating people from 5 years of age.
Under the strict order of Samdech Techo with the prompt action of doctors and relevant authorities at all levels, so far Cambodia has achieved vaccination of people from the age of 3 years more than 93% of the population. Citizens across the country. As of May 2, Cambodia has injected nearly 15 million people in the first dose, more than 14 million in the second dose, more than 8 million in the third dose and more than 1 million in the fourth dose.
Achieving a large number of vaccination plans at this high speed is also due to Cambodia's availability of vaccines at a high speed. So far, Cambodia has received a total of nearly 50 million doses of the vaccine, with nearly 9 million remaining in stock.
Through the implementation of this rapid vaccination plan, the Cambodian people have been able to overcome the 19 19 outbreak of Kovid and prevent the high mortality rate of 19 Kovid, and have reached the launch of social activities. Complete re-entry.
As a result of overcoming Kovid 19, the Royal Government also allowed people to gather and have fun during the New Year. The Royal Government has also decided to waive the obligation to wear masks in public places, except in closed or air-conditioned areas.
Cambodia has also recently been found by Japanese newspapers to be the second largest country in the world to recover economically after the Kovid 19 crisis.
