(Phnom Penh): The Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen has confirmed to Senior General Ming Oung Lang, Chairman of the State Administrative Council of the Republic of the Union of Myanmar, that all parties want to see Myanmar make immediate progress on three urgent priorities. 5 points unanimously agreed.
The three immediate priorities are: 1: stopping the violence, 2: providing humanitarian assistance to all people in need without obstruction, and 3: building trust and confidence to promote a constructive dialogue. Currently.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen's statement was made during a video conference with Senior General Ming Oung Lang, Chairman of the State Administrative Council of the Republic of the Union of Myanmar on May 2, 2022 to exchange views on the path. Towards accelerating the implementation of the five-point unanimous agreement.
