EU calls for halt to Russian oil imports in new sanctions package
The European Union (EU) will propose a phase-out ban on oil imports from Russia as part of new sanctions against Russia over its invasion of Ukraine, sources said on Sunday. According to the AFP news agency.
The European Commission, which has imposed sanctions on the bloc, is currently preparing new sanctions proposals that could be submitted to all 27 member states by Wednesday morning, the AFP news agency reported, citing some diplomats.
Many diplomats have said a ban on oil imports from Russia was possible after Germany changed its position, saying the move would hurt its economy.
The European Commission will propose a gradual ban on oil imports within six to eight months to give countries time to diversify their oil supplies, the source told AFP.
This ban requires unanimous support and cannot be blocked. Hungary is expected to face strong opposition as it relies on Russian oil and has close ties to the Kremlin.
Other countries are concerned that a ban on oil will increase prices at gas stations as consumer prices are rising sharply due to the war.
