Bak Kheng Water Treatment Plant invests more than 300 million USD to build 60% for the first phase and 37% for the second phase
(Phnom Penh): As of the first quarter of 2022, the project to build a Bak Kheng water treatment plant with a capacity of 390,000 cubic meters per day with an investment of more than 300 million USD, completed 60% for the first phase and Achieved 37% for the second step. This is according to the confirmation of Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority.
The two-phase Bak Kheng water supply investment project will use an investment budget of more than 300 million US dollars and the production capacity will reach 390 thousand cubic meters / day by the end of 2023, which is a record high capacity.
By the first quarter of 2022, the construction of the first phase of Bak Kheng water treatment plant with a capacity of 195,000 cubic meters per day achieved about 60% of the first phase of the project, which divided the site into three major parts. Important:
* Section 3: Water pipe installation site:
Meanwhile, the construction of the second phase of the Bak Kheng water treatment plant, which has a capacity of 195,000 cubic meters per day, is also underway at the same time, with the construction work of this plant has now reached about 37%.
The management of the Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority has paid close attention to the water supply by working hard to accelerate the construction of the Bak Kheng water treatment plant in accordance with the planned plan as well as the study of the master plan until 2030. To meet the demand for clean water in Phnom Penh and Takhmao. Xi Jinping: "Labor is an honor"
