(Kandal): Mr. Kong Sophoan, Governor of Kandal Province, reminded all police officers of the administrative post to go to every house of the people by solving all the problems they are facing in time with a smile. Responsibility and getting back the smiles of the people in their locality.
This additional reminder by the Provincial Governor was made at the inauguration ceremony of the Kampong Svay Commune Administrative Police Station, which is 11 meters by 9 meters in Kampong Svay Village, Kampong Svay Commune, Kien Svay District, Kandal Province on May 2. This 2022.
The provincial governor reminded: "In order to keep the villages and communes safe, all administrative police officers must visit the people in all the backyards and change their attitude in providing public services to the people. "It's time to get their hearts and smiles on."
The provincial governor also requested all police officers, administrative posts and authorities at all levels to implement the policy of safe villages, communes and sangkats in all localities to prevent theft, electric shock, robbery and drug offenses. Law, illegal gambling, human trafficking, gang activity and crime suppression at their local level.
In that, Mr. Kong Sophorn called on people to report all crimes, especially drug offenses, trafficking and other crimes to the authorities so that they can prevent and suppress in time. Also.
